WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:09.099
I had to think that whoever was behind was
me was just one of the employees, but then,

00:00:09.099 --> 00:00:12.920
seemingly just to disprove that theory, the
guy moves closer to me and starts breathing

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:13.920
down my neck.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:20.670
I was getting very uncomfortable, but then
just as I was about to say something...

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:26.660
Hello, and welcome to Al Dente Creepypasta,
horror stories cooked to perfection with a

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:28.520
splash of red sauce.

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:33.079
My name is CZ and I will be your server this
episode.

00:00:33.079 --> 00:00:35.270
Today's special comes in many courses.

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:38.800
As we celebrate the 10th episode of this series,
we're going to be looking back at some of

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:41.470
of the best stories from Season 1.

00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:45.940
This is going to be a long compilation of
original scary stories, so I'd recommend throwing

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:50.540
this on to listen to in the background, during
school or work, while you're in the car, while

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:51.900
you're surfing the web...

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:57.590
Or if you're really brave, put this video
on before bed and see if you can fall asleep...

00:00:57.590 --> 00:01:01.489
Now, I don't usually say this until the end
and I do kind of hate when YouTubers bring

00:01:01.489 --> 00:01:05.530
this up before you've watched the actual video...
but since this is such a long one I think

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:09.220
now is a good time to remind you to make sure
you've subscribed to the channel and turned

00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:14.000
deathbell notifications on so you don't miss
out on new horrors every week.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.060
Oh, and one more thing.

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:20.110
I've hidden a surprise somewhere in this video,
so those of you who listen through the entire

00:01:20.110 --> 00:01:21.929
thing will get to see it.

00:01:21.929 --> 00:01:29.680
So with all of the formalities now out of
the way, let's dig right in.

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:33.249
Number 1 - This Strange Man Is In All Of My
Dreams

00:01:33.249 --> 00:01:38.689
I'm sitting in an airport right now.

00:01:38.689 --> 00:01:42.880
My flight is delayed so I'm going to do my
best to write this story before it's time

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:44.090
to board the flight.

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:50.950
Have you ever dreamed of a character, who
seems to only exist in your dreams?

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:54.929
Most of the characters in my dreams are people
that I know I'm real life.

00:01:54.929 --> 00:02:00.029
Occasionally I'll dream of a character from
a TV show, or celebrity crush, but the point

00:02:00.029 --> 00:02:02.999
is they are all people that I can picture
in my head.

00:02:02.999 --> 00:02:09.530
Sure, there may be one that I made up from
time to time, but if that does happen they

00:02:09.530 --> 00:02:13.040
are usually only going to appear in one dream.

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:14.200
Except for this one guy.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:19.370
For the last few years this guy has been in
almost every one of my dreams; at least the

00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:21.310
ones that I can remember.

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:24.760
As far as I know he's never had a name.

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:29.560
He's bald, probably in his 60's or something
though I suck at guessing people's ages.

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:34.040
He has a thin mustache and wrinkles his eyes.

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:35.659
Yellow teeth.

00:02:35.659 --> 00:02:38.090
Not real straight.

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:42.390
I wouldn't call him overweight but he's definitely
not in shape.

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:46.840
The strange thing is: this is the first time
I've been able to clearly remember what he

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:48.740
looks like outside of my dream.

00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:51.599
But I'll get back to that in a minute.

00:02:51.599 --> 00:02:56.189
So usually this man just shows up in random
situations in my dream.

00:02:56.189 --> 00:03:00.870
Like he might be delivering me this package,
or if I'm having a test dream he'll be the

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:01.870
teacher.

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:06.090
If I'm being chased in my dream, he is usually
the malevolent pursuer.

00:03:06.090 --> 00:03:11.800
If it's a getting walked-in-on dream, he tends
to be the one to catch me.

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:14.640
So he always plays that kind of role.

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:18.280
I don't think I've ever held a conversation
with him in any of these.

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:22.069
I can’t really remember him talking at all
to be honest.

00:03:22.069 --> 00:03:23.790
So that brings me to today.

00:03:23.790 --> 00:03:29.769
I am flying out to Denver for work and the
flight gets delayed because of inclement weather.

00:03:29.769 --> 00:03:35.200
It’s early in the morning and I’m tired,
so I decided to nod off for a little bit in

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:36.200
the airport.

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:40.370
Now I can never remember the beginning of
my dreams but, the first thing I remember

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:43.650
was watching my son play Jak and Daxter.

00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:48.390
Quick backstory on that, my kid was really
into The Last of Us, so recently I dug out

00:03:48.390 --> 00:03:52.489
my old PS2 and introduced him to the Jak and
Daxter series because they're made by the

00:03:52.489 --> 00:03:55.800
same studio and he really took a liking to
it.

00:03:55.800 --> 00:04:00.299
I don’t know if other people have this happen
in their dreams, but I have a lot of dreams

00:04:00.299 --> 00:04:04.110
where I’ll be watching a movie or playing
a game, and I kind of gradually become one

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:05.129
of the characters.

00:04:05.129 --> 00:04:08.490
I’m assuming I’m not the only one who
gets that.

00:04:08.490 --> 00:04:13.110
So I’m in this game and I’m exploring
this area called Misty Island.

00:04:13.110 --> 00:04:16.769
I think I was supposed to be finding this
power cell or something, I don’t remember

00:04:16.769 --> 00:04:18.820
the exact details of the objective.

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:21.950
But me and my son were both inside of this
game.

00:04:21.950 --> 00:04:26.440
He kept running ahead to explore, and I would
try to keep close to him, because as the name

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:31.350
of the island suggests, it was very hazy and
I was afraid he was going to be lost or something

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:32.920
was going to happen to him.

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:37.760
The problem is, I kept slipping on the gravel
underneath my feet, and it was becoming a

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:40.280
challenge to even stay upright.

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:44.850
He was just kind of running around carelessly
and I lost him for a minute as he ran around

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:45.850
this cliff.

00:04:45.850 --> 00:04:47.060
I sprinted to catch up with him.

00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:50.610
When I came around the cliff, there was nothing
there.

00:04:50.610 --> 00:04:56.510
I was not only worried about my son getting
lost, but also the threat of Lurkers, which

00:04:56.510 --> 00:05:00.380
if you aren’t familiar with the game, are
these creepy purple reptilian creatures with

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:02.500
yellow eyes.

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:06.360
Almost on cue, one of these creatures crawled
out of the cliffside and crossed right in

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:08.590
front of me, stopping me in my tracks.

00:05:08.590 --> 00:05:13.140
It continued on towards the shore and disappeared
in the fog.

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:17.430
Then I noticed someone standing far in the
distance shrouded in fog.

00:05:17.430 --> 00:05:19.920
I called out my son’s name, but he didn’t
respond.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:23.030
He was just standing still staring out at
the water.

00:05:23.030 --> 00:05:26.470
I began to run up towards him, when a Lurker
bounded out from the trees, jumped, and struck

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:29.840
him in the head before scampering off!

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:33.090
My heart sank in my chest and I sprinted with
everything I had.

00:05:33.090 --> 00:05:36.650
When I reached him I discovered, it was not
my son, but rather…

00:05:36.650 --> 00:05:38.560
No… it couldn’t be…

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:48.840
What I saw lying there on the sand, was the
man from my dreams, only in video game polygon

00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:49.840
form.

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:55.120
Somehow, his appearance was even creepier
in compressed textures and PS2 graphics, yet

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:58.620
the injury to his head was terrifyingly realistic.

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:03.370
His body then compressed into green eco in
the typical fashion of the game’s death

00:06:03.370 --> 00:06:06.530
animation, and he was gone.

00:06:06.530 --> 00:06:09.880
I progressed to the area that is essentially
the end of the level and where I saw my son

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:12.530
standing up on a platform, waiting for me.

00:06:12.530 --> 00:06:19.080
As I got closer, I noticed there was someone
else standing there as well, and sure enough,

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:20.810
it was the man, again…

00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:26.930
He had his hand on my son’s shoulder and
they were both just staring at me.

00:06:26.930 --> 00:06:30.520
Not knowing what to do, I froze in my tracks.

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:31.840
Before I could come to a decision…

00:06:31.840 --> 00:06:36.780
I was jolted out of the game, and I was back
in my son’s room, staring at a blank screen.

00:06:36.780 --> 00:06:39.390
I looked over to the chair my son had been
sitting in.

00:06:39.390 --> 00:06:45.200
What I saw was the chord from his controller
stretched across the chair, like he had gotten

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:48.730
up and was standing as far back as the cable
length would allow him.

00:06:48.730 --> 00:06:57.290
I followed the stretch of cable with my eyes
to meet my son’s gaze… but was instead

00:06:57.290 --> 00:06:58.290
met with…

00:06:58.290 --> 00:07:00.100
[controller sound effect]

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:02.900
An adult pair of hands dropped the plastic
controller to the floor.

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:03.900
It was him.

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:07.410
He was just grinning at me with the most insane
stare.

00:07:07.410 --> 00:07:10.930
I was startled, nearly falling back out of
my chair.

00:07:10.930 --> 00:07:14.150
My first instinct was to swing my feet around
and stumble out of the room.

00:07:14.150 --> 00:07:15.160
I ran down the hall.

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:19.530
The house seemed to be empty, but strangely,
all of the doors to every room were open.

00:07:19.530 --> 00:07:21.490
I looked over my shoulder as I turned the
corner.

00:07:21.490 --> 00:07:24.930
He had grown to about 9 feet tall and his
eyes were deadlocked on me as he ducked under

00:07:24.930 --> 00:07:29.860
the doorframe exiting my son’s room and
began to make his way in my direction.

00:07:29.860 --> 00:07:30.940
I went for the front door.

00:07:30.940 --> 00:07:36.090
In typical nightmare fashion, it was locked,
but for whatever reason I didn’t think to

00:07:36.090 --> 00:07:37.720
just reach down and unlock it.

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:41.870
I fiddled with the doorknob anxiously as I
looked over my shoulder and saw the man walking

00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:45.120
around the corner and coming for me with that
creepy grin on his face.

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:46.120
[doorknob sound effect]

00:07:46.120 --> 00:07:47.330
The doorknob fell to the ground.

00:07:47.330 --> 00:07:49.460
The thing had broken off or something.

00:07:49.460 --> 00:07:53.140
As a last ditch effort I reared back and just
kicked the door in.

00:07:53.140 --> 00:07:57.090
What happened next, is sort of difficult to
put into words.

00:07:57.090 --> 00:08:03.490
I was in the car, just driving as fast as
I could, within reason.

00:08:03.490 --> 00:08:07.720
It was a lot like the phenomenon I explained
earlier, where at first I was watching the

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:10.490
video game and then we were gradually in it.

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:16.460
In this case, I started off alone in the car,
but at some point, I realized I was in the

00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:20.060
car with that guy.

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:24.020
I know it doesn't make sense, but in the context
of the dream I didn’t question it.

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:26.660
He wasn’t making any moves or anything.

00:08:26.660 --> 00:08:30.270
Literally, he was just sitting there with
his stupid grin.

00:08:30.270 --> 00:08:38.460
But as time went on, I was just getting more
nervous that he was about to do something.

00:08:38.460 --> 00:08:40.060
I kept looking over at him.

00:08:40.060 --> 00:08:41.060
Looking back at the road.

00:08:41.060 --> 00:08:42.250
Then back at him.

00:08:42.250 --> 00:08:45.780
I was trying to keep my eye on him and make
sure he wasn’t going anywhere.

00:08:45.780 --> 00:08:46.780
Him.

00:08:46.780 --> 00:08:47.780
The road.

00:08:47.780 --> 00:08:48.780
Him.

00:08:48.780 --> 00:08:49.780
The road.

00:08:49.780 --> 00:08:52.550
The next time I looked back at him, he was
breathing more and more heavily.

00:08:52.550 --> 00:08:53.700
I was getting nervous.

00:08:53.700 --> 00:08:55.200
My palms were sweating.

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:57.910
I looked back at the road to find I had run
out of road!

00:08:57.910 --> 00:09:00.140
I was about to drive over the edge into the
water!

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:05.170
I slammed the brakes, but it was too late,
I broke through the barrier and propelled

00:09:05.170 --> 00:09:06.170
off the edge!

00:09:06.170 --> 00:09:08.470
A shiver went up my spine as I was startled
awake.

00:09:08.470 --> 00:09:13.670
To my relief, it was all just a crazy dream.

00:09:13.670 --> 00:09:17.530
Just as I woke up, a woman in a purple dress
swiftly crossed in front of me.

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:19.750
My gaze followed her to the window.

00:09:19.750 --> 00:09:21.460
It was almost white with fog.

00:09:21.460 --> 00:09:26.120
It seemed that there would still be a significant
delay until we could take off.

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:27.120
[bottle sound effect]

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:28.380
Just then I dropped my bottle of water.

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:32.170
I had purchased before heading to my gate
and forgotten that I’d fallen asleep with

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:33.190
it in my hand.

00:09:33.190 --> 00:09:38.340
I reached down to grab and as I came back
up, I saw something that frightened and disturbed

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:39.630
me…

00:09:39.630 --> 00:09:42.120
The man from my dreams.

00:09:42.120 --> 00:09:45.900
He was sitting in the seat across from me.

00:09:45.900 --> 00:09:51.860
Just grinning at me.

00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:55.380
Number 2 - Costume Shop

00:09:55.380 --> 00:10:01.050
I know Halloween is supposed to be a spooky
holiday, but my first Halloween experience

00:10:01.050 --> 00:10:05.170
left me with scars and nightmares for years
to come.

00:10:05.170 --> 00:10:10.090
Having moved to the USA when I was 17, I had
never actually celebrated Halloween before

00:10:10.090 --> 00:10:13.660
because it wasn't even a known holiday in
my home country.

00:10:13.660 --> 00:10:17.490
A few years later, when I got my first job
as a computer consultant,

00:10:17.490 --> 00:10:20.700
I wanted to do whatever I could to get ahead
and move up in the company.

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:23.840
When my boss mentioned that there would be
a company Halloween party.

00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:28.640
I saw this as an opportunity to impress by
finding the best costume in the office.

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:33.020
I wanted to avoid the cheap quality of pop
up Halloween stores, so I found a nice costume

00:10:33.020 --> 00:10:35.920
rental shop with some supposedly higher quality
wares.

00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:38.450
I headed over there after staying late at
work that night.

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:43.060
It was pretty far away in the middle of nowhere,
but I was hoping it would be worth the extra

00:10:43.060 --> 00:10:44.060
miles.

00:10:44.060 --> 00:10:46.320
I got in there about an hour before close.

00:10:46.320 --> 00:10:49.230
But to my surprise, the place was pretty much
empty.

00:10:49.230 --> 00:10:53.400
There was only one customer in there, despite
the fact that we were already pretty late

00:10:53.400 --> 00:10:54.470
into October.

00:10:54.470 --> 00:10:59.210
I wasn't exactly sure what I wanted to go
as, so the owner of the store helped me pick

00:10:59.210 --> 00:11:01.470
out several costumes that I was interested
in,

00:11:01.470 --> 00:11:04.340
and let me into the changing room to see how
they all looked on me.

00:11:04.340 --> 00:11:07.490
I started to get undressed when I heard the
door chime,

00:11:07.490 --> 00:11:10.279
signaling that someone was entering or leaving.

00:11:10.279 --> 00:11:14.260
This was a fairly large shop, but it was small
enough that I could hear what was going on

00:11:14.260 --> 00:11:16.630
in the front from where I was.

00:11:16.630 --> 00:11:18.945
Which is why my heart sank, when I heard this:
"Put your hands up.

00:11:18.945 --> 00:11:23.160
This is a robbery."

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:26.680
I then hear a horrified scream, which I think
was coming from the other customer that was

00:11:26.680 --> 00:11:27.750
in the store with me.

00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:28.750
"You.

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:29.750
Don't move.

00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:31.270
Get up against the wall.

00:11:31.270 --> 00:11:33.910
I said back to the wall.

00:11:33.910 --> 00:11:34.910
Now!"

00:11:34.910 --> 00:11:36.080
That was a different voice.

00:11:36.080 --> 00:11:40.070
As far as I could tell, there were at least
two men who were operating this.

00:11:40.070 --> 00:11:46.860
The entire store was suddenly silent.

00:11:46.860 --> 00:11:49.490
That's when I heard what seemed like the loudest
gunshot I've ever heard.

00:11:49.490 --> 00:11:53.480
I literally had to cover my own mouth to prevent
myself from gasping or screaming,

00:11:53.480 --> 00:11:55.480
and tried to stay as quiet as possible.

00:11:55.480 --> 00:11:58.870
"Open up the register and step away."

00:11:58.870 --> 00:12:01.370
I heard the familiar sound of a cash register
opening,

00:12:01.370 --> 00:12:05.460
and it was quiet for a few moments as I could
only hear people shuffling around,

00:12:05.460 --> 00:12:09.050
which I assume was the guy hopping over the
counter and unloading the register into a

00:12:09.050 --> 00:12:10.420
bag or something.

00:12:10.420 --> 00:12:15.490
After that, there was a quieter exchange between
the first robber and the owner of the store.

00:12:15.490 --> 00:12:19.430
I couldn't hear it very clearly, but from
what I could gather, the robber had asked

00:12:19.430 --> 00:12:21.570
to be taken to the vault or something like
that.

00:12:21.570 --> 00:12:25.460
It seemed like the accomplice had stayed back
with the other customer, and the lights in

00:12:25.460 --> 00:12:27.730
the entire store had been turned off.

00:12:27.730 --> 00:12:30.130
Possibly to make it look like they were closed
from the outside.

00:12:30.130 --> 00:12:33.370
I thought about calling the police but I was
afraid that they would hear me,

00:12:33.370 --> 00:12:37.220
given how quiet it was and how well sound
seemed to travel in the store.

00:12:37.220 --> 00:12:41.010
My hands were shaking as I tried texting my
roommate to ask him to send help.

00:12:41.010 --> 00:12:53.300
But I was cut short when I heard two pairs
of footsteps headed in my direction.

00:12:53.300 --> 00:12:56.960
This sent me into a panic, since I had left
a couple of items on the floor.

00:12:56.960 --> 00:13:01.529
The door to the dressing room was a thin swinging
door with diagonal upward facing slots

00:13:01.529 --> 00:13:05.240
so that I could see out to the ceiling, but
someone on the outside would only be able

00:13:05.240 --> 00:13:07.171
to see part of the floor if they tried to
peak in.

00:13:07.171 --> 00:13:11.740
As quickly and quietly as possible,
I gathered up everything from the floor and

00:13:11.740 --> 00:13:12.900
moved it onto the bench.

00:13:12.900 --> 00:13:16.230
I picked my feet up onto the bench and tried
to squeeze myself into the corner.

00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:18.040
There is a small slot under the door.

00:13:18.040 --> 00:13:21.560
Not enough to fit through, but enough that
you could see if someone's feet were on the

00:13:21.560 --> 00:13:24.370
ground from the other side.

00:13:24.370 --> 00:13:27.900
I was able to see two pairs of shoes walk
right past my door

00:13:27.900 --> 00:13:30.210
while I tried not to breath.

00:13:30.210 --> 00:13:34.080
They seemed to go into the back somewhere
so I decided to finish my text message and

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:37.560
hope that my roommate would notice and contact
the police for me.

00:13:37.560 --> 00:13:42.770
This was before I knew that some call centers
allow you to send a text message to 911 directly

00:13:42.770 --> 00:13:46.800
which is now recommended for situations that
are too dangerous to talk.

00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:50.930
I was so nervous, as I waited for about 15
minutes while the owner and the robber were

00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:52.010
somewhere in the back.

00:13:52.010 --> 00:13:55.920
At no point during this experience was I ever
comfortable, but there was a point where I

00:13:55.920 --> 00:14:00.860
kind of got used to the situation and my heart
rated seemed to slow down a little bit.

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:02.040
Then...

00:14:02.040 --> 00:14:03.040
out of nowhere...

00:14:03.040 --> 00:14:07.240
This came from the back of the store.

00:14:07.240 --> 00:14:09.810
Because this happened after several minutes
of complete silence,

00:14:09.810 --> 00:14:13.410
I nearly had a heart attack when it happened
and fell off the bench.

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:17.750
I was praying that the other robber didn't
hear that, because I was convinced that the

00:14:17.750 --> 00:14:21.520
store owner was dead and I would be next if
they found out about me.

00:14:21.520 --> 00:14:24.140
The robber then walked back past my changing
room.

00:14:24.140 --> 00:14:25.510
"Do it."

00:14:25.510 --> 00:14:26.510
"No!

00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:27.510
Please!"

00:14:27.510 --> 00:14:32.040
I sat there in shock, thinking that I might
be the lone survivor of this crime with any

00:14:32.040 --> 00:14:33.060
luck.

00:14:33.060 --> 00:14:38.310
But whatever hope I did have was dashed, when
I heard what he said next:

00:14:38.310 --> 00:14:41.089
"Check the rest of the store."

00:14:41.089 --> 00:14:45.620
I didn't dare move a muscle as I heard the
two men methodically taking apart the rest

00:14:45.620 --> 00:14:46.620
of the store.

00:14:46.620 --> 00:14:49.730
I thought back to when the store owner had
let me into the changing room.

00:14:49.730 --> 00:14:52.410
How he had unlocked the door to let me go
in.

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:56.960
I thought maybe... just maybe... that they
would assume that the doors were locked at

00:14:56.960 --> 00:14:58.740
all times and leave it be.

00:14:58.740 --> 00:15:03.149
But again, my head started burning when I
saw a figure standing right outside my door

00:15:03.149 --> 00:15:06.240
through the slots,
trying to peek inside.

00:15:06.240 --> 00:15:09.980
He tried the doorhandle, and started loudly
banging on the door!

00:15:09.980 --> 00:15:12.670
"Anybody in there?

00:15:12.670 --> 00:15:14.470
Open up!"

00:15:14.470 --> 00:15:16.970
He then starts throwing himself against the
door like a madman!

00:15:16.970 --> 00:15:20.190
I can literally see the door breaking off
it's hinges before my eyes.

00:15:20.190 --> 00:15:29.470
It's not going to take much more abuse, when
finally...

00:15:29.470 --> 00:15:33.089
I hear the guy yell out "let's go" and they
both run for the exit.

00:15:33.089 --> 00:15:35.750
The rest of the night was pretty much a blur
to me.

00:15:35.750 --> 00:15:37.430
I remember the police arriving.

00:15:37.430 --> 00:15:39.620
Me being marched back through the store.

00:15:39.620 --> 00:15:41.540
Seeing police and ambulance lights.

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:45.610
Seeing the bloody mess made along the wall,
probably from that first customer.

00:15:45.610 --> 00:15:47.270
I was taken in for questioning.

00:15:47.270 --> 00:15:51.560
I probably wasn't very helpful, considering
that I never saw their faces.

00:15:51.560 --> 00:15:55.680
As far as I know, neither of them were ever
caught.

00:15:55.680 --> 00:16:00.040
It's pretty obvious to me why they decided
to steal from a small costume shop just before

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:03.380
Halloween,
but I still wonder why they felt the need

00:16:03.380 --> 00:16:04.839
to kill.

00:16:04.839 --> 00:16:08.650
Especially someone in my position who didn't
even see their faces.

00:16:08.650 --> 00:16:12.480
I've had many nightmares about the incident,
and have struggled to get the idea out of

00:16:12.480 --> 00:16:13.850
my head ever since.

00:16:13.850 --> 00:16:16.840
I've tried talking to therapists and friends
about the situation,

00:16:16.840 --> 00:16:19.170
and people have come up with their own theories.

00:16:19.170 --> 00:16:23.350
The best, and probably most haunting theory
that I've heard so far,

00:16:23.350 --> 00:16:27.810
Came from a witness who worked at a nearby
restaurant and was getting off his shift around

00:16:27.810 --> 00:16:30.500
the time that I was in the costume store that
night.

00:16:30.500 --> 00:16:35.050
After hearing about what happened in the news,
he theorized that the two criminals didn't

00:16:35.050 --> 00:16:38.560
do it for the money,
but rather did it for the thrill.

00:16:38.560 --> 00:16:42.800
I don't know if there's any truth to this,
but he said he noticed two men in tuxedos

00:16:42.800 --> 00:16:50.279
walk into the shop… ...wearing animal masks.

00:16:50.279 --> 00:16:57.100
Number 3 - Heartbreaker

00:16:57.100 --> 00:17:01.900
The stereotypical version of Valentine’s
Day has always gotten on my nerves.

00:17:01.900 --> 00:17:08.029
For one, the ads never show gay couples and
I tend to get asked out by guys who don’t

00:17:08.029 --> 00:17:11.039
believe I’m actually gay.

00:17:11.039 --> 00:17:13.549
This year wasn’t different by much.

00:17:13.549 --> 00:17:19.230
I had to sit through class, which I spent
texting my girlfriend, Amy, going over our

00:17:19.230 --> 00:17:21.439
plans for the night.

00:17:21.439 --> 00:17:25.169
Our LGBTQ friends were having a dinner party
and we agreed to go.

00:17:25.169 --> 00:17:29.629
As I was getting up to leave after class,
one of the guys walked over to me.

00:17:29.629 --> 00:17:31.809
I don't know who he is.

00:17:31.809 --> 00:17:34.340
He's one of the quiet guys who sits in the
back.

00:17:34.340 --> 00:17:38.519
He handed me a heart-shaped note reading “will
you be mine?”

00:17:38.519 --> 00:17:42.340
I sighed, noticing his friend nervously watching
in the back.

00:17:42.340 --> 00:17:44.570
Obviously, his friend was asking.

00:17:44.570 --> 00:17:47.460
“Sorry, but I have a girlfriend.”

00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:49.789
I tried to be nice about it.

00:17:49.789 --> 00:17:53.710
He went back to his friend and I could feel
a cold glare following me.

00:17:53.710 --> 00:17:58.190
I'm used to guys being rude, so I shrugged
it off.

00:17:58.190 --> 00:18:00.289
I went home and got ready for the night.

00:18:00.289 --> 00:18:05.389
It felt like something was staring at me from
outside and in the shadows.

00:18:05.389 --> 00:18:08.799
The feeling came back on and off throughout
the night.

00:18:08.799 --> 00:18:13.239
The party was amazing, lots of laughs and
booze.

00:18:13.239 --> 00:18:16.630
Everyone was intoxicated, especially Amy.

00:18:16.630 --> 00:18:19.260
As I drove her home, there was a car following
us.

00:18:19.260 --> 00:18:22.309
I could feel my hair standing on end.

00:18:22.309 --> 00:18:26.869
Every time we passed an intersection, I would
look back to see if it would turn.

00:18:26.869 --> 00:18:30.929
It finally turned when we were two blocks
from Amy's.

00:18:30.929 --> 00:18:37.030
I helped her inside and she complained constantly
that it was hot in her apartment, so I opened

00:18:37.030 --> 00:18:39.019
the window a bit.

00:18:39.019 --> 00:18:43.220
Most people would have made out and proceeded
to make love to their partner at this point,

00:18:43.220 --> 00:18:45.580
but I have more dignity than that.

00:18:45.580 --> 00:18:48.019
I gave her a kiss goodnight and left.

00:18:48.019 --> 00:18:51.710
It was strangely quiet on my way home.

00:18:51.710 --> 00:18:57.769
The feeling of being followed was finally
gone, replaced by an uneasy feeling in my

00:18:57.769 --> 00:18:58.769
gut.

00:18:58.769 --> 00:19:00.980
Maybe the alcohol was finally kicking in.

00:19:00.980 --> 00:19:04.260
I got back to my dorm and cracked the window
open.

00:19:04.260 --> 00:19:08.809
The night air felt good on my warm face and
soothed my upset stomach.

00:19:08.809 --> 00:19:12.119
I decided to take a shot of whiskey before
going to bed.

00:19:12.119 --> 00:19:15.080
As I laid there, I thought I could hear the
door rattle.

00:19:15.080 --> 00:19:20.289
It was probably my imagination, the shot I
took couldn't have hit me that hard.

00:19:20.289 --> 00:19:23.649
Then again, that's also probably the alcohol.

00:19:23.649 --> 00:19:29.630
I wasn’t sure, but I thought I could see
the shadow of feet from underneath the door.

00:19:29.630 --> 00:19:35.379
I could have sworn something hit the window,
but it was probably just the wind.

00:19:35.379 --> 00:19:40.230
The morning light hit my eyes and the onset
of a hangover made my head throb.

00:19:40.230 --> 00:19:43.210
The slight smell of blood made me groan.

00:19:43.210 --> 00:19:46.240
It shouldn't be that time, yet.

00:19:46.240 --> 00:19:48.049
I got up just to make sure.

00:19:48.049 --> 00:19:55.820
Instead of the expected, the rug felt wet
under my feet and I discovered a heart on

00:19:55.820 --> 00:19:57.150
the floor.

00:19:57.150 --> 00:20:00.149
There was a knife through it and blood staining
my rug.

00:20:00.149 --> 00:20:05.450
My heart was pounding as the metallic smell
flooded my senses.

00:20:05.450 --> 00:20:08.090
The breath caught in my throat and my stomach
twisted.

00:20:08.090 --> 00:20:11.320
I got up and rushed to the bathroom.

00:20:11.320 --> 00:20:13.190
The shock of it all made me sick, literally.

00:20:13.190 --> 00:20:19.240
I took a moment to drink some water after
painfully emptying the contents of my stomach,

00:20:19.240 --> 00:20:22.429
hoping to ease the sense of dread knotting
it.

00:20:22.429 --> 00:20:25.269
I went back, pausing outside my door.

00:20:25.269 --> 00:20:30.509
It had been a long time since I last prayed
and right now, I was praying that it was nothing.

00:20:30.509 --> 00:20:32.440
Praying that it was a delusion.

00:20:32.440 --> 00:20:35.570
I opened the door and it was still there.

00:20:35.570 --> 00:20:40.080
I couldn’t stop myself from gagging and
that's when I saw the writing.

00:20:40.080 --> 00:20:46.919
The wall had blood smeared on it, reading:
“Now you can be mine...”

00:20:46.919 --> 00:20:50.869
The police came and they couldn't find any
evidence of forced entry.

00:20:50.869 --> 00:20:54.359
No trace of who did it was left behind.

00:20:54.359 --> 00:20:59.340
I found out that the heart belonged to Amy
and it was determined that they entered through

00:20:59.340 --> 00:21:00.570
the window.

00:21:00.570 --> 00:21:06.610
I'm not sure how anyone could climb 3 stories
from the outside of the building, but now

00:21:06.610 --> 00:21:09.559
I never leave the window open at night.

00:21:09.559 --> 00:21:15.159
It’s been two years now and I even moved
to a different city because of rumors that

00:21:15.159 --> 00:21:16.330
I killed Amy.

00:21:16.330 --> 00:21:22.809
A new start was supposed to be a good thing,
until I found a heart-shaped note under my

00:21:22.809 --> 00:21:33.019
door reading: “you are mine...”

00:21:33.019 --> 00:21:38.980
Number 4 - I Found Some Disturbing Pictures
In My Child's Backpack

00:21:38.980 --> 00:21:43.759
My wife and I first decided to send our daughter,
Ella, to preschool when my wife went back

00:21:43.759 --> 00:21:45.580
to school to get her nursing degree.

00:21:45.580 --> 00:21:49.960
Ella was about 4 years old at the time, and
we were primarily concerned that she would

00:21:49.960 --> 00:21:53.279
have a hard time fitting in since all of the
other kids in the class had been together

00:21:53.279 --> 00:21:55.519
for a couple of years already at that point.

00:21:55.519 --> 00:21:57.519
The first couple of weeks went off without
a hitch...

00:21:57.519 --> 00:22:02.970
Or at least we didn't notice any issues until
one afternoon in September when Ella wasn't

00:22:02.970 --> 00:22:06.630
feeling well and went to bed right after we
picked her up from school.

00:22:06.630 --> 00:22:10.379
She had left her backpack dumped right next
to the door, and my wife commented on the

00:22:10.379 --> 00:22:14.490
fact that it was surprisingly heavy considering
how small of a bag it was.

00:22:14.490 --> 00:22:18.289
We were curious about what exactly they had
given her that would make the backpack so

00:22:18.289 --> 00:22:21.690
heavy so we decided to pop it open and take
a look.

00:22:21.690 --> 00:22:26.299
All that we had given her when she started
preschool were the basics: pencils, markers,

00:22:26.299 --> 00:22:31.580
crayons, a pad of paper, extra clothes, perhaps
a couple of other things that I'm forgetting

00:22:31.580 --> 00:22:36.679
right now, but the point is, we were very
surprised to see what we found in the backpack.

00:22:36.679 --> 00:22:41.200
It was filled to the brim with loose papers,
it was a complete mess, almost as if she had

00:22:41.200 --> 00:22:43.950
just stuffed the backpack full of paper one
sheet at a time.

00:22:43.950 --> 00:22:48.490
There must have been hundreds of sheets in
there... if not more.

00:22:48.490 --> 00:22:52.570
The strangest thing is, Ella had never really
been a very messy child.

00:22:52.570 --> 00:22:56.159
She keeps her room clean for the most part,
and she's the kind of girl who never really

00:22:56.159 --> 00:22:57.970
likes to get her hands messy.

00:22:57.970 --> 00:23:02.259
Naturally, my wife and I emptied out the backpack
and tried to sort through the mess.

00:23:02.259 --> 00:23:07.679
What we found were... mostly drawings; the
typical stuff you would expect from a young

00:23:07.679 --> 00:23:12.299
girl with the grass at the bottom and the
sun in the top corner of the page.

00:23:12.299 --> 00:23:16.429
Most of the drawings had three characters,
who I can only assume are supposed to be Ella,

00:23:16.429 --> 00:23:22.190
my wife and I. Most of the drawings were repeats
or some variation of this basic formula: the

00:23:22.190 --> 00:23:26.029
three of us standing in front of a house,
the three of us standing in flowers, at the

00:23:26.029 --> 00:23:27.440
beach, etcetera, etcetera.

00:23:27.440 --> 00:23:32.859
Not all of the pages were drawings, some of
them just contained black crayon scribbles

00:23:32.859 --> 00:23:33.859
all over the place.

00:23:33.859 --> 00:23:36.799
It looked almost as if she was trying to color
the page black.

00:23:36.799 --> 00:23:41.789
I remembered doing that when I was bored in
school as a kid as well, so I wasn't too concerned,

00:23:41.789 --> 00:23:43.929
until I saw that there were more of them.

00:23:43.929 --> 00:23:49.059
Subsequent pages contained less black scribbles
and more white space, and all of the lines

00:23:49.059 --> 00:23:51.690
seemed to be completely random from what I
could tell.

00:23:51.690 --> 00:23:55.230
We said something about getting her a bigger
folder and continued to sift through our daughter's

00:23:55.230 --> 00:23:59.440
drawings for a while, until my wife got a
call and I got hungry and went to go grab

00:23:59.440 --> 00:24:00.580
something from the fridge.

00:24:00.580 --> 00:24:04.129
After that, the issue never really came up
again for the next month or so.

00:24:04.129 --> 00:24:09.859
We got busy with life and... well, if you
have kids, you know how parenting can be.

00:24:09.859 --> 00:24:14.890
Anyways, one afternoon in October I was in
Ella's room getting her ready for bed, when

00:24:14.890 --> 00:24:18.820
she had to use the restroom, so I continued
to sit in there and wait for her when I noticed

00:24:18.820 --> 00:24:20.679
another messy stack of papers.

00:24:20.679 --> 00:24:24.529
We have a little table set up in her room
that she can use for her arts and crafts,

00:24:24.529 --> 00:24:28.470
and once again, there was a huge surplus of
drawings pouring out of her backpack.

00:24:28.470 --> 00:24:32.779
I was starting to wonder if they do anything
else at this pre-school of hers besides freetime

00:24:32.779 --> 00:24:35.739
to color, when I noticed something strange...

00:24:35.739 --> 00:24:41.940
there was a new character added to the family
portrait, and he looked disturbing to say

00:24:41.940 --> 00:24:42.940
the least.

00:24:42.940 --> 00:24:47.460
He was a tall slim bald man wearing long white
robes.

00:24:47.460 --> 00:24:52.690
This figure was completely devoid of any color,
except for the eyes and mouth, which were

00:24:52.690 --> 00:24:54.710
scribbled in a dark red.

00:24:54.710 --> 00:24:58.210
It looked like she had jammed the crayon into
the page as hard as she could to produce the

00:24:58.210 --> 00:25:02.679
eyes and mouth, resulting in a much more intense
pigment in those areas.

00:25:02.679 --> 00:25:06.559
Other then that, this character and the areas
surrounding his outline were the only parts

00:25:06.559 --> 00:25:08.979
of the page that were completely colorless.

00:25:08.979 --> 00:25:14.899
What was even more disturbing was the fact
that this character, and my wife were frowning,

00:25:14.899 --> 00:25:17.909
while Ella and I both had huge smiles on our
faces.

00:25:17.909 --> 00:25:20.279
It just didn't sit well with me.

00:25:20.279 --> 00:25:25.070
I continued to look through her drawings and
found that this fourth person was in EVERY

00:25:25.070 --> 00:25:26.070
DRAWING.

00:25:26.070 --> 00:25:31.269
As I flipped through them I noticed the guy
seemed to staring at... my wife.

00:25:31.269 --> 00:25:34.630
In some of the drawings, he seemed to be standing
behind her.

00:25:34.630 --> 00:25:39.059
I was legitimately creeped out by this, but
told myself that it must be an imaginary friend

00:25:39.059 --> 00:25:40.059
or something...

00:25:40.059 --> 00:25:44.200
I continued to flip through the pages and
ended up coming across more of those black

00:25:44.200 --> 00:25:50.330
scribbles, but these ones were, what I can
only describe as more violent, more intense.

00:25:50.330 --> 00:25:54.340
It was that same thing where it looked like
she had mashed the crayon into the page.

00:25:54.340 --> 00:26:00.470
To this point, I was able to look past what
I had seen, but what I saw next gave me a

00:26:00.470 --> 00:26:02.490
deep pit in my stomach.

00:26:02.490 --> 00:26:06.499
She had drawn pictures of my wife, laying
at the bottom of the ocean.

00:26:06.499 --> 00:26:11.850
Her eyes were scribbled out in black crayon
and she was wearing a huge frown.

00:26:11.850 --> 00:26:17.409
To my own dismay, this wasn't the only drawing
like this, she had drawn the same picture,

00:26:17.409 --> 00:26:21.120
over and over and over and over...

00:26:21.120 --> 00:26:25.269
My jaw hung agape as I tried to comprehend
what I was looking at when I realized that

00:26:25.269 --> 00:26:27.179
my wife was in the bath right now.

00:26:27.179 --> 00:26:29.789
Ella had probably gone into that same bathroom...

00:26:29.789 --> 00:26:33.679
Before I could react, I heard a cold voice
from behind.

00:26:33.679 --> 00:26:36.100
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

00:26:36.100 --> 00:26:39.309
I turned to see Ella standing at the door.

00:26:39.309 --> 00:26:42.809
I tried asking her about the pictures, but
she just refused to talk about it and climbed

00:26:42.809 --> 00:26:43.809
into bed.

00:26:43.809 --> 00:26:50.379
This wasn't just a case of kids will be kids;
she had a most serious tone about her.

00:26:50.379 --> 00:26:54.549
Thankfully, my wife didn't mention that anything
had happened while they were in the bathroom,

00:26:54.549 --> 00:26:58.909
but we were unable to get Ella to respond
to any of our questions about the pictures.

00:26:58.909 --> 00:27:08.519
Now, we're considering seeking professional
help.

00:27:08.519 --> 00:27:11.239
Number 5 - The Scarecrow

00:27:11.239 --> 00:27:15.909
I'll always remember 7th grade Halloween as
one of the last good, innocent years of trick-or-treating

00:27:15.909 --> 00:27:17.230
with my friends,
before the paradigm shift to haunted houses,

00:27:17.230 --> 00:27:18.230
parties, slutty costumes, boys and alcohol.

00:27:18.230 --> 00:27:21.799
I'll also remember it though, for one other
reason, that I haven't been able to erase

00:27:21.799 --> 00:27:31.799
from my mind since that night
I remember that day.

00:27:31.799 --> 00:27:34.070
It was Friday, so almost everyone wore their
costumes to school.

00:27:34.070 --> 00:27:38.849
Jane, Margret and I had decided to go as the
Powerpuff Girls,

00:27:38.849 --> 00:27:43.669
even though the show was long since irrelevant
at the time.

00:27:43.669 --> 00:27:46.970
Jane was Bubbles, Margret went as Buttercup,
and I,

00:27:46.970 --> 00:27:48.999
being the only one without the correct hair
color,

00:27:48.999 --> 00:27:51.140
wore a red wig to become Blossom.

00:27:51.140 --> 00:27:53.539
During homeroom, everyone was showing off
their costumes.

00:27:53.539 --> 00:27:58.630
One of our guy friends, Chris, was the only
one who didn't wear his costume to school.

00:27:58.630 --> 00:28:03.269
Chris was one of the more popular guys that
we knew, so I found it kind of strange that

00:28:03.269 --> 00:28:04.269
he hadn't dressed up.

00:28:04.269 --> 00:28:08.479
When Margret asked him why he didn't wear
a costume, he just told us that we'd have

00:28:08.479 --> 00:28:11.590
to stop by his place tonight if we wanted
to see his costume.

00:28:11.590 --> 00:28:15.019
We got the idea that whatever he was wearing,
was obviously too graphic to be brought to

00:28:15.019 --> 00:28:17.950
school,
and made plans to swing by and check it out

00:28:17.950 --> 00:28:19.450
some time that evening.

00:28:19.450 --> 00:28:23.299
By the time we made it to Chris's house, it
was starting to get pretty late.

00:28:23.299 --> 00:28:27.999
I figured we had about an hour or so of trick-or-treating
left before we had to call it a night.

00:28:27.999 --> 00:28:31.070
We were a bigger group of girls now, probably
six or seven of us.

00:28:31.070 --> 00:28:32.070
All in costume.

00:28:32.070 --> 00:28:35.799
His house didn't seem to have much in terms
of decoration,

00:28:35.799 --> 00:28:40.440
Just a few of those Halloween store cobwebs
you see on the porch and a scarecrow sitting

00:28:40.440 --> 00:28:42.080
on a bench near the front door.

00:28:42.080 --> 00:28:46.759
Someone rang the bell and Chris's mom showed
up dressed in regular clothes with a witch

00:28:46.759 --> 00:28:47.759
hat.

00:28:47.759 --> 00:28:50.590
Which I'm pretty sure she wore on multiple
years.

00:28:50.590 --> 00:28:53.149
As we picked out candy, Margret asked if Chris
was home,

00:28:53.149 --> 00:28:57.649
but his Mom told us he had gone out to scare
some trick-or-treaters with a couple friends.

00:28:57.649 --> 00:29:02.380
I was the last one in line to take a piece
of candy, so I thanked her and we went on

00:29:02.380 --> 00:29:03.789
our way.

00:29:03.789 --> 00:29:09.249
As we walked back to the sidewalk, I felt
something behind me tug on my wig...

00:29:09.249 --> 00:29:12.539
pulling it off my head a little bit.

00:29:12.539 --> 00:29:15.220
I looked back and screamed when I saw the
scarecrow standing just a couple inches behind

00:29:15.220 --> 00:29:16.220
me.

00:29:16.220 --> 00:29:20.070
A couple of the girls let out screams as well
when they turned around and noticed the scarecrow

00:29:20.070 --> 00:29:23.150
had moved from the bench and snuck up behind
us.

00:29:23.150 --> 00:29:27.269
Margret seemed to be the first one to come
to the realization that it was Chris, who

00:29:27.269 --> 00:29:30.649
had dressed up and waited for us inside the
scarecrow.

00:29:30.649 --> 00:29:33.889
When Jane asked how long he had to wait there,
he didn't say anything,

00:29:33.889 --> 00:29:37.649
and just stared at us which admittedly made
me a little bit uncomfortable.

00:29:37.649 --> 00:29:42.299
But I tried not to show it,
not wanting to give the known prankster any

00:29:42.299 --> 00:29:43.600
satisfaction.

00:29:43.600 --> 00:29:44.600
I guess he didn't want to break character,
because even as we invited him to come trick-or-treat

00:29:44.600 --> 00:29:51.269
at a few more houses, he remained silent for
the rest of the time.

00:29:51.269 --> 00:29:56.190
Jane and I poked fun at him for trying too
hard to be Mr. Creepy-Mysterious,

00:29:56.190 --> 00:30:01.859
trying to get him to crack or laugh or something,
but it didn't work.

00:30:01.859 --> 00:30:06.679
He just followed us from house to house for
another block or so until we all decided to

00:30:06.679 --> 00:30:09.549
go back to my house and hang out for a while.

00:30:09.549 --> 00:30:12.730
He would occasionally tug on my wig, but I
tried not to react, because I knew that was

00:30:12.730 --> 00:30:14.529
exactly what he wanted.

00:30:14.529 --> 00:30:19.549
So we stayed up late, seeing as how tomorrow
was a Saturday and we could sleep in as long

00:30:19.549 --> 00:30:20.549
as we wanted.

00:30:20.549 --> 00:30:24.940
One of the girls went home, but the rest of
us, and Chris, stayed up to watch a scary

00:30:24.940 --> 00:30:28.049
movie, which ended up not being so scary.

00:30:28.049 --> 00:30:33.390
Chris didn't even seem to want to watch the
movie, he just stared at us the entire time.

00:30:33.390 --> 00:30:37.369
I knew he was just trying to freak me out,
so I ignored him and tried to pay attention

00:30:37.369 --> 00:30:38.369
to the movie.

00:30:38.369 --> 00:30:40.590
I was bored and fell asleep about 20 minutes
in.

00:30:40.590 --> 00:30:45.200
When I woke up, it was around 3 in the morning,
and everyone else passed out on the couch.

00:30:45.200 --> 00:30:47.409
Chris, however, was gone.

00:30:47.409 --> 00:30:51.389
I figured that he wouldn't be able to mess
with us anymore and (he) walked home.

00:30:51.389 --> 00:30:57.220
When we got back to school on Monday we confronted
Chris about his little stunt on Halloween.

00:30:57.220 --> 00:31:02.750
He got this confused expression on his face
and told us that his family didn't own a scarecrow.

00:31:02.750 --> 00:31:04.580
Or a scarecrow costume.

00:31:04.580 --> 00:31:08.710
And that he had been out all evening trick-or-treating
with his friends.

00:31:08.710 --> 00:31:13.190
He even showed us a picture of his group,
with him wearing a Jeff the Killer costume.

00:31:13.190 --> 00:31:18.389
He seemed to have no idea what we were talking
about when we brought up the scarecrow.

00:31:18.389 --> 00:31:23.690
A couple of his friends even served as his
alibis, saying that they were with Chris the

00:31:23.690 --> 00:31:25.429
entire night.

00:31:25.429 --> 00:31:31.279
To this day, I don't know if this was an elaborate
prank, or if some stranger actually followed

00:31:31.279 --> 00:31:34.299
us around all night.

00:31:34.299 --> 00:31:40.139
But what really bothers me most to think about,
is the possibility that this guy came into

00:31:40.139 --> 00:31:47.100
my house, and after all of us were asleep,
left without taking anything or saying a word.

00:31:47.100 --> 00:31:52.909
I've never seen that particular scarecrow
costume again, and to this day...

00:31:52.909 --> 00:31:58.509
I've never gotten Chris to admit that he was
behind it.

00:31:58.509 --> 00:32:05.779
Number 6 - My Sleep Paralysis Amplified

00:32:05.779 --> 00:32:08.409
I started my new job a few days ago.

00:32:08.409 --> 00:32:13.450
Well, to be entirely accurate, it’s not
a new job, I just got transferred to another

00:32:13.450 --> 00:32:14.450
branch.

00:32:14.450 --> 00:32:15.450
In a another timezone.

00:32:15.450 --> 00:32:20.989
My doctor says that the stress of having a
new job, new schedule and new life are all

00:32:20.989 --> 00:32:26.179
probably contributing to my severe sleep issues
and hallucinations I’ve been having.

00:32:26.179 --> 00:32:29.299
OK, maybe I’m getting ahead of myself here.

00:32:29.299 --> 00:32:30.600
Let me take a step back.

00:32:30.600 --> 00:32:31.779
My name is Alex.

00:32:31.779 --> 00:32:34.330
I’m 28 years old and single.

00:32:34.330 --> 00:32:39.549
I work for a pretty sizable company that sells
consumer and professional grade amplifiers

00:32:39.549 --> 00:32:40.549
to musicians.

00:32:40.549 --> 00:32:45.080
I’m the guy who makes sure you actually
get the thing you ordered and get it on time.

00:32:45.080 --> 00:32:49.450
It was recently decided that it would be a
good idea for people like me, to be close

00:32:49.450 --> 00:32:52.230
to the people who are selling these products.

00:32:52.230 --> 00:32:54.499
Why they didn’t realize that in the first
place?

00:32:54.499 --> 00:32:55.499
Beyond me.

00:32:55.499 --> 00:32:59.359
But recently I found myself packing up and
moving across the country.

00:32:59.359 --> 00:33:04.499
So I was kind of annoyed about the whole relocation
thing for my first 10 minutes at the new office.

00:33:04.499 --> 00:33:09.019
I was supposed to be meeting some of these
sales people who I would now be working alongside.

00:33:09.019 --> 00:33:10.860
Enter Caitlyn.

00:33:10.860 --> 00:33:12.659
Luminescent light brown eyes.

00:33:12.659 --> 00:33:16.190
Short, but not too short, brunette hair.

00:33:16.190 --> 00:33:17.190
Dimples.

00:33:17.190 --> 00:33:18.190
To.

00:33:18.190 --> 00:33:19.190
Die for.

00:33:19.190 --> 00:33:22.419
I quickly got over any annoyance I had with
having to move and started to think I was

00:33:22.419 --> 00:33:24.509
going to like this new office.

00:33:24.509 --> 00:33:28.869
By the end of the first day, Caitlyn and I
already had at least three inside jokes.

00:33:28.869 --> 00:33:31.840
“See, I told you the copy machine outsmarted
Lenny!”

00:33:31.840 --> 00:33:34.219
I told her as I headed out for the day.

00:33:34.219 --> 00:33:36.259
Don’t worry, you’re not supposed to get
it.

00:33:36.259 --> 00:33:38.369
It’s one of our inside jokes.

00:33:38.369 --> 00:33:40.890
She laughed and told me she’d see me tomorrow.

00:33:40.890 --> 00:33:42.609
She has such a cute laugh.

00:33:42.609 --> 00:33:45.239
Sorry, I got distracted there for a second.

00:33:45.239 --> 00:33:47.440
At the end of the day, I was exhausted.

00:33:47.440 --> 00:33:48.440
Famished.

00:33:48.440 --> 00:33:50.179
I was so eager to retire to bed.

00:33:50.179 --> 00:33:52.619
But when I layed down and shut my eyes…

00:33:52.619 --> 00:33:55.039
I just couldn’t fall asleep.

00:33:55.039 --> 00:33:57.609
I kept opening my eyes and looking at the
clock.

00:33:57.609 --> 00:33:58.989
One o’clock.

00:33:58.989 --> 00:34:00.379
Two o’clock.

00:34:00.379 --> 00:34:01.769
Two thirty.

00:34:01.769 --> 00:34:03.719
Why wasn’t I falling asleep?

00:34:03.719 --> 00:34:04.950
Was it this new bed?

00:34:04.950 --> 00:34:06.830
Was it this new apartment?

00:34:06.830 --> 00:34:10.919
I looked around my new pad and thought about
how funny it was that I still always close

00:34:10.919 --> 00:34:13.960
bedroom door, despite being the only one here
now.

00:34:13.960 --> 00:34:16.539
Old habits do die hard I suppose.

00:34:16.539 --> 00:34:18.760
Maybe I couldn’t sleep because I was thinking
too much?

00:34:18.760 --> 00:34:22.379
Maybe Caitlyn was on my mind too.

00:34:22.379 --> 00:34:24.639
Eventually at some point I must have dozed
off.

00:34:24.639 --> 00:34:25.639
But when I awoke.

00:34:25.639 --> 00:34:28.280
It was still dark out.

00:34:28.280 --> 00:34:30.879
Out of the corner of my eye I saw the clock.

00:34:30.879 --> 00:34:33.319
Four twenty-three in the morning.

00:34:33.319 --> 00:34:34.319
Ugh.

00:34:34.319 --> 00:34:37.559
I was feeling pretty thirsty so I hopped up
to grab some water…

00:34:37.559 --> 00:34:38.559
only…

00:34:38.559 --> 00:34:43.500
when I hopped up to grab some water, my body
didn’t move an inch.

00:34:43.500 --> 00:34:47.000
Come to think of it, I hadn’t moved at all
since I had woken up.

00:34:47.000 --> 00:34:50.179
I immediately felt a wave of terror crash
over me.

00:34:50.179 --> 00:34:51.179
What was going on?

00:34:51.179 --> 00:34:52.179
Why can’t I move?

00:34:52.179 --> 00:34:53.179
What’s wrong with me?

00:34:53.179 --> 00:34:55.590
I was instantly overcome with anxiety and
discomfort.

00:34:55.590 --> 00:34:57.020
It was like a nightmare.

00:34:57.020 --> 00:34:59.210
Where nothing happens.

00:34:59.210 --> 00:35:02.619
But it was a nightmare because nothing was
happening.

00:35:02.619 --> 00:35:04.180
What if I was stuck like this forever?

00:35:04.180 --> 00:35:05.930
Who will think to come check on me?

00:35:05.930 --> 00:35:09.160
What if I starve to death like this?

00:35:09.160 --> 00:35:11.119
What if…

00:35:11.119 --> 00:35:14.970
What if…?!

00:35:14.970 --> 00:35:19.450
The next thing I remember was me waking up
the next morning.

00:35:19.450 --> 00:35:23.540
To my relief, I was able to get up and hit
the alarm clock now.

00:35:23.540 --> 00:35:25.650
What was that last night?

00:35:25.650 --> 00:35:27.030
Some kind of weird dream?

00:35:27.030 --> 00:35:29.059
Or was it real?

00:35:29.059 --> 00:35:33.240
It felt real… but it doesn’t seem real.

00:35:33.240 --> 00:35:35.060
I brought my own lunch to work that day.

00:35:35.060 --> 00:35:37.309
I opened up the fridge to find…

00:35:37.309 --> 00:35:39.240
it’s completely stuffed.

00:35:39.240 --> 00:35:43.319
I couldn’t find an open spot anywhere, so
I start to rearrange stuff to make room.

00:35:43.319 --> 00:35:45.020
“What are you doing?”

00:35:45.020 --> 00:35:46.260
I hear from behind me.

00:35:46.260 --> 00:35:49.210
I turn to see this guy Jerry standing there.

00:35:49.210 --> 00:35:51.760
Jerry is the head of the sales department.

00:35:51.760 --> 00:35:54.329
Every office has that guy, right?

00:35:54.329 --> 00:35:58.730
From what I could tell so far in my one day
here, Jerry is the guy who makes you want

00:35:58.730 --> 00:36:01.970
to take the stairs when you see him waiting
for the elevator.

00:36:01.970 --> 00:36:04.849
And I might be speaking from experience already.

00:36:04.849 --> 00:36:05.849
“I was just--”

00:36:05.849 --> 00:36:09.170
“Why do you have my food in your hand?”,
he asked in the most accusatory manner I’ve

00:36:09.170 --> 00:36:10.490
ever heard in my life.

00:36:10.490 --> 00:36:11.849
He snatched the bag from me.

00:36:11.849 --> 00:36:15.440
“I was just trying to make space, so that
I could fit my lunch.”

00:36:15.440 --> 00:36:16.440
“Yeah.

00:36:16.440 --> 00:36:17.440
OK.”

00:36:17.440 --> 00:36:18.930
He walked away.

00:36:18.930 --> 00:36:20.960
Hey, no complaint from me.

00:36:20.960 --> 00:36:23.460
Now I had a spot to put my lunch in!

00:36:23.460 --> 00:36:28.319
Throughout the day, I made sure to visit Caitlyn
and make sure she wasn’t “overworking”

00:36:28.319 --> 00:36:29.319
herself.

00:36:29.319 --> 00:36:31.720
Sometimes people forget to take little breaks.

00:36:31.720 --> 00:36:34.309
I was just looking out for my fellow employee.

00:36:34.309 --> 00:36:38.059
The lack of sleep the night before had me
all worn out.

00:36:38.059 --> 00:36:43.140
I was positive that this time, I would have
no trouble whatsoever with passing out.

00:36:43.140 --> 00:36:47.690
I shut my bedroom door behind me and literally
collapsed on my bed.

00:36:47.690 --> 00:36:51.089
I continued to lie awake for a while though.

00:36:51.089 --> 00:36:55.819
I looked at my clock periodically. 11:17.

00:36:55.819 --> 00:36:57.260
12:03.

00:36:57.260 --> 00:36:58.710
12:15.

00:36:58.710 --> 00:37:00.160
12:17.

00:37:00.160 --> 00:37:01.579
I was growing restless.

00:37:01.579 --> 00:37:06.160
I guess at some point though, I knocked out,
because a couple of hours later, I woke up

00:37:06.160 --> 00:37:07.980
in the middle of the night again.

00:37:07.980 --> 00:37:08.980
Great…

00:37:08.980 --> 00:37:12.510
I tried to look at the clock, but I couldn’t
see it from the position I was in.

00:37:12.510 --> 00:37:14.069
That’s when I realized…

00:37:14.069 --> 00:37:15.940
It had happened again.

00:37:15.940 --> 00:37:17.369
I couldn’t move.

00:37:17.369 --> 00:37:19.530
Once again I was overcome with fear.

00:37:19.530 --> 00:37:21.240
Was this going to become a regular thing?

00:37:21.240 --> 00:37:26.300
However, what I saw next was about to take
my fear and amplify it.

00:37:26.300 --> 00:37:30.760
My door was open, and this creature was standing
in the doorway.

00:37:30.760 --> 00:37:36.560
It was humanoid, but it’s body was all pitch
black and it was probably 7 or 8 feet tall.

00:37:36.560 --> 00:37:40.470
It’s head was shaped like the top of a tree
stump that had been struck by lightning and

00:37:40.470 --> 00:37:42.500
it’s eyes were glowing red.

00:37:42.500 --> 00:37:46.760
It’s mouth opening resembled a polygon with
completely random angles.

00:37:46.760 --> 00:37:51.599
But the scariest part to me, for whatever
reason, was it’s fingers.

00:37:51.599 --> 00:37:53.470
Each one was long and branch-like.

00:37:53.470 --> 00:37:56.280
Probably about 2ft in length.

00:37:56.280 --> 00:37:59.340
They were just dangling there and he…

00:37:59.340 --> 00:38:00.430
well…

00:38:00.430 --> 00:38:04.059
it was moving them around in a wave motion.

00:38:04.059 --> 00:38:05.200
I tried to move.

00:38:05.200 --> 00:38:06.290
I tried to scream!

00:38:06.290 --> 00:38:10.369
But what I found is that I could not even
do that.

00:38:10.369 --> 00:38:17.890
It started to pace towards my bed.

00:38:17.890 --> 00:38:22.049
I could not even describe to you the motion
it used to walk.

00:38:22.049 --> 00:38:24.460
It reached the foot the bed.

00:38:24.460 --> 00:38:29.730
I was fighting with every ounce of energy
I had, but my body would not budge.

00:38:29.730 --> 00:38:33.760
It came along the side of the bed and continued
to inch closer to me.

00:38:33.760 --> 00:38:39.260
I tried to scream for help, and just managed
to get out the slightest sound.

00:38:39.260 --> 00:38:40.330
“H-help.

00:38:40.330 --> 00:38:41.400
Help!”

00:38:41.400 --> 00:38:42.480
“HELP!”

00:38:42.480 --> 00:38:45.599
I screamed out as I sat up.

00:38:45.599 --> 00:38:47.809
It was morning.

00:38:47.809 --> 00:38:52.319
Again I was left with the mystery of what
this sleep paralysis was.

00:38:52.319 --> 00:38:57.309
I decided it was time to see a doctor about
it and made an appointment for after work.

00:38:57.309 --> 00:39:01.250
I wasn't going to let my rough night ruin
my perfect day, however.

00:39:01.250 --> 00:39:03.579
Today, I had a plan.

00:39:03.579 --> 00:39:06.440
When I got to work, Jerry was waiting for
the elevator.

00:39:06.440 --> 00:39:12.099
I smoothly redirected myself towards the stairs,
I could almost feel him sneering at me back.

00:39:12.099 --> 00:39:15.930
By the time I made it up the stairs, Jerry
was talking to Caitlyn about something.

00:39:15.930 --> 00:39:19.030
Luckily I saw him walk away as I walked up.

00:39:19.030 --> 00:39:21.200
I stopped and said hello to Caitlyn.

00:39:21.200 --> 00:39:23.770
She flashed her infectious smile at me.

00:39:23.770 --> 00:39:27.369
Sure, I was tired, but things were going well.

00:39:27.369 --> 00:39:29.119
I didn't bring my lunch to work today.

00:39:29.119 --> 00:39:33.880
Instead, when it got to my break time, I went
over to Caitlin's desk and invited her to

00:39:33.880 --> 00:39:35.619
go grab some food with me.

00:39:35.619 --> 00:39:37.580
She delightfully accepted.

00:39:37.580 --> 00:39:39.230
We got sandwiches.

00:39:39.230 --> 00:39:40.960
And we totally hit it off.

00:39:40.960 --> 00:39:43.569
We were talking and cracking jokes the entire
time.

00:39:43.569 --> 00:39:47.940
She does this little thing where she'll get
excited about something and kind of bite her

00:39:47.940 --> 00:39:48.940
lip.

00:39:48.940 --> 00:39:49.940
It's incredible.

00:39:49.940 --> 00:39:52.680
We got back to the office and she offered
me a mint from her drawer.

00:39:52.680 --> 00:39:57.250
I accepted, so she went to open the little
box of mints and accidentally spilled a bunch

00:39:57.250 --> 00:39:58.700
of them on her desk.

00:39:58.700 --> 00:40:01.160
We both reached for the loose mints.

00:40:01.160 --> 00:40:04.300
I saw my chance and grabbed her hand and held
it in mine.

00:40:04.300 --> 00:40:06.900
“Here relax, I'll take care of this.”

00:40:06.900 --> 00:40:10.109
I told her, and used my other hand to gather
the mints.

00:40:10.109 --> 00:40:11.569
“What's going on here?”

00:40:11.569 --> 00:40:15.340
I heard the stern voice that belonged to Jerry
as he walked up.

00:40:15.340 --> 00:40:16.910
She quickly pulled her hands away.

00:40:16.910 --> 00:40:21.420
I finished gathering up the mints and after
taking one for myself, deposited the rest

00:40:21.420 --> 00:40:22.420
back in the container.

00:40:22.420 --> 00:40:25.859
I was taken aback by what she said next…

00:40:25.859 --> 00:40:30.180
She told him… hey babe, we just got back
from lunch.

00:40:30.180 --> 00:40:34.420
My heart sank deep into my chest and my head
started burning up.

00:40:34.420 --> 00:40:36.880
Did my ears deceive me?

00:40:36.880 --> 00:40:42.099
Did she really just call Jerry, the prick
of the office and her boss, “babe”?

00:40:42.099 --> 00:40:45.210
Surely this must be a joke; a cruel meme of
some kind.

00:40:45.210 --> 00:40:49.549
He came up behind her and kissed the top of
her head, crushing whatever hope I had left

00:40:49.549 --> 00:40:52.700
and glaring at me as he did so.

00:40:52.700 --> 00:40:53.780
I couldn't believe it.

00:40:53.780 --> 00:40:56.059
How is this idiot better than me?

00:40:56.059 --> 00:40:58.329
I felt myself starting to blush.

00:40:58.329 --> 00:41:01.109
I felt so stupid thinking she was into me.

00:41:01.109 --> 00:41:02.109
She was just being friendly.

00:41:02.109 --> 00:41:03.910
How did I not see this coming?

00:41:03.910 --> 00:41:04.910
“Uhh…

00:41:04.910 --> 00:41:07.089
I gotta get back to work.”

00:41:07.089 --> 00:41:09.309
She thanked me for my company at lunch.

00:41:09.309 --> 00:41:13.589
As I turned away I could feel his glare on
me so strongly that I wished I’d worn sunscreen.

00:41:13.589 --> 00:41:16.559
“You went out to lunch with that guy?”

00:41:16.559 --> 00:41:20.289
I heard him ask her, with an attitude as I
fled the scene.

00:41:20.289 --> 00:41:21.289
Great.

00:41:21.289 --> 00:41:23.540
Three days and I was already making enemies.

00:41:23.540 --> 00:41:26.630
The rest of my afternoon was so hard to get
through.

00:41:26.630 --> 00:41:29.299
I was constantly dozing off at my desk.

00:41:29.299 --> 00:41:31.890
Not enough to fully fall asleep, mind you.

00:41:31.890 --> 00:41:35.910
Just enough to feel as about as miserable
as I felt rejected.

00:41:35.910 --> 00:41:40.880
I wanted to just go home and sleep, but I
had my doctor's appointment that evening.

00:41:40.880 --> 00:41:43.609
The doc confirmed what I pretty much already
knew.

00:41:43.609 --> 00:41:45.569
I had sleep paralysis.

00:41:45.569 --> 00:41:47.839
One and every 12 people get it or something.

00:41:47.839 --> 00:41:51.720
He questioned me about my lifestyle and when
he found out I had just made a big move, he

00:41:51.720 --> 00:41:54.849
was almost positive that was the reason for
my issues.

00:41:54.849 --> 00:41:58.910
Psychological stress and abnormal sleep cycles
are apparently the two biggest factors that

00:41:58.910 --> 00:42:00.619
usually contribute to it.

00:42:00.619 --> 00:42:05.700
He told me that the hallucinations are a common
symptom, basically my body thinks it’s asleep

00:42:05.700 --> 00:42:06.700
while it’s awake.

00:42:06.700 --> 00:42:10.660
I was supposed to see a psychiatrist if the
problem persisted once I’d settled into

00:42:10.660 --> 00:42:11.660
my new routine.

00:42:11.660 --> 00:42:16.619
Not exactly the treatment I was hoping for,
but it was somewhat reassuring that he expected

00:42:16.619 --> 00:42:18.619
me to recover on my own.

00:42:18.619 --> 00:42:21.789
That night I actually had a better time falling
asleep than before.

00:42:21.789 --> 00:42:24.260
I must have been out by 11 or 12.

00:42:24.260 --> 00:42:29.020
But that didn’t stop me from waking up in
the middle of the night again, unable to move,

00:42:29.020 --> 00:42:30.730
unable to speak.

00:42:30.730 --> 00:42:34.529
Officially knowing that I suffered from sleep
paralysis didn’t make the experience any

00:42:34.529 --> 00:42:35.529
less scary.

00:42:35.529 --> 00:42:38.150
When you have it, it feels like you’re never
going to wake up from it.

00:42:38.150 --> 00:42:44.329
And the things you see feel incredibly real,
and you feel incredibly helpless.

00:42:44.329 --> 00:42:48.420
That’s why I wanted to scream when I saw
a knife-wielding silhouette standing in my

00:42:48.420 --> 00:42:49.420
doorframe.

00:42:49.420 --> 00:42:53.710
The man stepped forward and caught a little
bit of moonlight, just enough for me to identify

00:42:53.710 --> 00:42:55.900
who it was.

00:42:55.900 --> 00:42:56.900
Jerry.

00:42:56.900 --> 00:42:59.890
As per usual, he did NOT look happy to see
me.

00:42:59.890 --> 00:43:05.079
He tip-toed across the room to the foot of
my bed and stared down at me with disgust.

00:43:05.079 --> 00:43:09.950
He continued to look at me for about 2 full
minutes.

00:43:09.950 --> 00:43:11.680
His body was trembling.

00:43:11.680 --> 00:43:17.349
Finally, he came around to the side of the
bed, taking an almost identical path to the

00:43:17.349 --> 00:43:19.779
creature from the night before.

00:43:19.779 --> 00:43:23.339
He raised the knife in the air, gripping it
so hard that I could see the loss of circulation

00:43:23.339 --> 00:43:24.339
to his fingers.

00:43:24.339 --> 00:43:29.829
He froze in that position, almost like he
was waiting for me to make the first move.

00:43:29.829 --> 00:43:30.940
I couldn’t take it!

00:43:30.940 --> 00:43:32.339
The anxiety was killing me!

00:43:32.339 --> 00:43:35.140
I just wanted him to do it already to get
it over with!

00:43:35.140 --> 00:43:41.270
The last thing I could remember though, was
him, stuck in that position, trembling like

00:43:41.270 --> 00:43:43.289
a maniac.

00:43:43.289 --> 00:43:45.309
Morning came.

00:43:45.309 --> 00:43:51.099
I turned off my alarm clock and the post-nightmare
relief felt incredible as it dawned on me.

00:43:51.099 --> 00:43:53.420
I actually felt pretty decent for once.

00:43:53.420 --> 00:43:58.680
Not back to where I was before the move, but
not 100% exhausted either.

00:43:58.680 --> 00:44:03.000
It was Friday so I thought maybe I’d have
the energy to go out on the town and explore

00:44:03.000 --> 00:44:05.180
my new city after work tonight.

00:44:05.180 --> 00:44:07.510
Maybe it would help get my mind off things.

00:44:07.510 --> 00:44:11.329
I hopped out of bed and as I began to get
dressed…

00:44:11.329 --> 00:44:13.000
I realized something.

00:44:13.000 --> 00:44:17.890
Something that flushed whatever optimism or
relief I had away.

00:44:17.890 --> 00:44:23.190
Something that made my body and legs lock
up, just as they had the two previous nights.

00:44:23.190 --> 00:44:27.539
Something that made my heart sink deep into
my chest, just as it had when I found out

00:44:27.539 --> 00:44:29.400
about Caitlyn and Jerry.

00:44:29.400 --> 00:44:37.839
What I realized was… my bedroom door was
open...

00:44:37.839 --> 00:44:41.910
7 - Play With Me

00:44:41.910 --> 00:44:44.390
Are you awake?

00:44:44.390 --> 00:44:47.710
Why are you hiding?

00:44:47.710 --> 00:44:59.730
I don't mean you any harm.

00:44:59.730 --> 00:45:10.400
I know it's late, but I want to play!

00:45:10.400 --> 00:45:21.420
You haven't picked me up for nearly a month…I
want to have tea with you again.

00:45:21.420 --> 00:45:36.339
I promise not to spill.

00:45:36.339 --> 00:45:47.119
I didn't know it was hot and I'm sorry it
ruined your favorite shirt.

00:45:47.119 --> 00:45:52.980
I'm happy to have tea and eat biscuits with
you today!

00:45:52.980 --> 00:45:57.349
Your eyes are beautiful with that dress….I
wish I had such lovely eyes.

00:45:57.349 --> 00:45:58.359
Don't turn away from me!

00:45:58.359 --> 00:45:59.359
Why are you ignoring me?

00:45:59.359 --> 00:46:01.839
Is it because you don't love me like your
other dolls?

00:46:01.839 --> 00:46:02.839
No!

00:46:02.839 --> 00:46:03.839
Don't put me away!

00:46:03.839 --> 00:46:04.839
I didn't mean anything by it!

00:46:04.839 --> 00:46:05.839
Please love me….I'm not as pretty as your
other dolls, but I want affection too.

00:46:05.839 --> 00:46:06.839
Don't leave me...here.

00:46:06.839 --> 00:46:07.839
Do my cries and scratches in the night scare
you?

00:46:07.839 --> 00:46:08.839
If you take me out one more time...we can
play a game.

00:46:08.839 --> 00:46:09.839
It'll be easy, I promise.

00:46:09.839 --> 00:46:10.839
Please don't fret, I only want to play with
you.

00:46:10.839 --> 00:46:11.839
We can be best friends forever, I’ll never
leave you.

00:46:11.839 --> 00:46:12.839
I thought you were lonely.

00:46:12.839 --> 00:46:13.839
Isn’t that why you have so many dolls?

00:46:13.839 --> 00:46:14.839
You hugged me and loved me...now why do you
hate me?

00:46:14.839 --> 00:46:15.839
We had lots of fun together.

00:46:15.839 --> 00:46:16.839
Is my hair too knotted or my dress too dirty?

00:46:16.839 --> 00:46:17.839
I know it’s late, but will you play with
me?

00:46:17.839 --> 00:46:18.839
One last time?

00:46:18.839 --> 00:46:19.839
I hate seeing you cry.

00:46:19.839 --> 00:46:20.839
We can play hide-and-seek.

00:46:20.839 --> 00:46:21.839
You hide and I’ll seek you.

00:46:21.839 --> 00:46:24.290
If you win, you can do whatever you want with
me and I promise to behave.

00:46:24.290 --> 00:46:30.589
If I win, then you have to play with me when
I want to play.

00:46:30.589 --> 00:46:31.650
I’m glad you’re letting me out to play
this time!

00:46:31.650 --> 00:46:33.480
I promise not to disappoint.

00:46:33.480 --> 00:46:40.400
Don’t worry, I won’t peek, not one bit.

00:46:40.400 --> 00:46:44.109
Be quick though!

00:46:44.109 --> 00:46:45.349
1...2...3….…6....….10!

00:46:45.349 --> 00:46:54.000
Ready or not, I’m coming for you!

00:46:54.000 --> 00:46:57.710
Where are you?

00:46:57.710 --> 00:47:01.890
Are you in the closet?

00:47:01.890 --> 00:47:06.619
I thought I heard a door close...no?

00:47:06.619 --> 00:47:10.170
Okay, perhaps you went downstairs.

00:47:10.170 --> 00:47:13.270
I can’t wait to find you.

00:47:13.270 --> 00:47:14.920
Did you go all the way to the basement?

00:47:14.920 --> 00:47:15.920
Careful, you know you’re not supposed to
play down here.

00:47:15.920 --> 00:47:16.920
Oh?

00:47:16.920 --> 00:47:17.920
You chose the doll house?

00:47:17.920 --> 00:47:19.340
The one that was made for us to play in together?

00:47:19.340 --> 00:47:22.000
I'm happy that you thought of me.

00:47:22.000 --> 00:47:24.279
Now we can be together forever.

00:47:24.279 --> 00:47:27.240
Don't worry, no one will find us here.

00:47:27.240 --> 00:47:29.410
I made sure of that.

00:47:29.410 --> 00:47:34.859
The door is locked and now it can be us.

00:47:34.859 --> 00:47:35.859
What's that?

00:47:35.859 --> 00:47:36.859
You're hungry?

00:47:36.859 --> 00:47:37.859
We can have another tea party.

00:47:37.859 --> 00:47:38.859
What do you mean no?

00:47:38.859 --> 00:47:42.180
I don't know how long it's been, so why do
you keep asking?

00:47:42.180 --> 00:47:45.049
You know they can't hear you, so why waste
your voice?

00:47:45.049 --> 00:47:46.049
Wake up!

00:47:46.049 --> 00:47:47.049
Why won't you move?

00:47:47.049 --> 00:47:48.049
Wake up!!

00:47:48.049 --> 00:47:49.910
It's time to play!

00:47:49.910 --> 00:48:01.109
Why are you so cold?

00:48:01.109 --> 00:48:14.680
Do you need a blanket?

00:48:14.680 --> 00:48:19.000
I can find one.

00:48:19.000 --> 00:48:21.890
Answer me!!

00:48:21.890 --> 00:48:30.549
Why are you ignoring me again?!?!

00:48:30.549 --> 00:48:33.751
It's been a long time since you moved...it
smells like something is rotting.

00:48:33.751 --> 00:48:34.751
Why did you have to die?

00:48:34.751 --> 00:48:35.751
It's dark and cold...but I won't leave you.

00:48:35.751 --> 00:48:36.751
I never will.

00:48:36.751 --> 00:48:38.829
Number 8 - Creepy Clown School Lockdown

00:48:38.829 --> 00:48:43.529
As a kid, I never understood why some of my
classmates were afraid of clowns.

00:48:43.529 --> 00:48:45.359
I didn't really find them scary.

00:48:45.359 --> 00:48:47.430
Not that I found that funny either.

00:48:47.430 --> 00:48:50.190
Most of them just looked kind of goofy and
dumb.

00:48:50.190 --> 00:48:54.599
I remember having this exact argument with
my best friend Kevin at the lunch tables in

00:48:54.599 --> 00:48:55.609
elementary.

00:48:55.609 --> 00:49:00.130
His argument was always that I needed to see
the movie IT in order to understand, but being

00:49:00.130 --> 00:49:03.349
in second grade at the time, my parents would
never let me watch it.

00:49:03.349 --> 00:49:06.960
I actually remember on Halloween, some of
the older kids in the neighborhood dressed

00:49:06.960 --> 00:49:10.099
up as clowns and went around scaring trick-or-treaters.

00:49:10.099 --> 00:49:14.059
Maybe I just had thick skin, but I remember
one of them chasing our entire friend group

00:49:14.059 --> 00:49:18.040
away and me being left on the sidewalk laughing
at their expense.

00:49:18.040 --> 00:49:22.930
But anyways, this story takes place in November
of that second grade year.

00:49:22.930 --> 00:49:24.300
Just after Halloween.

00:49:24.300 --> 00:49:27.019
We were sitting in math class, boring as ever.

00:49:27.019 --> 00:49:31.579
When situations like this arise, which were
quite often during math, Kevin and I would

00:49:31.579 --> 00:49:34.099
meet in the bathroom and trade baseball cards.

00:49:34.099 --> 00:49:35.200
We had a system.

00:49:35.200 --> 00:49:39.250
One of us would give the signal, and we would
stagger our bathroom requests as not to raise

00:49:39.250 --> 00:49:40.880
suspicion from our teacher.

00:49:40.880 --> 00:49:44.880
On this particular occasion, Kevin had gone
off to the bathroom first and I gave it a

00:49:44.880 --> 00:49:47.319
good 5 minutes before raising my hand.

00:49:47.319 --> 00:49:51.900
As I was waiting to be called on, our teacher,
Mr Davis, was interrupted by the sound of

00:49:51.900 --> 00:49:56.559
the intercom, which was strange because they
usually only did announcements at the beginning

00:49:56.559 --> 00:49:58.160
and end of the day.

00:49:58.160 --> 00:50:01.809
"Attention all students and staff.

00:50:01.809 --> 00:50:08.390
At this time we are conducting an internal
lockdown.

00:50:08.390 --> 00:50:10.730
This is not a drill.

00:50:10.730 --> 00:50:11.730
Please initiate lockdown at this time."

00:50:11.730 --> 00:50:16.319
Our teacher was pretty calm with his response,
walking over to the door and locking it.

00:50:16.319 --> 00:50:20.549
He told us all to line up along the back wall
and keep quiet as he crossed the room to pull

00:50:20.549 --> 00:50:21.660
down the blinds.

00:50:21.660 --> 00:50:26.170
I figured he had been though many lockdown
drills before and this probably wasn't anything

00:50:26.170 --> 00:50:27.170
big.

00:50:27.170 --> 00:50:31.420
We had a lock down at my old school once and
it turned out to be a parent who just forgot

00:50:31.420 --> 00:50:32.440
to sign in.

00:50:32.440 --> 00:50:34.920
We waited like that for about 5 minutes.

00:50:34.920 --> 00:50:40.520
One kid asked Mr. Davis much longer it would
be, he got a hard Shh! from our teacher, signalling

00:50:40.520 --> 00:50:42.650
that no talking would be tolerated.

00:50:42.650 --> 00:50:46.119
It was about at that time when I remembered
that Kevin was still in the bathroom.

00:50:46.119 --> 00:50:50.849
I debated in my head on whether I should bring
this to the teacher's attention, but was ultimately

00:50:50.849 --> 00:50:54.410
too scared after seeing that other kid get
scolded for making a peep.

00:50:54.410 --> 00:50:59.049
That might sound kind of ridiculous given
the circumstances, but keep in mind, I was

00:50:59.049 --> 00:51:03.210
only 7 years old at the time and still very
intimidated by authority.

00:51:03.210 --> 00:51:07.049
We waited in silence for a little while longer.

00:51:07.049 --> 00:51:11.069
With each minute that passed, the situation
got more tense.

00:51:11.069 --> 00:51:13.160
I started to feel anxiety.

00:51:13.160 --> 00:51:15.810
Butterflies in my stomach.

00:51:15.810 --> 00:51:21.630
That's when there was another announcement
on the intercom.

00:51:21.630 --> 00:51:31.710
This... circus music started playing over
the intercom.

00:51:31.710 --> 00:51:35.519
And then... after that...

00:51:35.519 --> 00:51:37.931
There was, what sounded like laughter in the
background.

00:51:37.931 --> 00:51:42.119
One of the girls in the class asked Mr. Davis
what was going on.

00:51:42.119 --> 00:51:46.549
He told her to keep quiet, but his voice cracked
and he stuttered in saying so.

00:51:46.549 --> 00:51:50.000
That may have actually been the scariest part
of the whole ordeal for me.

00:51:50.000 --> 00:51:53.990
Being a kid, and seeing an adult... and on
top of that, someone who you're supposed to

00:51:53.990 --> 00:51:56.990
feel safe with being visably shaken like that.

00:51:56.990 --> 00:51:58.480
It was terrifying.

00:51:58.480 --> 00:52:00.849
I guess I wasn't the only one who felt that
way.

00:52:00.849 --> 00:52:05.099
I could hear sniffles coming from one of the
other kids, like they had been crying.

00:52:05.099 --> 00:52:07.829
Abruptly, the music just stopped.

00:52:07.829 --> 00:52:11.510
We were all sitting on the floor in a line
in the corner of the room.

00:52:11.510 --> 00:52:15.090
I actually closed my eyes, as if that would
somehow help me.

00:52:15.090 --> 00:52:20.870
But nothing could block out the breathing
that I heard blaring over the school intercom.

00:52:20.870 --> 00:52:25.730
Until it stopped.

00:52:25.730 --> 00:52:27.809
We sat in silence for a while longer.

00:52:27.809 --> 00:52:29.230
Hearts racing.

00:52:29.230 --> 00:52:30.780
Minds racing faster.

00:52:30.780 --> 00:52:34.079
The silence was broken by a slam and a group
of screams!

00:52:34.079 --> 00:52:36.740
The sound traveled from down the hall.

00:52:36.740 --> 00:52:40.790
At this, I opened my eyes to see Mr. Davis
jump up and push the big wooden teacher's

00:52:40.790 --> 00:52:44.309
desk from across the room in front of the
door.

00:52:44.309 --> 00:52:46.950
I noticed tears streaming down his cheeks
as he did so.

00:52:46.950 --> 00:52:51.190
I started to feel sick to my stomach as the
anxiety continued to build.

00:52:51.190 --> 00:52:57.210
Footsteps approached from down the hallway.

00:52:57.210 --> 00:53:03.190
They stopped near our door.

00:53:03.190 --> 00:53:05.400
I could see a shadow on the wall.

00:53:05.400 --> 00:53:06.490
Someone was standing out there.

00:53:06.490 --> 00:53:08.900
I could tell by the shape that...

00:53:08.900 --> 00:53:11.910
It was the shadow of a clown.

00:53:11.910 --> 00:53:16.099
After a short pause it seemed the shadow had
disappeared and I started to feel a little

00:53:16.099 --> 00:53:19.150
bit of relief that the clown had walked away.

00:53:19.150 --> 00:53:24.619
There was a bang on the door and suddenly,
and standing at the door window was a terrifying

00:53:24.619 --> 00:53:29.539
looking clown with bright white face paint,
a huge cartoony, toothy smile painted on his

00:53:29.539 --> 00:53:33.900
face to contrast the cold evil looking smirk
on his actual lips.

00:53:33.900 --> 00:53:38.150
He was somewhat overweight and wore a big
baggy clown suit.

00:53:38.150 --> 00:53:41.520
The whole class screamed as he repeatedly
tried to open the door.

00:53:41.520 --> 00:53:45.440
He went from trying to wiggle the doorknob
free to rearing back and trying to kick in

00:53:45.440 --> 00:53:48.859
the wooden door, the class screaming each
time he did so.

00:53:48.859 --> 00:53:52.299
It realistically didn't last that long before
he gave up and moved on, but it felt like

00:53:52.299 --> 00:53:54.099
forever to me at the time.

00:53:54.099 --> 00:53:57.550
That was the last we saw of the mysterious
lockdown clown.

00:53:57.550 --> 00:54:01.369
But in all of the hysteria, I completely forgot
about Kevin.

00:54:01.369 --> 00:54:06.160
The lockdown lasted for another 20 minutes
or so until each room was cleared.

00:54:06.160 --> 00:54:10.329
They made the announcement over the intercom,
telling us the lockdown was over and teachers

00:54:10.329 --> 00:54:11.500
could resume classes.

00:54:11.500 --> 00:54:15.640
They didn't actually ever say what had happened,
probably not wanting to raise any panic.

00:54:15.640 --> 00:54:20.440
A few minutes later, Kevin appeared at the
door and looked like an absolute wreck.

00:54:20.440 --> 00:54:26.480
His hair was literally standing up on end,
he had dark circles around his eyes and tears

00:54:26.480 --> 00:54:27.839
streaming down his face.

00:54:27.839 --> 00:54:30.660
His entire body was shaking.

00:54:30.660 --> 00:54:34.069
I'd never seen someone looking so disheveled.

00:54:34.069 --> 00:54:39.039
Class was once again interrupted so that our
teacher could escort Kevin to the nurse.

00:54:39.039 --> 00:54:41.420
He didn't come back to class after that.

00:54:41.420 --> 00:54:47.009
And his parents ended up holding him out of
school for 3 FULL WEEKS to recover.

00:54:47.009 --> 00:54:49.720
He came back just before Winter Break.

00:54:49.720 --> 00:54:53.950
I asked him what had happened a couple times,
but he always just told me that he didn't

00:54:53.950 --> 00:54:55.230
want to talk about it.

00:54:55.230 --> 00:54:59.190
He ended up coming to school for the rest
of second semester before his family moved

00:54:59.190 --> 00:55:01.170
away at the start of that summer.

00:55:01.170 --> 00:55:03.900
He was just never quite the same after that.

00:55:03.900 --> 00:55:08.340
We never got an official story on what had
happened, only a swirl of rumors that the

00:55:08.340 --> 00:55:10.549
intruder had never actually been found.

00:55:10.549 --> 00:55:14.999
I shudder to think about what would have happened
if Mr. Davis hadn't pushed the desk up along

00:55:14.999 --> 00:55:16.079
the door...

00:55:16.079 --> 00:55:22.710
Anyways, I remembered about this story all
these years later because...

00:55:22.710 --> 00:55:23.789
I oftentimes cut through this park on the
way home from the bus station.

00:55:23.789 --> 00:55:26.150
They had a carnival going on over the weekend.

00:55:26.150 --> 00:55:30.290
It was was closed now, and it was about 2:00AM
as I cut through the fairground.

00:55:30.290 --> 00:55:35.809
At one of the ticket booths, a light had been
left on, the only light in entirety of area

00:55:35.809 --> 00:55:37.180
for that matter.

00:55:37.180 --> 00:55:44.049
And that's when I saw a clown crash up against
the glass and stare at me with those wide

00:55:44.049 --> 00:55:45.049
eyes.

00:55:45.049 --> 00:55:48.000
It may have been just some teenagers, or YouTubers
pulling a prank.

00:55:48.000 --> 00:55:49.000
But I ran.

00:55:49.000 --> 00:55:50.610
As fast as I could.

00:55:50.610 --> 00:55:54.520
And didn't stop until I was locked inside
of my room.

00:55:54.520 --> 00:56:04.170
Because clowns terrify me now.

00:56:04.170 --> 00:56:06.809
Number 9 - Jason

00:56:06.809 --> 00:56:11.940
This is a story that took place 6 months ago,
when my first son, Elliott had just turned

00:56:11.940 --> 00:56:13.520
5 years old.

00:56:13.520 --> 00:56:17.829
Jason was first introduced into our lives
when we decided to hold off sending Elliott

00:56:17.829 --> 00:56:19.470
to Kindergarten.

00:56:19.470 --> 00:56:23.599
Since his birthday was so close to the cut-off,
we decided it would be best him to go start

00:56:23.599 --> 00:56:27.309
school as one of the older kids in his class
as opposed to the youngest.

00:56:27.309 --> 00:56:31.480
So when he started talking to Jason, we felt
like we had made the right decision.

00:56:31.480 --> 00:56:34.279
Jason is Elliott’s imaginary friend.

00:56:34.279 --> 00:56:38.480
I can’t imagine how the other Kindergarteners
would have reacted to the idea of an imaginary

00:56:38.480 --> 00:56:42.900
friend, so it seemed like starting a bit later
would give him time to go through this phase

00:56:42.900 --> 00:56:45.599
and be ready for school next fall.

00:56:45.599 --> 00:56:49.800
The first time I can remember hearing about
Jason was one evening just as we were finishing

00:56:49.800 --> 00:56:50.960
up dinner.

00:56:50.960 --> 00:56:54.759
Elliott had requested that he be allowed to
take some food up to his food to give to Jason.

00:56:54.759 --> 00:56:59.970
Julianna, my other half, inquisitively asked
him who Jason was, to which he replied, “my

00:56:59.970 --> 00:57:01.779
friend who lives in the closet upstairs.”

00:57:01.779 --> 00:57:07.140
Julianna granted him permission to take the
rest of his food up with as long as he promised

00:57:07.140 --> 00:57:10.309
to come clean the dish before he went off
the bed.

00:57:10.309 --> 00:57:15.230
I shot her a look, but she, being the free-willed
spirit that she is, ignored me until Elliott

00:57:15.230 --> 00:57:16.839
had run up the steps.

00:57:16.839 --> 00:57:20.780
I didn’t think it was a good idea to encourage
that kind of behaviour, but she assured me

00:57:20.780 --> 00:57:25.460
that having an imaginary friend was totally
normal, and that it would be a good idea to

00:57:25.460 --> 00:57:29.019
humor him until he was ready to grow out of
it on his own.

00:57:29.019 --> 00:57:34.000
Hesitantly, I agreed and eventually I would
talk to Elliott about Jason on a day to day

00:57:34.000 --> 00:57:35.000
basis.

00:57:35.000 --> 00:57:38.670
Eventually, I learned how to use Jason to
my advantage.

00:57:38.670 --> 00:57:41.990
For example, when Elliott didn’t want to
get in the car to go to the dentist, I would

00:57:41.990 --> 00:57:47.109
tell him that Jason said he wanted to go to
the dentist, and that Elliott should come.

00:57:47.109 --> 00:57:50.210
At times, Elliott would hardly mention Jason
at all.

00:57:50.210 --> 00:57:53.859
Other times, it seemed that Jason was all
he wanted to talk about.

00:57:53.859 --> 00:57:57.230
One time we caught him taking snacks from
the kitchen and he claimed that they were

00:57:57.230 --> 00:57:58.230
for Jason.

00:57:58.230 --> 00:58:02.980
Julianna wisely let this slide, and later
told me that if this was the only way that

00:58:02.980 --> 00:58:08.180
we could get Elliott to eat, it was OK with
her, and after many long battles at the dinner

00:58:08.180 --> 00:58:10.099
table, I was quick to agree.

00:58:10.099 --> 00:58:14.390
I would oftentimes hear Elliott in his room
“talking” to Jason, and I wondered how

00:58:14.390 --> 00:58:17.309
long this whole phase would last.

00:58:17.309 --> 00:58:22.619
At one point I asked him what Jason looked
like and he told me that he told me that he

00:58:22.619 --> 00:58:26.460
wore a “black snow hat” and had a long
fuzzy beard.

00:58:26.460 --> 00:58:30.940
I was taken off guard by this, since I had
always imagined that Elliott’s idea of Jason

00:58:30.940 --> 00:58:32.450
was a kid who was his age.

00:58:32.450 --> 00:58:37.299
I brought this up with Juliana, and she assured
me that it was perfectly normal for a kid

00:58:37.299 --> 00:58:39.930
to have an adult as an imaginary friend.

00:58:39.930 --> 00:58:45.150
After all, we are both adults and he spends
most of his time with us, so it makes sense

00:58:45.150 --> 00:58:47.759
that he would see an adult as his friend.

00:58:47.759 --> 00:58:51.589
She even said that her younger sister had
an imaginary friend as a kid who was supposedly

00:58:51.589 --> 00:58:56.480
an old man named Vin, which she thinks is
a result of them having spent a lot of time

00:58:56.480 --> 00:58:58.410
at their grandparents house back then.

00:58:58.410 --> 00:59:04.390
I had never had an imaginary friend, or any
siblings, so I just had to take my wife’s

00:59:04.390 --> 00:59:05.780
word on all of this.

00:59:05.780 --> 00:59:11.760
That is… until one day, that changed everything
and... still makes me paranoid.

00:59:11.760 --> 00:59:17.150
We had just gotten back from this Italian
restaurant, one of the only decent places

00:59:17.150 --> 00:59:21.180
that we can get Elliott to eat on a consistent
basis.

00:59:21.180 --> 00:59:25.140
We parked in the driveway and decided to go
for a short walk, since it was pretty nice

00:59:25.140 --> 00:59:26.480
out that evening.

00:59:26.480 --> 00:59:30.640
Normally we come into the house through the
garage, but since we had gone for a walk,

00:59:30.640 --> 00:59:33.890
we entered in the front door on this occasion.

00:59:33.890 --> 00:59:35.890
As we were taking our shoes off, I heard…

00:59:35.890 --> 00:59:39.900
what I thought was the sound of a cough coming
from upstairs…

00:59:39.900 --> 00:59:43.010
I turned to Julianna wondering if she had
heard it too.

00:59:43.010 --> 00:59:48.369
She looked pale, and shocked as she asked
me in a panic, “what was that?”

00:59:48.369 --> 00:59:52.910
This was probably loud enough that if someone
was upstairs they might here.

00:59:52.910 --> 00:59:56.299
Elliott told us that it was probably just
Jason.

00:59:56.299 --> 01:00:00.509
I told my wife and son to stay put and I went
to investigate.

01:00:00.509 --> 01:00:04.310
When I got upstairs and went into Elliott’s
room, the light was on and the window was

01:00:04.310 --> 01:00:05.310
open.

01:00:05.310 --> 01:00:08.369
I searched the entire house, but was unable
to find anything.

01:00:08.369 --> 01:00:12.440
The window from Elliott’s room leads onto
a section of roof that is pretty high up,

01:00:12.440 --> 01:00:15.210
but not impossible to jump down from.

01:00:15.210 --> 01:00:20.030
We later interrogated Elliott to see if he
had left the window open, but he swore he

01:00:20.030 --> 01:00:21.030
couldn’t remember.

01:00:21.030 --> 01:00:25.670
We tried to get him to tell us if Jason was
real, but it was a delicate situation.

01:00:25.670 --> 01:00:29.810
We didn’t want to scare him for life, but
we didn’t want him to be in danger either.

01:00:29.810 --> 01:00:34.619
Of course, at his age, I don’t think he
fully understood the difference between real

01:00:34.619 --> 01:00:36.119
and pretend yet.

01:00:36.119 --> 01:00:40.320
We did end up calling the police, and I half
expected them to find proof that someone was

01:00:40.320 --> 01:00:44.569
living in the closet, but they couldn’t
find any DNA that didn’t belong to Elliott

01:00:44.569 --> 01:00:46.599
anywhere in the room.

01:00:46.599 --> 01:00:50.249
Elliott made friends with a couple of kids
on the block, and he never really brings up

01:00:50.249 --> 01:00:56.029
Jason anymore, but it truly chills me to think
that someone could have been in our house

01:00:56.029 --> 01:00:57.470
talking to our son.

01:00:57.470 --> 01:00:59.599
In his room while he slept.

01:00:59.599 --> 01:01:03.400
Possibly using him to sneak food up, and to
be honest, who knows what else?

01:01:03.400 --> 01:01:07.880
Now, I check all the upstairs rooms every
night before bed.

01:01:07.880 --> 01:01:09.819
Including the closets and under the bed.

01:01:09.819 --> 01:01:13.900
I try to do it when Elliott is not in the
room so he doesn’t get to thinking.

01:01:13.900 --> 01:01:18.410
He’ll be starting school in the fall, and
I doubt we’ll really have any confirmation

01:01:18.410 --> 01:01:23.039
on whether Jason was just an imaginary friend
or not until he’s a little bit older.

01:01:23.039 --> 01:01:27.910
Julianna and I have a second child on the
way now though, so I really hope we find out

01:01:27.910 --> 01:01:36.759
sooner rather than later....

01:01:36.759 --> 01:01:39.710
Number 10 - Christina Grimmie Final Goodbye

01:01:39.710 --> 01:01:44.390
I've always been strangely fascinated by tragedy.

01:01:44.390 --> 01:01:48.609
Now, don't get me wrong, it's not like I'm
happy that terrible things happen.

01:01:48.609 --> 01:01:51.769
I certainly don't encourage terrorism or anything,
but

01:01:51.769 --> 01:01:55.070
I have spent many nights on the weird side
of YouTube,

01:01:55.070 --> 01:02:00.279
watching 9/11 videos or watching houses get
swept away by Hurricane Katrina.

01:02:00.279 --> 01:02:04.299
I think we all have a small tendency for our
eyes to be drawn to the morbid.

01:02:04.299 --> 01:02:07.960
Just look how drivers stop to stare at the
wreckage during a highway traffic accident

01:02:07.960 --> 01:02:10.489
and in turn, slow down the traffic themselves.

01:02:10.489 --> 01:02:14.989
I also think that our curiosity with such
things as a culture is related to our love

01:02:14.989 --> 01:02:16.119
for ghost towns.

01:02:16.119 --> 01:02:20.410
I always think it's amazing when a place that
once had so much buzz and attention

01:02:20.410 --> 01:02:23.089
becomes barren and empty so quickly.

01:02:23.089 --> 01:02:26.529
Sometimes, tragedy and ghost towns can go
hand in hand.

01:02:26.529 --> 01:02:28.720
Just look at Pompeii or Chernobyl.

01:02:28.720 --> 01:02:32.289
One night in late 2016,
I found a similar example.

01:02:32.289 --> 01:02:35.059
A virtual ghost town, if you will.

01:02:35.059 --> 01:02:38.289
While browsing YouTube at 3 in the morning
before going to bed,

01:02:38.289 --> 01:02:41.819
I stumbled upon a video from Christina Grimmie.

01:02:41.819 --> 01:02:44.560
Christina was a YouTube singer who was tragically
shot and killed

01:02:44.560 --> 01:02:47.289
just after her concert in Orlando back in
June.

01:02:47.289 --> 01:02:51.680
This was a truly sad and scary time for her
fans and the community.

01:02:51.680 --> 01:02:56.150
Christina was just 22 years old and she was
one of the first big YouTubers to pass away.

01:02:56.150 --> 01:03:00.249
Since she posted so regularly, I imagine that
fans were left with a much bigger hole in

01:03:00.249 --> 01:03:03.220
their lives
as compared to other celebrity deaths.

01:03:03.220 --> 01:03:06.279
As I clicked through some of her videos
and read some of the comments,

01:03:06.279 --> 01:03:09.430
I could see that many of her fans saw her
as a friend,

01:03:09.430 --> 01:03:11.499
and were torn apart at her death.

01:03:11.499 --> 01:03:15.130
She even used to refer to her fan-base as
her friend-base.

01:03:15.130 --> 01:03:17.690
I came to think that I would have been friends
with her too.

01:03:17.690 --> 01:03:21.140
I hadn't heard about Christina until after
her untimely death,

01:03:21.140 --> 01:03:25.220
but in looking at some of her other content,
I started to see what the big deal was.

01:03:25.220 --> 01:03:28.069
She was a beautiful girl with a beautiful
voice.

01:03:28.069 --> 01:03:30.109
She was a self-proclaimed Legend of Zelda
nerd

01:03:30.109 --> 01:03:32.380
and she even had a Death Note tattoo.

01:03:32.380 --> 01:03:34.980
I imagine we would have gotten along very
well

01:03:34.980 --> 01:03:36.150
had we known each other.

01:03:36.150 --> 01:03:38.630
Naturally, I did quite a bit of digging.

01:03:38.630 --> 01:03:40.480
Watching videos and reading comments.

01:03:40.480 --> 01:03:45.579
There was a lot of pain carried on that page,
but in a way her channel was a lot like a

01:03:45.579 --> 01:03:46.579
ghost town.

01:03:46.579 --> 01:03:49.539
Sure, there are still occasional posts from
her manager,

01:03:49.539 --> 01:03:53.210
including a memorial video and some prerecorded
music videos,

01:03:53.210 --> 01:03:55.910
but for the most part, it was a ghost channel.

01:03:55.910 --> 01:03:59.779
In many ways it served as a memorial,
with people leaving their condolences on her

01:03:59.779 --> 01:04:01.309
discussion page.

01:04:01.309 --> 01:04:04.470
Most of the comments were fangirls talking
about how much they miss her

01:04:04.470 --> 01:04:07.430
with the occasional "why couldn't it have
been Keemstar?"

01:04:07.430 --> 01:04:08.430
comment.

01:04:08.430 --> 01:04:10.440
But by far, the most interesting thing to
me is

01:04:10.440 --> 01:04:13.799
looking at those videos uploaded right before
her death.

01:04:13.799 --> 01:04:18.039
some of her final recorded moments on camera,
and seeing people's reactions now that she's

01:04:18.039 --> 01:04:19.039
gone.

01:04:19.039 --> 01:04:20.770
I don't really know what it is.

01:04:20.770 --> 01:04:26.150
I feel bad for her and her fans, but
These videos just captivate my attention.

01:04:26.150 --> 01:04:30.549
This led me to start looking at some of the
tribute videos that have been made in her

01:04:30.549 --> 01:04:32.920
honor,
and it's here that I stumbled upon a playlist

01:04:32.920 --> 01:04:35.190
called "Christina Grimmie Unlisted".

01:04:35.190 --> 01:04:38.829
So, I guess that Christina got her start by
doing mostly covers

01:04:38.829 --> 01:04:41.660
and some of them have since been struck down
because of copyright

01:04:41.660 --> 01:04:44.109
while others were switched to private or unlisted.

01:04:44.109 --> 01:04:48.299
In fact, most of the videos on this playlist
couldn't be watched because

01:04:48.299 --> 01:04:49.450
they were changed to private.

01:04:49.450 --> 01:04:51.650
But the rest of them were just unlisted.

01:04:51.650 --> 01:04:55.390
But what caught my attention was one unlisted
video titled "FINAL GOODBYE."

01:04:55.390 --> 01:04:59.690
With a thumbnail of Christina waving at the
camera.

01:04:59.690 --> 01:05:05.200
The video was about 5 minutes long as I recall
and of course, I clicked on it to see what

01:05:05.200 --> 01:05:07.640
exactly this final goodbye video was.

01:05:07.640 --> 01:05:12.249
Less than one second into the video, I was
shocked with what I saw.

01:05:12.249 --> 01:05:16.569
It was a video of Christina in her room, only...

01:05:16.569 --> 01:05:22.009
her face was covered in what looked like blood
and she was crying her eyes out as she talked.

01:05:22.009 --> 01:05:24.640
It looked like she had been sobbing for hours.

01:05:24.640 --> 01:05:28.670
She was holding the camera and recording herself
and it was basically just shaking all over

01:05:28.670 --> 01:05:29.670
the place.

01:05:29.670 --> 01:05:33.640
My first thought was that this was some kind
of Halloween or April fools prank that she

01:05:33.640 --> 01:05:36.029
had done
but I looked at the date of the video

01:05:36.029 --> 01:05:40.289
and it said it was uploaded today,
which was obviously impossible.

01:05:40.289 --> 01:05:41.970
I was in complete shock.

01:05:41.970 --> 01:05:46.390
It had only a couple hundred views and started
with her barely able to get any words out

01:05:46.390 --> 01:05:47.619
through all the crying.

01:05:47.619 --> 01:05:52.289
I can't remember all of her exact words
but she started talking in typical vlog format

01:05:52.289 --> 01:05:55.099
save for the fact that she was sobbing through
all of it.

01:05:55.099 --> 01:05:56.099
"Hey guys."

01:05:56.099 --> 01:05:57.099
"It's Christina."

01:05:57.099 --> 01:06:01.430
"I... just wanted to say thank you for
all the love and support that you've given

01:06:01.430 --> 01:06:02.430
me."

01:06:02.430 --> 01:06:03.430
"Over the last several months."

01:06:03.430 --> 01:06:04.430
"And...

01:06:04.430 --> 01:06:13.420
I'm sorry that I had to leave you like this."

01:06:13.420 --> 01:06:15.400
She was coughing and choking on her own words
as she spoke.

01:06:15.400 --> 01:06:16.400
"I want you all to be strong."

01:06:16.400 --> 01:06:17.400
"I wish I could stay here with every last
one of you."

01:06:17.400 --> 01:06:19.039
"Thank you guys so much for being there and
supporting me along the way."

01:06:19.039 --> 01:06:20.950
"You guys were literally the biggest part
of me."

01:06:20.950 --> 01:06:24.349
"It was an incredible journey, and I'm so
sorry that it had to end this way."

01:06:24.349 --> 01:06:31.089
"I loved going on tour so much because I got
to see all of your smiling faces."

01:06:31.089 --> 01:06:32.880
"And no one can take that away from me."

01:06:32.880 --> 01:06:33.880
"No matter what."

01:06:33.880 --> 01:06:49.970
"I just wish that I had gotten one final chance
to say goodbye."

01:06:49.970 --> 01:06:53.470
I guess I wasn't alone,
because when I scrolled down to the comments

01:06:53.470 --> 01:06:55.049
they were pouring in.

01:06:55.049 --> 01:06:58.359
Some of them were as shocked as I was
wondering how this was even possible

01:06:58.359 --> 01:07:00.769
and trying to analyze the situation.

01:07:00.769 --> 01:07:04.900
Others were just overwhelmingly thankful for
her coming back to give them closure.

01:07:04.900 --> 01:07:07.960
It seemed like all of the comments that I
saw were positive ones.

01:07:07.960 --> 01:07:12.019
I guess because you'd have to be a fan of
hers to be seeking out the video.

01:07:12.019 --> 01:07:15.359
Before I got to the end of the video,
it stopped playing on its own and I got the

01:07:15.359 --> 01:07:18.089
familiar
"an unknown error has occurred" message.

01:07:18.089 --> 01:07:22.039
I tried refreshing the page, but it told me
that the user had removed the video.

01:07:22.039 --> 01:07:24.930
I frantically went to her channel to see if
it could be found, but

01:07:24.930 --> 01:07:25.930
it was nowhere.

01:07:25.930 --> 01:07:28.900
I searched YouTube to see if anyone has reuploaded
it, but

01:07:28.900 --> 01:07:29.980
it couldn't be found.

01:07:29.980 --> 01:07:33.619
I even tried to find that "Christina Grimmie
Unlisted" playlist,

01:07:33.619 --> 01:07:35.670
but it seemed like that was gone too.

01:07:35.670 --> 01:07:37.849
I was trying to process what had just happened.

01:07:37.849 --> 01:07:40.539
Had I dozed off and imagined that?

01:07:40.539 --> 01:07:42.390
I certainly didn't think so.

01:07:42.390 --> 01:07:43.480
Everything seemed so real.

01:07:43.480 --> 01:07:47.720
It was so vivid that I still can't get her
face in that video out of my head.

01:07:47.720 --> 01:07:50.380
I was starting to think I had imagined it
somehow,

01:07:50.380 --> 01:07:53.920
until I went to her channel and looked at
the discussion comments.

01:07:53.920 --> 01:07:56.140
Several comments had just come in, saying
things like,

01:07:56.140 --> 01:07:57.140
"Thank you.

01:07:57.140 --> 01:07:59.529
Thank you for everything."

01:07:59.529 --> 01:08:01.049
Now...

01:08:01.049 --> 01:08:02.569
I'm...

01:08:02.569 --> 01:08:06.440
I'm not really sure...

01:08:06.440 --> 01:08:08.529
Number 11 - Wakeup Syndrome

01:08:08.529 --> 01:08:16.319
Do you ever wake up in a hotel, or at a friend's
house, and for those first few seconds of

01:08:16.319 --> 01:08:20.150
consciousness, not know exactly where you
are?

01:08:20.150 --> 01:08:25.040
Like it takes a few moments for you to realize
you aren't in your own bed; that you've gone

01:08:25.040 --> 01:08:29.480
on vacation, or that you've passed out in
a buddy's guest room?

01:08:29.480 --> 01:08:32.859
This always used to happen to me when I would
go away to summer camp as a kid.

01:08:32.859 --> 01:08:35.390
It would happen during the first week or so.

01:08:35.390 --> 01:08:40.010
I would wake up, thinking I was in my own
bed… at least until I opened my eyes and

01:08:40.010 --> 01:08:45.930
came to the realization that I was in a cabin,
miles away from home.

01:08:45.930 --> 01:08:49.540
That same thing would always happen to me
during those first couple days home from camp.

01:08:49.540 --> 01:08:54.390
I would pop out of bed ready to go for a hike
or a kayak, only to discover that my mind

01:08:54.390 --> 01:08:56.930
had been playing tricks on me again.

01:08:56.930 --> 01:09:01.540
I don’t know if there is a proper term for
this phenomenon, but I’m sure that anyone

01:09:01.540 --> 01:09:03.663
who has traveled before probably knows what
I’m talking about.

01:09:03.663 --> 01:09:09.340
When I first started university, I used to
get that feeling all of the time.

01:09:09.340 --> 01:09:13.100
I'd imagine I was back at home in high school.

01:09:13.100 --> 01:09:18.510
Back then, if I slept in too late, Mom would
send my sister Tara in to wake me up.

01:09:18.510 --> 01:09:21.810
Tara was always the early riser between the
two of us.

01:09:21.810 --> 01:09:26.400
On weekends, you could count on her being
up before 9:00 every day.

01:09:26.400 --> 01:09:31.190
I was always more of a night owl and preferred
to stay up late watching movies, then sleep

01:09:31.190 --> 01:09:33.230
in to around noon or something.

01:09:33.230 --> 01:09:39.330
But during the school week, as you can imagine,
no such snoozing was allowed, and Tara would

01:09:39.330 --> 01:09:41.020
be sent in to wake me up.

01:09:41.020 --> 01:09:42.340
Tara: “Naaattthhhaaannn!

01:09:42.340 --> 01:09:44.310
Nathan, wake up!

01:09:44.310 --> 01:09:47.590
You're gonna miss the bus!

01:09:47.590 --> 01:09:50.230
Come on you sleepyhead!”

01:09:50.230 --> 01:09:54.170
Sometimes she would even bring our dog, Myuu,
in to help her out.

01:09:54.170 --> 01:09:56.720
Tara: "Go get him Myuu!"

01:09:56.720 --> 01:10:01.300
At 15-20 pounds, Myuu was hardly a force to
be taken seriously.

01:10:01.300 --> 01:10:07.070
But what made him such an effective alarm
clock was his constant burning desire for

01:10:07.070 --> 01:10:08.070
attention.

01:10:08.070 --> 01:10:13.190
He would jump all the way up on my bed, run
on top of my weary body and lick my face until

01:10:13.190 --> 01:10:16.940
finally, I mustered up the stamina to wake
up and go get ready for school.

01:10:16.940 --> 01:10:17.940
Tara: "That a boy Myuu!

01:10:17.940 --> 01:10:18.940
Good job buddy".

01:10:18.940 --> 01:10:19.940
When I moved away to attend school, I quickly
learned I’d have to set my own alarm clocks

01:10:19.940 --> 01:10:20.940
if I wanted to make it to class on time.

01:10:20.940 --> 01:10:24.680
The human mind really is an amazing thing,
for better or for worse.

01:10:24.680 --> 01:10:30.150
Every week or so during my first term, I would
wake up in my dorm thinking I was still back

01:10:30.150 --> 01:10:31.830
home in my old bed again.

01:10:31.830 --> 01:10:36.820
I would even hear Tara's words echo in my
head before I could peel my eyes open.

01:10:36.820 --> 01:10:37.820
Tara: "Naaattthhhann!

01:10:37.820 --> 01:10:39.080
Wake up dude.

01:10:39.080 --> 01:10:42.240
The bus is going to be here!"

01:10:42.240 --> 01:10:44.830
Eventually, it stopped happening.

01:10:44.830 --> 01:10:47.640
At least for the most part.

01:10:47.640 --> 01:10:51.020
I guess my mind just grew accustomed to the
fact that I’d be staying in the dorms from

01:10:51.020 --> 01:10:52.350
now on.

01:10:52.350 --> 01:10:56.280
But every now and then, it still happens.

01:10:56.280 --> 01:11:03.230
I’m a sophomore now and last week, I’d
visited home for Spring Break.

01:11:03.230 --> 01:11:07.331
I got back to school late last night and immediately
hit the sack before meeting up with any of

01:11:07.331 --> 01:11:08.450
my friends.

01:11:08.450 --> 01:11:14.260
Sure enough, this morning, I awoke with that
same old feeling.

01:11:14.260 --> 01:11:19.830
As I slowly started to wake up, my eyes remained
closed as I tried to doze back off to sleep.

01:11:19.830 --> 01:11:22.790
In my mind, I was home.

01:11:22.790 --> 01:11:28.680
I even heard my sister’s words echoing through
my head, just like old times.

01:11:28.680 --> 01:11:30.390
Tara: "Naaattthhhann!

01:11:30.390 --> 01:11:32.100
Wake up!

01:11:32.100 --> 01:11:35.900
Do you want to make us late?"

01:11:35.900 --> 01:11:41.770
I groaned, and rolled over, trying to ignore
the world around me for just a little while

01:11:41.770 --> 01:11:42.770
longer.

01:11:42.770 --> 01:11:48.870
But as I started to come to, I soon realized
it was all in my head, and I was back at university

01:11:48.870 --> 01:11:53.390
again, Tara was not here and I could sleep
in to my heart’s content.

01:11:53.390 --> 01:11:56.570
But then it happened.

01:11:56.570 --> 01:12:00.010
Once I realized where I was, I started to
fall back to sleep.

01:12:00.010 --> 01:12:04.540
And for a short while, I was relaxed.

01:12:04.540 --> 01:12:15.030
THAT'S WHEN I FELT MYUU LICK MY FACE.

01:12:15.030 --> 01:12:16.660
Number Twelve.

01:12:16.660 --> 01:12:19.870
Island Adventure.

01:12:19.870 --> 01:12:24.660
A woman at the airport had asked me if I was
looking forward to my vacation.

01:12:24.660 --> 01:12:28.620
To simply say yes would have been an understatement.

01:12:28.620 --> 01:12:34.470
I had to work overtime for 5 months in order
to afford to get here.

01:12:34.470 --> 01:12:40.490
Then I had to find time off from work, and
get off at the same time as my boyfriend.

01:12:40.490 --> 01:12:46.450
We had to research: the perfect resort on
the perfect island with the perfect weather.

01:12:46.450 --> 01:12:49.390
But we made it.

01:12:49.390 --> 01:12:55.290
Nothing else was between me, the warm tropical
sunshine, a cold refreshing margarita and

01:12:55.290 --> 01:13:01.350
the relaxing sound of waves crashing on the
sand in front me and carelessly rolling back

01:13:01.350 --> 01:13:03.080
into the sea.

01:13:03.080 --> 01:13:09.190
As I dug my toes into the soft sand and laid
back on my beach chair, I thought about all

01:13:09.190 --> 01:13:13.890
possibilities that awaited us here at the
Grand Maritime Beach Resort.

01:13:13.890 --> 01:13:16.850
Kayaking through the ocean breeze.

01:13:16.850 --> 01:13:20.480
Living the high life at the offshore casino.

01:13:20.480 --> 01:13:23.510
Backpacking the expansive rainforest by moonlight.

01:13:23.510 --> 01:13:28.210
Or regenerating my body at the luxury poolside
spa.

01:13:28.210 --> 01:13:34.140
Maybe I'd even try SCUBA diving, though I
wasn’t sure I liked the idea of breathing

01:13:34.140 --> 01:13:35.950
through a tube.

01:13:35.950 --> 01:13:41.560
I think before any of that though, I'd just
kick back on the beach and enjoy some sunlight.

01:13:41.560 --> 01:13:48.530
We'd had a long trip and it felt good to just
drop our bags, slip into a bikini and take

01:13:48.530 --> 01:13:50.620
in the saltwater aroma.

01:13:50.620 --> 01:13:54.830
*Yawn* I... could feel myself starting to
fade....

01:13:54.830 --> 01:13:58.640
*Yawn* off too…

01:13:58.640 --> 01:13:59.910
"Lucy.

01:13:59.910 --> 01:14:01.400
Lucy, you OK?"

01:14:01.400 --> 01:14:03.350
My boyfriend's touch snapped me out of a daze
after being awoken by that boat horn.

01:14:03.350 --> 01:14:05.420
"Uhh yeah, I just fell asleep.

01:14:05.420 --> 01:14:06.420
What time is it?"

01:14:06.420 --> 01:14:07.420
"About 2.

01:14:07.420 --> 01:14:08.870
You were tired.

01:14:08.870 --> 01:14:10.390
You look dead."

01:14:10.390 --> 01:14:11.390
"Thanks..."

01:14:11.390 --> 01:14:12.390
"I was just going up to the bar.

01:14:12.390 --> 01:14:13.520
Do you want anything to drink?"

01:14:13.520 --> 01:14:17.180
"You could grab me a Piña Colada I guess."

01:14:17.180 --> 01:14:18.180
"OK."

01:14:18.180 --> 01:14:21.140
He kissed me and headed off to the bar.

01:14:21.140 --> 01:14:27.110
Before I could doze off again a strange little
man came walking down the beach with a clipboard.

01:14:27.110 --> 01:14:31.380
He looked like one of the locals, a bit of
an oddball one at that.

01:14:31.380 --> 01:14:35.850
He went from chair to chair, making his way
up to where I was.

01:14:35.850 --> 01:14:40.960
When he arrived, he asked if I was interested
in going on an 'island adventure'.

01:14:40.960 --> 01:14:45.820
He explained that it would include backpacking
in the rainforest, ziplining, roasting food

01:14:45.820 --> 01:14:50.770
by a campfire and bathing in a private waterfall
grotto.

01:14:50.770 --> 01:14:56.670
The clipboard included photos of what looked
like an absolutely amazing time to me, so

01:14:56.670 --> 01:15:02.200
I told him it looked perfect and I wanted
to sign my boyfriend and I up for it.

01:15:02.200 --> 01:15:07.700
He told me to follow him down the beach to
the activity shack so I could make a reservation.

01:15:07.700 --> 01:15:11.570
I dipped my feet in the water as we strolled
the length of the shore, but the man kept

01:15:11.570 --> 01:15:13.120
rushing me along.

01:15:13.120 --> 01:15:17.380
I didn't think much of it at the time, just
assuming he was impatient.

01:15:17.380 --> 01:15:22.190
That should have been my first of many red
flags.

01:15:22.190 --> 01:15:25.150
Next we walked off the property of the resort.

01:15:25.150 --> 01:15:28.480
I asked if the expedition was included in
the resort package.

01:15:28.480 --> 01:15:33.750
He told me it was, and I had no reason to
believe otherwise.

01:15:33.750 --> 01:15:36.320
We finally get down to the little hut.

01:15:36.320 --> 01:15:41.690
All I remember was it being completely empty
and not really looking like an activity shack

01:15:41.690 --> 01:15:43.380
at all.

01:15:43.380 --> 01:15:48.540
The guy quickly apologized and told me that
the activity director must have already headed

01:15:48.540 --> 01:15:51.960
up to the site to begin preparing for the
excursion.

01:15:51.960 --> 01:15:56.370
I was starting to get pretty annoyed at this
point and told him I better walk back and

01:15:56.370 --> 01:16:01.620
let my boyfriend know, but he assured me that
the site was just across the street and it

01:16:01.620 --> 01:16:04.370
would only be a couple more minutes.

01:16:04.370 --> 01:16:08.490
I was reluctant but didn't want to be rude,
since he insisted.

01:16:08.490 --> 01:16:14.390
Besides, it would be good for me to get to
scope out where we would be exploring.

01:16:14.390 --> 01:16:16.370
So we made our way inland.

01:16:16.370 --> 01:16:19.110
I had to run across the street barefoot.

01:16:19.110 --> 01:16:20.750
No crosswalk.

01:16:20.750 --> 01:16:26.260
This led us directly into the rainforest and
when we got there, I started to get a bad

01:16:26.260 --> 01:16:27.260
feeling.

01:16:27.260 --> 01:16:32.810
There was no set path we were following, we
was just leading me deeper into the forest.

01:16:32.810 --> 01:16:38.520
The other thing that set me off at this point
was the complete lack of other tourists.

01:16:38.520 --> 01:16:44.100
I thought for sure we'd see other couples
signing up as well, but... scratch that, it

01:16:44.100 --> 01:16:49.270
wasn't just a lack of other tourists, it was
a lack of of people.

01:16:49.270 --> 01:16:52.140
There was nobody out here.

01:16:52.140 --> 01:16:56.660
Just me and this guy who randomly approached
me on the beach.

01:16:56.660 --> 01:17:00.850
I had no real idea that he actually worked
for the resort.

01:17:00.850 --> 01:17:06.391
He was kind of scraggy and unkempt, certainly
not up to the standards of grooming we had

01:17:06.391 --> 01:17:08.100
seen at the front desk.

01:17:08.100 --> 01:17:13.940
But he did look to be an island local, like
most of the employees we had seen at the resort.

01:17:13.940 --> 01:17:18.440
And it's not like the island adventure expedition
wasn't advertised in the brochures.

01:17:18.440 --> 01:17:23.940
But something deep inside me said that this
wasn't the real thing.

01:17:23.940 --> 01:17:25.750
I got more and more nervous.

01:17:25.750 --> 01:17:30.580
I was honestly thinking about turning and
running, but the only thing that stopped me

01:17:30.580 --> 01:17:36.060
from doing it was how embarrassing it would
be if this was legit, because there was still

01:17:36.060 --> 01:17:37.880
some doubt in my mind.

01:17:37.880 --> 01:17:44.620
Besides, it's not like I'd make it very far
with no shoes and no idea where I was going.

01:17:44.620 --> 01:17:50.040
I debated doing it anyway in my head when
something emerged in the distance.

01:17:50.040 --> 01:17:54.740
Another man was standing out there, veiled
by a layer of fog and facing slightly away

01:17:54.740 --> 01:17:56.810
from us.

01:17:56.810 --> 01:18:01.720
Relief washed over me when the guy I was with
called out to him in another language and

01:18:01.720 --> 01:18:04.080
the guy came up to us.

01:18:04.080 --> 01:18:08.510
Realistically, it was just a couple minutes,
just as he had told me back at the activity

01:18:08.510 --> 01:18:10.000
shack.

01:18:10.000 --> 01:18:14.120
Before I could feel silly for doubting him,
the two men went back and forth in their native

01:18:14.120 --> 01:18:15.240
tongue.

01:18:15.240 --> 01:18:20.630
I don't know what they were saying obviously,
but I just know they were talking very quickly.

01:18:20.630 --> 01:18:28.180
But, what was weird was this new guy was staring
at me, not making eye contact with the other

01:18:28.180 --> 01:18:29.180
man.

01:18:29.180 --> 01:18:35.640
Actually, he wasn't just staring at me, he
was eyeing my body... up and down.

01:18:35.640 --> 01:18:41.190
I felt exposed and uncomfortable, but let's
face it, it wasn't the first time a guy couldn't

01:18:41.190 --> 01:18:43.040
keep his eyes off.

01:18:43.040 --> 01:18:47.500
It's just that usually they try a little bit
to hide it.

01:18:47.500 --> 01:18:50.950
He continued to fire off questions I couldn't
understand.

01:18:50.950 --> 01:18:54.170
I looked up at the rainforest we'd be exploring.

01:18:54.170 --> 01:18:56.670
It wasn't exactly as I’d pictured it.

01:18:56.670 --> 01:18:58.510
How far was the zipline?

01:18:58.510 --> 01:19:00.200
Where was the waterfall?

01:19:00.200 --> 01:19:04.950
That's when... both of them went quiet.

01:19:04.950 --> 01:19:07.510
I looked back down at them.

01:19:07.510 --> 01:19:09.980
Both of them were staring at me.

01:19:09.980 --> 01:19:16.010
I smiled sheepishly, then the two men simultaneously
grabbed me!

01:19:16.010 --> 01:19:22.060
I tried to scream, but one of their hands
reached over muffled my mouth as both of them

01:19:22.060 --> 01:19:24.440
dragged me down to the ground!

01:19:24.440 --> 01:19:30.470
I was completely helpless to resist with the
full weight of two bodies crushing me.

01:19:30.470 --> 01:19:37.600
A hand pinched my nose and closed my nostrils;
tears began to flow but I couldn’t breathe!

01:19:37.600 --> 01:19:40.220
I was completely powerless.

01:19:40.220 --> 01:19:42.540
There was nothing I could do.

01:19:42.540 --> 01:19:47.270
The black started to envelop me from the corners
of my vision.

01:19:47.270 --> 01:19:53.660
Just before I blacked out, I saw something
in a blur through my tears, deep in the distance.

01:19:53.660 --> 01:19:57.500
There was a third person way back in the trees.

01:19:57.500 --> 01:20:04.660
It was the last thing I saw before the black
crashed in and I was out.

01:20:04.660 --> 01:20:08.120
For the second time that day, I awoke in a
haze.

01:20:08.120 --> 01:20:10.140
I thought I never would.

01:20:10.140 --> 01:20:12.850
But I was alive.

01:20:12.850 --> 01:20:13.880
It was getting dark out.

01:20:13.880 --> 01:20:16.540
But we were still in the forest.

01:20:16.540 --> 01:20:18.670
A different part of the forest.

01:20:18.670 --> 01:20:21.090
I didn’t know how deep in we were.

01:20:21.090 --> 01:20:23.270
I actually couldn’t make out much.

01:20:23.270 --> 01:20:25.310
My vision was a blur.

01:20:25.310 --> 01:20:28.040
It was like looking through beer goggles.

01:20:28.040 --> 01:20:33.200
My right arm felt dead, almost impossible
to lift, but with some effort I could move

01:20:33.200 --> 01:20:38.050
it around and shoo off some of the hundreds
of bugs flying right over my body.

01:20:38.050 --> 01:20:42.300
It didn’t do much good, they were everywhere.

01:20:42.300 --> 01:20:45.670
The two men were sitting by a campfire talking.

01:20:45.670 --> 01:20:48.230
Clearly they hadn’t noticed me wake up.

01:20:48.230 --> 01:20:51.340
From what I could tell, they were about 10
meters away.

01:20:51.340 --> 01:20:54.080
There was also a Jeep parked nearby now too.

01:20:54.080 --> 01:20:57.700
I felt as if I was hungover and drunk at the
same time.

01:20:57.700 --> 01:21:03.160
But this was my only chance to try to escape
and I knew it.

01:21:03.160 --> 01:21:05.620
There were just a few problems.

01:21:05.620 --> 01:21:11.910
I had no idea where I was, how far we were
from the beach, or from any civilization for

01:21:11.910 --> 01:21:13.220
that matter.

01:21:13.220 --> 01:21:15.780
I was not in much condition to run.

01:21:15.780 --> 01:21:20.700
I still had no shoes, and my bikini was not
great for running in to begin with.

01:21:20.700 --> 01:21:23.480
Normally I might be more confident.

01:21:23.480 --> 01:21:29.210
I do jog for 45 minutes almost every day,
so I had pretty good endurance.

01:21:29.210 --> 01:21:33.020
I don’t know what these two men were capable
of though.

01:21:33.020 --> 01:21:37.210
And then there was that third guy I had seen
in the distance.

01:21:37.210 --> 01:21:38.460
Where was he?

01:21:38.460 --> 01:21:40.310
Was he one of them?

01:21:40.310 --> 01:21:43.270
Was he going to be patrolling the perimeter?

01:21:43.270 --> 01:21:48.090
Before I could think of a plan, I saw them
turn their back to me and go the car.

01:21:48.090 --> 01:21:50.530
This was my chance.

01:21:50.530 --> 01:21:52.120
I wobbled to feet.

01:21:52.120 --> 01:21:56.420
I didn’t break into a full sprint right
away, trying to strike a balance between speed

01:21:56.420 --> 01:21:58.320
and stealth.

01:21:58.320 --> 01:22:04.490
As I got further from the campfire, it got
very dark, even just a few meters ahead of

01:22:04.490 --> 01:22:07.550
me was starting to look pitch black.

01:22:07.550 --> 01:22:09.090
It wasn’t long before…

01:22:09.090 --> 01:22:11.500
I stepped on something hard and rough.

01:22:11.500 --> 01:22:15.380
It rolled me off my feet and I went crashing
to the ground.

01:22:15.380 --> 01:22:16.610
Shoot.

01:22:16.610 --> 01:22:20.960
I heard their yelling out in the distance
as they realized I was gone.

01:22:20.960 --> 01:22:25.150
I pulled myself to feet, feeling even woozier
than before.

01:22:25.150 --> 01:22:28.000
I heard the Jeep start somewhere in the background.

01:22:28.000 --> 01:22:34.000
The headlights flared up behind me so I scrambled
my way to the nearest bump in the terrain

01:22:34.000 --> 01:22:37.760
and ducked out behind it, doing my best not
to move a muscle.

01:22:37.760 --> 01:22:43.480
The area lit up as the vehicle turned around
and headed in my direction.

01:22:43.480 --> 01:22:48.810
It pretty much mowed over the low-lying vegetation
as it tore over the bumpy terrain and headed

01:22:48.810 --> 01:22:51.150
straight for me.

01:22:51.150 --> 01:22:54.730
They… they didn’t see me.

01:22:54.730 --> 01:22:58.360
The jeep passed and I was safe for a little
while longer.

01:22:58.360 --> 01:23:02.981
I figured I’d have to develop a strategy
so I could continue in one direction, as not

01:23:02.981 --> 01:23:05.740
to send myself in circles.

01:23:05.740 --> 01:23:09.620
I decided to go perpendicular to the way they
had just driven.

01:23:09.620 --> 01:23:15.060
That way if they try to comb the area it will
take them a long time to get to me.

01:23:15.060 --> 01:23:16.620
I got to me feet and set off.

01:23:16.620 --> 01:23:24.020
But then I heard something that stopped me
in my tracks.

01:23:24.020 --> 01:23:25.460
It wasn’t loud.

01:23:25.460 --> 01:23:29.300
I wasn’t even entirely sure I had heard
it all.

01:23:29.300 --> 01:23:32.380
Until I heard it again.

01:23:32.380 --> 01:23:34.080
There were footsteps.

01:23:34.080 --> 01:23:36.370
Probably a good 30 meters or so.

01:23:36.370 --> 01:23:40.830
My head was still spinning and I couldn’t
exactly tell which direction they were coming

01:23:40.830 --> 01:23:42.110
from.

01:23:42.110 --> 01:23:45.000
Once again I had to reassess my situation.

01:23:45.000 --> 01:23:46.510
I looked around.

01:23:46.510 --> 01:23:51.360
Absolutely no light, other than the faint
moon’s glow.

01:23:51.360 --> 01:23:54.480
I couldn’t make out where the footsteps
were coming from.

01:23:54.480 --> 01:23:56.850
Or who they were coming from.

01:23:56.850 --> 01:24:00.230
What if only one of them had gotten in the
car?

01:24:00.230 --> 01:24:04.400
Or could this be that third person I had seen
in the distance?

01:24:04.400 --> 01:24:06.940
It could be a random person for all I knew.

01:24:06.940 --> 01:24:09.920
It might be worth calling out for help.

01:24:09.920 --> 01:24:12.980
But if it was one of them…

01:24:12.980 --> 01:24:15.080
I didn’t have time to sit and think about
it.

01:24:15.080 --> 01:24:17.370
The footsteps were getting louder.

01:24:17.370 --> 01:24:20.000
I decided to try and quietly move away.

01:24:20.000 --> 01:24:22.960
It was getting harder to get around though.

01:24:22.960 --> 01:24:27.620
Not only was it dark but my vision was swirling
more and more.

01:24:27.620 --> 01:24:32.540
It seemed like the more ground I covered,
the louder the other footsteps got.

01:24:32.540 --> 01:24:37.950
The anxiety, the swirling headache, the sick
feeling I had…

01:24:37.950 --> 01:24:40.390
all of it was getting to me.

01:24:40.390 --> 01:24:43.180
Before I knew what had happened, I collapsed.

01:24:43.180 --> 01:24:47.080
I laid on the ground breathing heavily.

01:24:47.080 --> 01:24:51.580
The last thing I saw this time was a pair
of boots on the ground in front of me.

01:24:51.580 --> 01:24:55.510
They walked up and stopped just before my
face.

01:24:55.510 --> 01:24:57.950
I couldn’t go on.

01:24:57.950 --> 01:25:03.660
I felt myself start to fade once again…

01:25:03.660 --> 01:25:05.810
Number Thirteen.

01:25:05.810 --> 01:25:07.200
International Waters.

01:25:07.200 --> 01:25:10.320
“Molly, come on!

01:25:10.320 --> 01:25:12.400
They’re leaving!”

01:25:12.400 --> 01:25:15.640
I called back to my wife as she waddled down
the dock in her high heels.

01:25:15.640 --> 01:25:17.520
*sigh* What’s the point?

01:25:17.520 --> 01:25:19.480
I thought to myself.

01:25:19.480 --> 01:25:21.180
We were going to miss it.

01:25:21.180 --> 01:25:23.520
It was already three minutes past two.

01:25:23.520 --> 01:25:25.830
The boat should have left by now.

01:25:25.830 --> 01:25:30.730
Sure enough, just as we reached the end of
the dock, the ship pulled away and headed

01:25:30.730 --> 01:25:31.730
out to sea.

01:25:31.730 --> 01:25:34.960
If only she hadn’t taken so long to get
ready…

01:25:34.960 --> 01:25:35.960
“Oh, no!!

01:25:35.960 --> 01:25:36.960
Shoot!

01:25:36.960 --> 01:25:37.960
I’m sorry Tom.

01:25:37.960 --> 01:25:39.820
Agh, we just missed it too!”

01:25:39.820 --> 01:25:40.820
“Come on.

01:25:40.820 --> 01:25:45.240
At least we can still enjoy the poolside bar
for a few more hours while the sun’s still

01:25:45.240 --> 01:25:46.240
up.”

01:25:46.240 --> 01:25:47.450
I turned back towards the mainland.

01:25:47.450 --> 01:25:49.890
Then I heard a voice behind me.

01:25:49.890 --> 01:25:54.440
It came from one of the island locals who
was sitting at the end of the pier.

01:25:54.440 --> 01:25:58.110
Apparently there was going to be be a smaller
shuttle boat that would take people out to

01:25:58.110 --> 01:26:00.580
the casino boat in about an hour.

01:26:00.580 --> 01:26:01.580
Perfect for us.

01:26:01.580 --> 01:26:05.060
I made sure next time we were waiting out
there 15 minutes early.

01:26:05.060 --> 01:26:10.480
Right at 3:00PM, the same guy from the dock
earlier pulled up in a tiny speedboat.

01:26:10.480 --> 01:26:14.910
He helped us aboard, then, once we were seated,
he fired up the engine.

01:26:14.910 --> 01:26:19.870
I asked him if we were going to wait for any
other guests, but he told us we were the only

01:26:19.870 --> 01:26:23.120
ones, so just like that, we took off.

01:26:23.120 --> 01:26:27.060
The sea breeze whipped through our hair as
the island behind us got smaller and smaller

01:26:27.060 --> 01:26:28.540
in the distance.

01:26:28.540 --> 01:26:32.870
Molly grabbed onto me for safety as we looked
on at the sparkling horizon.

01:26:32.870 --> 01:26:39.030
Eventually, a speck appeared on that horizon,
and not long after, that speck became a boat;

01:26:39.030 --> 01:26:42.590
the boat upon which we would be spending the
rest of our evening.

01:26:42.590 --> 01:26:44.730
When we walked in, the place was popping.

01:26:44.730 --> 01:26:48.760
Blackjack tables, poker, craps, roulette,
slot machines, a disco ball bumping to beat

01:26:48.760 --> 01:26:52.750
of the bass and bottle girls for every table,
couch and lounge chair.

01:26:52.750 --> 01:26:55.600
It looked like there was more in the rooms
beyond as well.

01:26:55.600 --> 01:26:59.860
We spent probably the first four hours or
so in this initial room.

01:26:59.860 --> 01:27:04.021
I wasn’t really keeping track of time, but
that was more of an estimate based of the

01:27:04.021 --> 01:27:06.340
amount of drinks my wife and I downed.

01:27:06.340 --> 01:27:10.630
We jumped around from game to game, spending
some of the time together and some apart.

01:27:10.630 --> 01:27:15.220
I wanted to give one more spin at the roulette
table, and I wasn’t sure where exactly my

01:27:15.220 --> 01:27:16.270
wife had run off to.

01:27:16.270 --> 01:27:20.800
I was getting kind of low on chips and wondered
if she was doing any better.

01:27:20.800 --> 01:27:25.590
I noticed the guy next to me had a huge stack
of chips, the most I had seen anyone with

01:27:25.590 --> 01:27:26.970
the entire night.

01:27:26.970 --> 01:27:32.980
I inquired about where he had all the good
luck and he told me he made almost all of

01:27:32.980 --> 01:27:34.720
his earnings in... “the private rooms.”

01:27:34.720 --> 01:27:39.180
He went on to explain that the casino operates
off shore because what goes on in the private

01:27:39.180 --> 01:27:40.980
rooms is very illegal.

01:27:40.980 --> 01:27:42.760
But not in international waters.

01:27:42.760 --> 01:27:44.320
I asked if he had any tips.

01:27:44.320 --> 01:27:49.090
He told me to stay calm, be logical and don’t
do anything rash.

01:27:49.090 --> 01:27:53.780
He said you can make a lot of money there,
but you have to know when to sit back and

01:27:53.780 --> 01:27:58.171
observe and when it’s a good time to punch
it and buy in high.

01:27:58.171 --> 01:28:02.750
And the last thing he told me was that this
room was not for the light hearted, or the

01:28:02.750 --> 01:28:04.030
morally righteous.

01:28:04.030 --> 01:28:06.380
I went to go find Molly.

01:28:06.380 --> 01:28:10.760
The first area beyond the curtained door was
just a little waiting area with a bouncer.

01:28:10.760 --> 01:28:15.160
He asked us if we wanted to play in a private
room and made sure we knew that we’d have

01:28:15.160 --> 01:28:19.990
to stay for the duration of the game, so if
we needed to use the restroom, to do it now.

01:28:19.990 --> 01:28:24.050
He reiterated what that one guy had told me
about this being a moral ground zero.

01:28:24.050 --> 01:28:25.560
Then we waited.

01:28:25.560 --> 01:28:30.520
I hadn’t noticed anyone come out of the
room, but after we’d waited about 20 minutes,

01:28:30.520 --> 01:28:35.280
the door opened and we found two chairs in
front of a bank teller window type of thing

01:28:35.280 --> 01:28:38.720
with a little slot, presumably to exchange
our chips.

01:28:38.720 --> 01:28:43.700
Beyond the window was a bigger room with several
vertical wall panels made up of grey metal

01:28:43.700 --> 01:28:44.800
sheets.

01:28:44.800 --> 01:28:49.330
There was a door in the corner of the room
and a large mirror on each wall.

01:28:49.330 --> 01:28:54.310
A bright, disc-shaped light on the ceiling
was the only means of illumination.

01:28:54.310 --> 01:28:56.430
Someone stepped into the room with us.

01:28:56.430 --> 01:28:58.930
It was one of their bottle girls.

01:28:58.930 --> 01:29:02.630
She poured each of us a glass and explained
that tonight’s game would come in three

01:29:02.630 --> 01:29:03.820
parts.

01:29:03.820 --> 01:29:09.750
Minimum bet would be 15 credits and we would
be required to place a bet for each game.

01:29:09.750 --> 01:29:14.930
The first game would require us to bet on
who could hang in the longest.

01:29:14.930 --> 01:29:18.650
Suddenly I felt kind of a nasty feeling as
I thought about all the warnings of moral

01:29:18.650 --> 01:29:19.790
values.

01:29:19.790 --> 01:29:23.810
When it was described to me I imagined something
along the lines of the board game Sorry!

01:29:23.810 --> 01:29:26.440
where you had to bump off the other players
to win.

01:29:26.440 --> 01:29:31.740
I hadn’t even anticipated the possibility
of a survival game… soooo you can imagine

01:29:31.740 --> 01:29:36.220
my relief when they wheeled five horizontal
bars into the room beyond our window.

01:29:36.220 --> 01:29:38.130
I guess my wife had gotten the same idea.

01:29:38.130 --> 01:29:43.630
“When they said ‘who can hang in the longest,’
what came to your mind?”

01:29:43.630 --> 01:29:44.630
“Uh… haha.

01:29:44.630 --> 01:29:47.980
I guess I thought we were sponsoring the Hunger
Games for a second there.”

01:29:47.980 --> 01:29:53.770
That’s when they marched five women, completely
naked, out onto the floor.

01:29:53.770 --> 01:29:59.720
My wife glared at me; I told her I honestly
had no idea, but she crossed her arms.

01:29:59.720 --> 01:30:02.420
Each of the women took their place under the
bars.

01:30:02.420 --> 01:30:07.380
My immediate thought when I saw them was that
they-- looked tired and disheveled, they certainly

01:30:07.380 --> 01:30:09.360
didn’t seem happy to be there.

01:30:09.360 --> 01:30:13.130
But given what I thought the circumstances
were a minute ago, it didn’t bother me as

01:30:13.130 --> 01:30:14.510
much as it should have.

01:30:14.510 --> 01:30:18.690
“So we just have to pick to which one can
hang on the bar the longest?

01:30:18.690 --> 01:30:19.710
Seems easy.

01:30:19.710 --> 01:30:22.060
The lightest one should have the advantage.

01:30:22.060 --> 01:30:23.060
Second from the right.”

01:30:23.060 --> 01:30:24.360
“Yeah but what about grip strength?”

01:30:24.360 --> 01:30:27.370
“How would we know what their grip strength
is like?”

01:30:27.370 --> 01:30:28.380
“I don’t know.

01:30:28.380 --> 01:30:29.710
Maybe the one on the left?

01:30:29.710 --> 01:30:31.300
Maybe the one next to her?”

01:30:31.300 --> 01:30:32.710
“This feels so wrong.

01:30:32.710 --> 01:30:35.500
It’s like we’re slave traders up here
or something.”

01:30:35.500 --> 01:30:40.360
I could tell that she was half joking, but
a small part of me did feel that it was wrong,

01:30:40.360 --> 01:30:43.950
sitting up here judging these exposed women
based on their bodies.

01:30:43.950 --> 01:30:47.190
Our drinks were refilled and we were given
a little card.

01:30:47.190 --> 01:30:52.310
Without going into too much detail, the card
contained odds and buy-in price for each candidate.

01:30:52.310 --> 01:30:56.450
Our skinny candidate had the best odds, but
that also meant she had the biggest buy-in

01:30:56.450 --> 01:30:57.660
price.

01:30:57.660 --> 01:31:01.180
So the system that they had here was kind
of the inverse of what you might expect from

01:31:01.180 --> 01:31:03.610
a horse track or something similar.

01:31:03.610 --> 01:31:06.490
We still decided to go for the small chick
anyways.

01:31:06.490 --> 01:31:10.590
I could feel the drinks starting to get to
me as I counted out the necessary amount of

01:31:10.590 --> 01:31:13.550
chips to put in the slot in order to bet on
her.

01:31:13.550 --> 01:31:18.480
Once the bets were in, one more of the casino
employees went down into the room and dumped

01:31:18.480 --> 01:31:21.270
a bucket of water on the floor.

01:31:21.270 --> 01:31:26.330
The water spread evenly throughout the room,
creating a shallow pool all the way around.

01:31:26.330 --> 01:31:28.050
“What is that for?”

01:31:28.050 --> 01:31:29.340
“I don’t know.

01:31:29.340 --> 01:31:32.400
Maybe it’s to make it obvious if someone
touches the ground?”

01:31:32.400 --> 01:31:36.730
To be honest, I really had no idea, but soon
I would find out.

01:31:36.730 --> 01:31:41.230
The competition began and all five ladies
jumped up onto the bar.

01:31:41.230 --> 01:31:45.000
One of them immediately lost their handle
came crashing down to the ground.

01:31:45.000 --> 01:31:47.850
Her scream was cut short by an electric buzz!

01:31:47.850 --> 01:31:50.360
She was flailing and freaking out on the ground.

01:31:50.360 --> 01:31:52.360
“Oh my God…”

01:31:52.360 --> 01:31:55.200
That’s when I realized the true intent of
the groundwater…

01:31:55.200 --> 01:31:58.100
It wasn’t to show who had touched the ground…

01:31:58.100 --> 01:31:59.700
I mean, maybe it was.

01:31:59.700 --> 01:32:03.350
But the main purpose was a motivation to stay
on the bar.

01:32:03.350 --> 01:32:07.040
There was some kind of an electric current
running through the water, probably not enough

01:32:07.040 --> 01:32:10.240
to kill, but definitely enough to pack a punch.

01:32:10.240 --> 01:32:14.000
The poor lady was screeching and desperately
trying to get back on the bar, but she just

01:32:14.000 --> 01:32:15.940
didn’t have what it takes it to hold on.

01:32:15.940 --> 01:32:21.940
She kept falling, and getting shocked, then
trying to pull back up and falling again.

01:32:21.940 --> 01:32:24.900
It was… hard to watch.

01:32:24.900 --> 01:32:29.280
After about 20 seconds, the girl next to her
went down, and it looked like the surge that

01:32:29.280 --> 01:32:31.250
went through her was even more violent.

01:32:31.250 --> 01:32:37.050
She however, was able to get back up on the
bar and wrap her legs around it in order to

01:32:37.050 --> 01:32:38.890
avoid further pain.

01:32:38.890 --> 01:32:42.020
The first woman just wasn’t able to pull
herself up though.

01:32:42.020 --> 01:32:45.520
Molly was having difficulty stomaching what
she was seeing.

01:32:45.520 --> 01:32:48.520
She grabbed my hand and gave me a helpless
look of concern.

01:32:48.520 --> 01:32:50.490
“Let’s get out of here.”

01:32:50.490 --> 01:32:52.990
We headed for the exit, but the door was locked.

01:32:52.990 --> 01:32:53.990
“Hey!

01:32:53.990 --> 01:32:54.990
We’re done!

01:32:54.990 --> 01:32:56.030
Let us out!”

01:32:56.030 --> 01:33:00.500
But we were reminded that we had to agreed
to stay for the entire game.

01:33:00.500 --> 01:33:04.920
And I realized that, not only would we have
to sit there, but we’d also have to place

01:33:04.920 --> 01:33:10.380
bets and continue to support the degrading,
inhumane experiences that were going on down

01:33:10.380 --> 01:33:11.380
there.

01:33:11.380 --> 01:33:13.400
What had I gotten us into?

01:33:13.400 --> 01:33:17.210
Another girl fell and got a short jolt of
electricity before hopping up and wrapping

01:33:17.210 --> 01:33:19.580
her legs around the bar for safety.

01:33:19.580 --> 01:33:24.960
It came down to two final girls, our girl
and the more muscular looking girl I had suggested

01:33:24.960 --> 01:33:25.960
earlier.

01:33:25.960 --> 01:33:29.410
Our girl started to lose her grip and shifted
around to regain her position.

01:33:29.410 --> 01:33:33.510
But a couple seconds later she was wobbling
again.

01:33:33.510 --> 01:33:37.540
She cried out and actually burst into tears
while still holding onto the bar.

01:33:37.540 --> 01:33:42.980
I guess she already knew she was going to
lose but continued to hold out as long as

01:33:42.980 --> 01:33:44.270
possible.

01:33:44.270 --> 01:33:49.720
Before long she slipped, and I could actually
hear her yell out, ‘NO!’ as she did so.

01:33:49.720 --> 01:33:54.780
Luckily, she only got a few seconds of voltage,
the currents seemed to turn off, and the last

01:33:54.780 --> 01:33:57.580
woman let herself down from the bar in safety.

01:33:57.580 --> 01:34:01.100
The whole thing was maybe only a minute and
half, but the first to have fallen was in

01:34:01.100 --> 01:34:02.710
pain for all of it.

01:34:02.710 --> 01:34:06.230
She was alive but she didn’t get up right
away.

01:34:06.230 --> 01:34:10.570
Her hair was literally standing up in all
directions and her skin was charred like something

01:34:10.570 --> 01:34:12.190
out of a cartoon.

01:34:12.190 --> 01:34:15.090
It was just disgusting to watch.

01:34:15.090 --> 01:34:18.920
Barbaric, but that’s probably not a strong
enough word to describe the pain she must

01:34:18.920 --> 01:34:20.220
have been in…

01:34:20.220 --> 01:34:24.790
Eventually the room was cleared and a water
vacuum was used to dry things up as the bars

01:34:24.790 --> 01:34:28.280
were taken out in preparation of the next
game.

01:34:28.280 --> 01:34:34.130
They ended up bringing out these big wide
yellow rulers, four feet in length and placing

01:34:34.130 --> 01:34:35.730
them against the wall.

01:34:35.730 --> 01:34:39.940
When they brought the women back out, they
had on nothing but these knee-high boots,

01:34:39.940 --> 01:34:45.070
which subsequently latched into the wall at
the knee and at the toe, so their shins were

01:34:45.070 --> 01:34:48.400
pretty much locked in, parallel to the wall.

01:34:48.400 --> 01:34:55.170
As our drinks were refilled, we were given
another card, simply labeled “flexibility”.

01:34:55.170 --> 01:34:59.510
Like before, it gave us odds and buy-in price
for each of the contestants.

01:34:59.510 --> 01:35:03.480
I noticed that some of the contestants were
the same, but some had been swapped out.

01:35:03.480 --> 01:35:06.670
The final two girls from the last game were
still there.

01:35:06.670 --> 01:35:09.010
We again contemplated not betting.

01:35:09.010 --> 01:35:12.990
We stalled for a few minutes, hoping they
would just start the game without our bet.

01:35:12.990 --> 01:35:17.340
The bottle girl came back in and old us there
had been a change and exchanged the card we

01:35:17.340 --> 01:35:18.670
had for another card.

01:35:18.670 --> 01:35:21.320
The only difference was they added one more
contestant.

01:35:21.320 --> 01:35:25.650
Again, we tried to wait it out without betting
and we were interrupted by a bouncer who burst

01:35:25.650 --> 01:35:29.140
into our room and told us to hurry up and
make a bet.

01:35:29.140 --> 01:35:34.190
We tried to explain that we were no longer
comfortable with it, but it didn’t help.

01:35:34.190 --> 01:35:38.510
I quickly realized our best option was to
just finish the game and not come back.

01:35:38.510 --> 01:35:42.380
We soon realized there were only two contestants
out of the six that we could even afford with

01:35:42.380 --> 01:35:46.780
the chips that we had left, and they were
the bottom two in terms of odds.

01:35:46.780 --> 01:35:52.050
We went with the cheapest one, wanting to
support this heinous game as little as possible.

01:35:52.050 --> 01:35:56.790
The game started and the object was to bend
back as far as possible in a bridge position.

01:35:56.790 --> 01:36:00.610
Their score was measured by how close they
could get their hands to their heels.

01:36:00.610 --> 01:36:05.570
It didn’t seem like this game would be anywhere
near as brutal as the last one, but I was

01:36:05.570 --> 01:36:08.060
unfortunately surprised to see how close it
came.

01:36:08.060 --> 01:36:11.440
I saw contortions that I didn’t even think
were possible.

01:36:11.440 --> 01:36:15.340
All of the contestants were able to see each
other, and each of them seemed to be trying

01:36:15.340 --> 01:36:16.610
their hardest.

01:36:16.610 --> 01:36:21.900
If there was some kind of external motivator
in this game like there was in the last, I

01:36:21.900 --> 01:36:26.280
couldn’t see what it was, but I could tell
none of them wanted to lose.

01:36:26.280 --> 01:36:30.910
It got to the point of one girl pushing herself
so hard that she screamed out and collapsed

01:36:30.910 --> 01:36:34.440
on the floor when she wasn’t able to go
any further.

01:36:34.440 --> 01:36:39.281
As they continued to strain, there were two
clear leaders: the petite girl and the more

01:36:39.281 --> 01:36:42.820
buff looking one who were the final two of
the previous round.

01:36:42.820 --> 01:36:47.340
This time the smaller girl came out on top,
and her rival slammed her hand on the floor

01:36:47.340 --> 01:36:48.420
in frustration.

01:36:48.420 --> 01:36:52.520
Round two was over, only one to go.

01:36:52.520 --> 01:36:57.330
The ladies were pushed to the breaking point,
but I was just glad that we got through that

01:36:57.330 --> 01:36:59.340
one with nobody’s back being broken.

01:36:59.340 --> 01:37:03.680
It wasn’t even the worst thing in the world,
and I was hoping that the final round would

01:37:03.680 --> 01:37:08.840
also be more tame and we could get out of
there with somewhat of a lighter conscience.

01:37:08.840 --> 01:37:13.600
Hopefully we’d be able to suppress this
night and enjoy the rest of our vacation after

01:37:13.600 --> 01:37:14.600
this.

01:37:14.600 --> 01:37:18.460
That all went out the window with what happened
next though.

01:37:18.460 --> 01:37:24.470
Five men came into the room, each carrying
a long nosed rifle gun, but before you ask,

01:37:24.470 --> 01:37:29.050
no, nobody was shot during this game, but
I didn’t know that at the time.

01:37:29.050 --> 01:37:33.200
That’s not to say what actually ended up
going down wasn’t horrifying though.

01:37:33.200 --> 01:37:37.190
The barrel of each each of these guns was
painted with a series of rainbow colored stripes

01:37:37.190 --> 01:37:39.860
stretching from the tip of the gun inwards.

01:37:39.860 --> 01:37:44.130
I didn’t understand what the meaning of
any of this was, until the bottle girl came

01:37:44.130 --> 01:37:46.570
in and gave us the final card.

01:37:46.570 --> 01:37:50.530
Printed upon it was the name of this last
game: Penetration.

01:37:50.530 --> 01:37:55.920
I looked at it in disbelief, but before I
could even begin to protest, Molly pointed

01:37:55.920 --> 01:38:00.400
out that with the chips we had left, we couldn’t
even afford the cheapest buy-in.

01:38:00.400 --> 01:38:03.920
Maybe this would finally prompt them kicking
us out.

01:38:03.920 --> 01:38:07.170
We were more than ready to be done with this.

01:38:07.170 --> 01:38:12.000
But after we once again failed to place a
bet, the bouncer came in to see what was up.

01:38:12.000 --> 01:38:16.130
We explained our situation and he told us
we’d have to get some more chips and told

01:38:16.130 --> 01:38:18.230
my wife to come with him.

01:38:18.230 --> 01:38:21.710
Minutes later he came back with a velvet bag
and handed it to me.

01:38:21.710 --> 01:38:23.840
It was filled with tons of chips!

01:38:23.840 --> 01:38:26.250
Way more than we ever had before.

01:38:26.250 --> 01:38:27.610
More than that guy at the roulette table.

01:38:27.610 --> 01:38:29.690
More than we could probably afford.

01:38:29.690 --> 01:38:31.070
“Where’s my wife?”

01:38:31.070 --> 01:38:32.110
I asked.

01:38:32.110 --> 01:38:33.590
But he was already gone.

01:38:33.590 --> 01:38:37.770
That’s when the bottle girl came through
one more time, with another card in hand and

01:38:37.770 --> 01:38:39.960
told me that there’s been a change.

01:38:39.960 --> 01:38:44.860
I turned around and looked through the window
into the game room, and what I saw was more

01:38:44.860 --> 01:38:49.940
upsetting and disturbing than anything else
I had laid eyes on that evening.

01:38:49.940 --> 01:38:52.230
Stripped down and shaking with fear...

01:38:52.230 --> 01:38:55.150
Molly joined the lineup of contestants.

01:38:55.150 --> 01:38:57.510
Number Fourteen.

01:38:57.510 --> 01:38:59.880
Isolated Getaway.

01:38:59.880 --> 01:39:05.070
This... isn’t easy for me to talk about.

01:39:05.070 --> 01:39:08.870
If you’ve ever tried to make long-term plans
in a relationship, you’ll probably know

01:39:08.870 --> 01:39:10.239
what it’s like.

01:39:10.239 --> 01:39:15.250
My boyfriend and I had gone out for two years
and decided to plan a relaxing little getaway.

01:39:15.250 --> 01:39:19.450
You never think that this kind of thing will
happen when you’re planning your trip but…

01:39:19.450 --> 01:39:22.670
we ended up splitting up a month and half
before.

01:39:22.670 --> 01:39:26.730
Ideally, I would have waited until after the
vacation to break up with him, but when I

01:39:26.730 --> 01:39:31.150
caught him fooling around with his physical
therapist, I didn’t even wait a day before

01:39:31.150 --> 01:39:32.150
ending it.

01:39:32.150 --> 01:39:36.780
Lucky for me, I still had a suite booked at
the Grand Maritime Beach Resort.

01:39:36.780 --> 01:39:41.010
For whatever reason, even though he did all
the research and booking, the reservation

01:39:41.010 --> 01:39:44.710
was made under both of our names with my email
address!

01:39:44.710 --> 01:39:48.690
I figured it to be a good consolation prize
for the suffering he put through.

01:39:48.690 --> 01:39:52.680
Besides, I wasn’t going to let him ruin
my much needed time off.

01:39:52.680 --> 01:39:54.390
He’d already done enough damage.

01:39:54.390 --> 01:39:58.090
I’d be enjoying this vacation with or without
him.

01:39:58.090 --> 01:40:02.900
It felt amazing to hop off the plane and stuff
my winter jacket in my bag for the rest of

01:40:02.900 --> 01:40:03.900
the week.

01:40:03.900 --> 01:40:07.420
I breezed through the airport, at the end
of which this short chubby guy asked me if

01:40:07.420 --> 01:40:08.920
I need a ride.

01:40:08.920 --> 01:40:13.320
I told him I was looking for the Grand Maritime
shuttle and it turned out that he was the

01:40:13.320 --> 01:40:14.320
driver!

01:40:14.320 --> 01:40:17.320
I guess I lucked out because we didn’t even
have to wait for any other passengers.

01:40:17.320 --> 01:40:20.510
I’d be enjoying that sunshine before I knew
it.

01:40:20.510 --> 01:40:24.760
Once we arrived at the resort, they told me
my room wasn’t quite ready, but they offered

01:40:24.760 --> 01:40:29.660
to take my bags and let me enjoy the pool
and beach while they made the preparations.

01:40:29.660 --> 01:40:32.220
To be honest, that’s exactly what I wanted.

01:40:32.220 --> 01:40:34.430
I could worry about unpacking later.

01:40:34.430 --> 01:40:38.200
I got changed in the bathroom and found myself
a poolside chair.

01:40:38.200 --> 01:40:42.920
The resort was… not at all what I remembered
my ex describing to me.

01:40:42.920 --> 01:40:44.690
First, I expected more people.

01:40:44.690 --> 01:40:47.460
I mean, I was the only one at the pool area.

01:40:47.460 --> 01:40:51.170
It looked like there were some more people
by the beach, but I felt like it should be

01:40:51.170 --> 01:40:53.180
much more busy at this time of year.

01:40:53.180 --> 01:40:57.110
Still, I didn’t mind some isolation and
time to myself.

01:40:57.110 --> 01:40:59.700
It was also kind of a shoddy place.

01:40:59.700 --> 01:41:02.890
I remembered it looking much better in the
photos.

01:41:02.890 --> 01:41:05.340
Leave it to my stupid ex not to do the research...

01:41:05.340 --> 01:41:06.340
Who cares though.

01:41:06.340 --> 01:41:09.280
I was here, catching some sun and not at work.

01:41:09.280 --> 01:41:12.260
A couple of loose pool tiles could not change
that.

01:41:12.260 --> 01:41:14.890
I decided to take a look around the resort
a bit.

01:41:14.890 --> 01:41:16.800
Again, I was pretty unimpressed.

01:41:16.800 --> 01:41:19.460
Actually, it was kind of creepy.

01:41:19.460 --> 01:41:25.000
It felt as though it hadn’t been renovated
since the 70s and there was nobody around.

01:41:25.000 --> 01:41:28.780
It was like exploring the ruins of a forgotten
old resort.

01:41:28.780 --> 01:41:33.080
There was a smaller pool that I came across
was empty and filled with moss.

01:41:33.080 --> 01:41:37.320
The paintings on the walls were cute… or
at least they might have been several years

01:41:37.320 --> 01:41:41.800
ago, but the paint had chipped away so that
the eyes of they tribal figures that were

01:41:41.800 --> 01:41:44.340
depicted just looked like empty voids.

01:41:44.340 --> 01:41:48.540
I felt more like I was in a forbidden temple
than a welcoming beach resort.

01:41:48.540 --> 01:41:53.200
Corroded statues and broken fences were just
a couple more clues as to why this place was

01:41:53.200 --> 01:41:54.620
so empty.

01:41:54.620 --> 01:41:58.880
There was even a boat on the beach that was
turned over in the sand, gutted for parts

01:41:58.880 --> 01:42:00.790
and covered in graffiti.

01:42:00.790 --> 01:42:05.040
Perhaps the strangest part about it was the
tinny little speakers hidden in rocks around

01:42:05.040 --> 01:42:09.590
the resort which were probably the only evidence
that the place was actually operational.

01:42:09.590 --> 01:42:13.300
I decided to just go back to the pool and
tan until my room was ready.

01:42:13.300 --> 01:42:17.480
While I waited, one of the staff came up to
me and asked if I was interested in their

01:42:17.480 --> 01:42:18.790
complimentary massage.

01:42:18.790 --> 01:42:20.800
That sounded good to me.

01:42:20.800 --> 01:42:23.690
I followed him in into the spa building next
to the pool.

01:42:23.690 --> 01:42:28.580
I laid out face down on the massage table
and he began to go to work on my shoulders.

01:42:28.580 --> 01:42:30.780
It was… oddly quiet.

01:42:30.780 --> 01:42:32.650
No music or anything.

01:42:32.650 --> 01:42:35.750
Just the sound of him breathing and the kneading
of my flesh.

01:42:35.750 --> 01:42:40.110
It was a bit uncomfortable, but at the same
time it just felt so good so I tried to ignore

01:42:40.110 --> 01:42:41.110
it.

01:42:41.110 --> 01:42:43.030
Then it got more uncomfortable.

01:42:43.030 --> 01:42:47.580
The guy just presumptuously unhooks my bikini
and goes to work on that part of my back and

01:42:47.580 --> 01:42:48.580
sides.

01:42:48.580 --> 01:42:52.270
I don’t usually get a lot of massages, but
shouldn’t he ask first before doing something

01:42:52.270 --> 01:42:53.690
like that?

01:42:53.690 --> 01:42:58.330
Then I remembered why I was here and I thought
I should just let myself live a little.

01:42:58.330 --> 01:43:03.270
Someone else came into the room and started
talking to the masseuse in a language I couldn’t

01:43:03.270 --> 01:43:04.270
understand.

01:43:04.270 --> 01:43:08.270
It sounded like he was answering a bunch of
questions, and he sounded kind of angry.

01:43:08.270 --> 01:43:10.960
His voice got louder as he came into the room.

01:43:10.960 --> 01:43:15.480
It sounded like he was right next to my head,
so I opened my eyes and this guy was right

01:43:15.480 --> 01:43:17.310
there staring at me!

01:43:17.310 --> 01:43:20.210
I panicked, but I didn’t quite know what
to do.

01:43:20.210 --> 01:43:21.840
He started pacing around the table.

01:43:21.840 --> 01:43:23.020
Talking to the guy.

01:43:23.020 --> 01:43:25.660
It felt like his eyes were locked onto me.

01:43:25.660 --> 01:43:30.500
My relaxation level dropped fast and my nervousness
level was skyrocketing.

01:43:30.500 --> 01:43:32.160
This guy was unbelievable.

01:43:32.160 --> 01:43:35.610
But then, he actually grabbed my butt!

01:43:35.610 --> 01:43:37.110
I screamed out, “Hey!”

01:43:37.110 --> 01:43:39.980
but I couldn’t fully turn away without exposing
myself.

01:43:39.980 --> 01:43:42.260
I was just about ready to be done with this
massage.

01:43:42.260 --> 01:43:45.840
Why wasn’t the masseuse telling this creep
to buzz off?

01:43:45.840 --> 01:43:47.850
The guy didn’t even let go of me when I
yelled at him!

01:43:47.850 --> 01:43:48.850
What the hell?

01:43:48.850 --> 01:43:52.520
They just carried on their conversation, only
raising their voices, so I started kicking

01:43:52.520 --> 01:43:55.510
and thrashing my feet and screaming at them
to stop!

01:43:55.510 --> 01:44:00.260
Only problem was, I could raise all the ruckus
I wanted but we all knew there was probably

01:44:00.260 --> 01:44:01.840
nobody out there to hear me.

01:44:01.840 --> 01:44:06.120
I tried to fight my way out but the masseuse
ended my struggle swiftly when he dug his

01:44:06.120 --> 01:44:10.170
thumbs somewhere into my shoulders as hard
as he could.

01:44:10.170 --> 01:44:12.630
He must have hit some kind of pressure point
or something because that’s the last thing

01:44:12.630 --> 01:44:13.670
I remembered.

01:44:13.670 --> 01:44:16.270
I was out.

01:44:16.270 --> 01:44:17.360
I woke up.

01:44:17.360 --> 01:44:22.510
By the time I remembered what had happened,
I realized I was in a far worse situation.

01:44:22.510 --> 01:44:27.750
I was on a speedboat zipping through the ocean,
accompanied by only that strange man who had

01:44:27.750 --> 01:44:28.750
violated me.

01:44:28.750 --> 01:44:31.910
I could see the island off in the distance
and it was only getting further and further

01:44:31.910 --> 01:44:32.910
away.

01:44:32.910 --> 01:44:36.040
I jumped out of the boat and swam as fast
as I possibly could!

01:44:36.040 --> 01:44:41.050
I heard the engine die and the driver turn
around as soon as he realized I was gone.

01:44:41.050 --> 01:44:43.630
Before I knew it, the boat was back in front
of me.

01:44:43.630 --> 01:44:47.900
He told me it was stupid to try to swim back
and that it was further than it looked and

01:44:47.900 --> 01:44:49.250
yanked me back in.

01:44:49.250 --> 01:44:50.640
He was right.

01:44:50.640 --> 01:44:53.870
I didn’t have the stamina to swim all the
back to shore.

01:44:53.870 --> 01:44:58.790
As I stared off at how far it really was,
I saw a resort on the coast that looked far

01:44:58.790 --> 01:45:00.150
nicer than my own.

01:45:00.150 --> 01:45:04.190
Why couldn’t my stupid ex have just done
his research and booked a decent place?

01:45:04.190 --> 01:45:07.010
That’s when I realized something…

01:45:07.010 --> 01:45:11.080
The sign displayed above the resort could
just barely be read in the distance…

01:45:11.080 --> 01:45:18.510
It said: Grand Maritime Beach Resort.

01:45:18.510 --> 01:45:20.170
Number Fifteen.

01:45:20.170 --> 01:45:23.860
Last Resort.

01:45:23.860 --> 01:45:26.780
I looked up and saw a ship departing from
the dock.

01:45:26.780 --> 01:45:31.980
A couple of jetski riders zoomed by the ship’s
wake, even managing to catch a little air.

01:45:31.980 --> 01:45:32.980
That looked fun.

01:45:32.980 --> 01:45:34.570
Maybe I could do a little bit of that later.

01:45:34.570 --> 01:45:38.610
I dug my toes into the warm sand and looked
at my watch.

01:45:38.610 --> 01:45:39.750
It was 2:03.

01:45:39.750 --> 01:45:43.020
It seemed like as good a time as any to grab
myself a drink.

01:45:43.020 --> 01:45:48.070
Afterall, the bar here at the Grand Maritime
was complimentary, so why not?

01:45:48.070 --> 01:45:49.070
"Lucy.

01:45:49.070 --> 01:45:50.070
Lucy, you OK?"

01:45:50.070 --> 01:45:54.150
I shook my sleeping girlfriend’s shoulder
lightly to see if she wanted anything.

01:45:54.150 --> 01:45:57.430
"Uhh yeah, I just fell asleep.

01:45:57.430 --> 01:45:58.490
What time is it?"

01:45:58.490 --> 01:45:59.850
"About 2.

01:45:59.850 --> 01:46:01.120
You were tired.

01:46:01.120 --> 01:46:02.660
You look dead."

01:46:02.660 --> 01:46:03.660
"Thanks..."

01:46:03.660 --> 01:46:04.900
"I was just going up to the bar.

01:46:04.900 --> 01:46:05.900
Do you want anything to drink?"

01:46:05.900 --> 01:46:09.170
"You could grab me a Piña Colada I guess."

01:46:09.170 --> 01:46:10.170
"OK."

01:46:10.170 --> 01:46:13.090
With that, I kissed her and headed off to
the bar.

01:46:13.090 --> 01:46:16.790
When I got back with the drinks, my girlfriend
seemed to have wandered off, so I resumed

01:46:16.790 --> 01:46:21.270
my position on the lounge chair and stared
at the shoreline for a bit, full of hope that

01:46:21.270 --> 01:46:23.690
this was going to be the best vacation ever.

01:46:23.690 --> 01:46:26.460
This was so nice.

01:46:26.460 --> 01:46:27.730
About 15 minutes went by.

01:46:27.730 --> 01:46:30.110
Lucy still didn’t show up.

01:46:30.110 --> 01:46:31.590
Ten minutes more.

01:46:31.590 --> 01:46:32.690
Another 15 minutes.

01:46:32.690 --> 01:46:35.000
Where had she run off to?

01:46:35.000 --> 01:46:37.680
There was this old German couple at the chairs
behind us.

01:46:37.680 --> 01:46:41.880
I asked if they’d seen a blond girl in a
black bikini sitting here, and where she might

01:46:41.880 --> 01:46:42.880
have headed off to.

01:46:42.880 --> 01:46:45.810
They said they had seen her talking to “the
survey guy”.

01:46:45.810 --> 01:46:50.300
When I asked who the survey guy was, they
told me he was going around from chair to

01:46:50.300 --> 01:46:54.280
chair with a clipboard asking people if they’d
like to fill out a 15-minute satisfaction

01:46:54.280 --> 01:46:57.200
survey and that they’d seen him talking
to Lucy.

01:46:57.200 --> 01:47:00.230
I asked what direction they’d gone, but
neither one of them was sure.

01:47:00.230 --> 01:47:02.370
I immediately knew something wrong.

01:47:02.370 --> 01:47:07.800
Lucy was not the type to spend 15 minutes
filling out a survey, especially on vacation.

01:47:07.800 --> 01:47:12.560
The next closest person was an attractive
young girl sipping on a smoothie by herself.

01:47:12.560 --> 01:47:17.140
I asked her if she might have seen my girlfriend,
possibly with a guy holding a clipboard?

01:47:17.140 --> 01:47:21.360
She told me she wasn’t sure about Lucy,
but that she may have seen the clipboard guy.

01:47:21.360 --> 01:47:25.480
According to her, he had been going from chair
to chair and had asked her if she wanted to

01:47:25.480 --> 01:47:30.610
sign up for some kind of ‘island adventure’
thing, but she had politely declined.

01:47:30.610 --> 01:47:33.780
Apparently he was really pushing it but she
just wasn’t interested.

01:47:33.780 --> 01:47:34.780
“Excuse me.”

01:47:34.780 --> 01:47:38.850
We were interrupted by a guy who was about
my age, wearing long swim trunks.

01:47:38.850 --> 01:47:41.410
“My apologies for interrupting.

01:47:41.410 --> 01:47:45.780
I just happened to overhear you say you were
looking for your girlfriend.

01:47:45.780 --> 01:47:49.830
My wife seems to have disappeared off this
beach earlier this morning when I ran back

01:47:49.830 --> 01:47:51.540
to the room to get some sunscreen.

01:47:51.540 --> 01:47:54.770
I’ve been looking all over and haven’t
been able to find her.”

01:47:54.770 --> 01:47:57.770
“Yeah, I just went to bar and came back.

01:47:57.770 --> 01:48:01.340
She was gone, it’s been almost and hour
so I started asking around.”

01:48:01.340 --> 01:48:04.020
“Why don’t we both investigate.

01:48:04.020 --> 01:48:07.590
Knowing my wife there’s probably some spa
we don’t know about that they’ve both

01:48:07.590 --> 01:48:08.590
run off to.”

01:48:08.590 --> 01:48:09.620
“Yeah, you’re probably right.

01:48:09.620 --> 01:48:10.630
Let’s go find them.”

01:48:10.630 --> 01:48:14.410
The girl I was talking to said the guy with
the clipboard was headed down the beach to

01:48:14.410 --> 01:48:16.690
the left so we continued that way.

01:48:16.690 --> 01:48:18.990
“My name’s Mike by the way.”

01:48:18.990 --> 01:48:19.990
“Gary.”

01:48:19.990 --> 01:48:21.610
We continued asking around.

01:48:21.610 --> 01:48:26.460
One guy said that he’d seen the survey guy
come by but had told him he wasn’t interested.

01:48:26.460 --> 01:48:28.440
Another couple said they hadn’t seen either
of them.

01:48:28.440 --> 01:48:32.430
And then one chick said that some guy had
asked her to come down to the activity shack

01:48:32.430 --> 01:48:36.370
to sign up for some kind of rainforest adventure
and she’d said no.

01:48:36.370 --> 01:48:39.590
That’s when I remembered Lucy and I checking
into the hotel.

01:48:39.590 --> 01:48:42.460
She found this pamphlet with all these activities.

01:48:42.460 --> 01:48:46.490
I think she told me she was interested in
doing some rainforest hike or something.

01:48:46.490 --> 01:48:49.070
Mike and I decided to look for this activity
shack.

01:48:49.070 --> 01:48:51.620
We headed down the beach to the end of the
resort’s property.

01:48:51.620 --> 01:48:54.760
“Well Mike, I guess this is where we turn
back.”

01:48:54.760 --> 01:48:58.550
“I say we continue searching down the beach
for this supposed activity shack.

01:48:58.550 --> 01:49:01.810
I’ve already searched every inch of the
resort for my wife.

01:49:01.810 --> 01:49:04.820
I’m convinced they’re off the property
somewhere.”

01:49:04.820 --> 01:49:06.960
“I guess I’ll walk down a bit further
with you.

01:49:06.960 --> 01:49:08.980
I’ve got nothing to lose by checking.”

01:49:08.980 --> 01:49:12.120
We continued down the beach until we found
an empty shack.

01:49:12.120 --> 01:49:16.280
It didn’t look like an activity shack per
say, just more of a little hut.

01:49:16.280 --> 01:49:18.680
Before moving on, Mike noticed something in
the sand.

01:49:18.680 --> 01:49:21.510
He pulled up and dusted off a clipboard.

01:49:21.510 --> 01:49:26.660
There was one page on it, an empty spreadsheet
with the words “resort survey” crudely

01:49:26.660 --> 01:49:28.130
printed at the top.

01:49:28.130 --> 01:49:29.660
We looked at each other.

01:49:29.660 --> 01:49:30.660
Mike was wide-eyed.

01:49:30.660 --> 01:49:34.730
He flipped over the paper, and the back was
completely different, a colored advertisement

01:49:34.730 --> 01:49:39.400
with bright graphics of ziplining, a campfire
and a waterfall.

01:49:39.400 --> 01:49:41.080
Something here didn’t add up.

01:49:41.080 --> 01:49:45.730
I only saw two pairs of footsteps in the sand
heading out of the activity shack.

01:49:45.730 --> 01:49:50.170
Instead of leading back to the resort, they
led back inland towards a street.

01:49:50.170 --> 01:49:52.510
Something was not right here.

01:49:52.510 --> 01:49:56.300
Mike and I headed to the street where some
sand was kicked up onto the pavement.

01:49:56.300 --> 01:50:00.070
Someone had definitely J-walked right here,
so we headed across the street and into a

01:50:00.070 --> 01:50:01.070
rainforest.

01:50:01.070 --> 01:50:04.570
We decided to spread out a bit and cover as
much ground as possible.

01:50:04.570 --> 01:50:08.700
We made sure to stay within an earshot of
each other, so when we inevitably got lost,

01:50:08.700 --> 01:50:12.250
at least we weren’t separated from each
other.

01:50:12.250 --> 01:50:14.300
“Lucy!

01:50:14.300 --> 01:50:16.340
Lucy!”

01:50:16.340 --> 01:50:19.320
It seemed like we were totally alone in this
forest.

01:50:19.320 --> 01:50:20.900
It seemed useless.

01:50:20.900 --> 01:50:22.550
I was about ready to turn and go back.

01:50:22.550 --> 01:50:24.110
They couldn’t be out here…

01:50:24.110 --> 01:50:26.310
But that’s when I heard Mike call out to
me.

01:50:26.310 --> 01:50:27.310
“Gary!

01:50:27.310 --> 01:50:28.310
Over here!

01:50:28.310 --> 01:50:29.310
Come quick!”

01:50:29.310 --> 01:50:30.370
My heart jolted and I ran over to him.

01:50:30.370 --> 01:50:34.650
“I was looking around over here and I saw
something way off in the distance.

01:50:34.650 --> 01:50:36.440
There were three figures standing there.

01:50:36.440 --> 01:50:37.670
Two men and a woman.

01:50:37.670 --> 01:50:48.800
I was about to call out to them when the two
men jumped the lady and knocked her out!”

01:50:48.800 --> 01:50:52.280
I felt a sharp pain of nervousness and excitement
in my chest.

01:50:52.280 --> 01:50:53.420
Could it have been Lucy?

01:50:53.420 --> 01:50:56.920
I wanted to be close to finding her but I
couldn’t stand the idea of her not being

01:50:56.920 --> 01:50:57.920
OK.

01:50:57.920 --> 01:50:58.920
“When they noticed me staring they carried
her into a car and sped off.

01:50:58.920 --> 01:50:59.920
I think it could have been your girlfriend.”

01:50:59.920 --> 01:51:00.920
We ran over there.

01:51:00.920 --> 01:51:02.660
There was no real evidence to speak of, but
there were tire tracks that we could follow.

01:51:02.660 --> 01:51:06.460
Not only was it our best bet of finding our
women, but it was probably our only bet for

01:51:06.460 --> 01:51:07.880
finding our way out of here.

01:51:07.880 --> 01:51:11.440
We ended up following these tracks for 3 full
hours.

01:51:11.440 --> 01:51:14.970
It was getting dark by the time we came across
a little campsite.

01:51:14.970 --> 01:51:18.510
There was a bonfire that had recently been
put out, the wood was still charred and I

01:51:18.510 --> 01:51:19.510
could smell smoke.

01:51:19.510 --> 01:51:23.700
The tracks continued on from there though
and 30 minutes later we were finally led out

01:51:23.700 --> 01:51:26.720
of the forest where the tiremarks continued
on sand.

01:51:26.720 --> 01:51:30.200
It was a private little beach area hidden
by rocks on both sides.

01:51:30.200 --> 01:51:34.060
We eventually reached the end of the tracks,
where a Jeep was parked in the sand near the

01:51:34.060 --> 01:51:37.590
water and some footsteps led right into to
the ocean itself.

01:51:37.590 --> 01:51:38.590
Shoot.

01:51:38.590 --> 01:51:40.470
We wouldn’t be able to track them though
the water.

01:51:40.470 --> 01:51:43.650
And there were so many different ways they
could have gone.

01:51:43.650 --> 01:51:47.340
My heart ached as the hope inside of me began
to die.

01:51:47.340 --> 01:51:52.350
I stared into the same crystal blue waters
that I had just hours before, but now with

01:51:52.350 --> 01:51:53.870
an outlook of despair.

01:51:53.870 --> 01:51:56.440
I felt like I was never going to see her again.

01:51:56.440 --> 01:51:59.400
I looked over to Mike.

01:51:59.400 --> 01:52:01.780
“I have an idea.”

01:52:01.780 --> 01:52:05.630
I’d never ridden a jetski before but I was
going to have to learn quick.

01:52:05.630 --> 01:52:09.930
It was easy enough to get the hang of and
I soon found myself focusing more on looking

01:52:09.930 --> 01:52:12.040
for that boat than worrying about the controls.

01:52:12.040 --> 01:52:15.230
We were back in front of the Grand Maritime
resort now.

01:52:15.230 --> 01:52:18.020
There was a little speedboat whipping across
the current in the distance.

01:52:18.020 --> 01:52:21.030
A woman sat up and jumped off of the boat!

01:52:21.030 --> 01:52:23.930
She was thrashing in the water, swimming back
toward the coast.

01:52:23.930 --> 01:52:26.470
The driver of the boat turned back and pulled
her back in.

01:52:26.470 --> 01:52:27.970
“Did you see that?”

01:52:27.970 --> 01:52:28.970
“Yeah.

01:52:28.970 --> 01:52:29.970
That was weird.

01:52:29.970 --> 01:52:31.790
Let’s keep an eye on them.”

01:52:31.790 --> 01:52:35.740
So we did our best to follow this boat, making
sure not to get too close or follow him too

01:52:35.740 --> 01:52:37.130
directly at any point.

01:52:37.130 --> 01:52:41.230
We zig-zagged our way around, just staying
barely within an eyeshot.

01:52:41.230 --> 01:52:45.480
Eventually the boat pulled in next to a much
larger ship which was anchored out at sea.

01:52:45.480 --> 01:52:49.990
The guy tied a rope tethering him to the larger
ship, then climbed aboard dragging the woman

01:52:49.990 --> 01:52:50.990
with him.

01:52:50.990 --> 01:52:53.300
“You park yours up next to that speedboat.

01:52:53.300 --> 01:52:57.000
I’ll hide mine along the other side of the
ship and swim back around to this side.

01:52:57.000 --> 01:53:01.190
That way if they see yours we have a backup
to escape on.”

01:53:01.190 --> 01:53:02.570
This was it.

01:53:02.570 --> 01:53:05.800
If we didn’t find Lucy here, I was probably
never going to see her again.

01:53:05.800 --> 01:53:08.420
I parked the jetski and climbed onto the boat.

01:53:08.420 --> 01:53:15.770
We headed down a dark metal hallway, trying
to keep our footsteps as quiet as possible.

01:53:15.770 --> 01:53:20.100
As we traveled down, the sound of music thumping
from another room got louder.

01:53:20.100 --> 01:53:23.280
Some kind of party was going on on the other
side of this wall.

01:53:23.280 --> 01:53:27.030
There was a door on the side, or we could
just continue further down the hall into the

01:53:27.030 --> 01:53:28.060
dark.

01:53:28.060 --> 01:53:32.740
I decided to peak inside of the door and opened
it juuussstttt a crack.

01:53:32.740 --> 01:53:34.520
It was a huge room.

01:53:34.520 --> 01:53:36.400
Dark, with vibrant neon lights.

01:53:36.400 --> 01:53:40.170
Tons of people dressed up sat at slot machines
and blackjack tables.

01:53:40.170 --> 01:53:43.760
I quickly and quietly closed the door, hoping
I hadn’t been noticed.

01:53:43.760 --> 01:53:47.510
I nodded my head at Mike to continue further
down the corridor, which we couldn’t see

01:53:47.510 --> 01:53:49.550
the end of because of the dark.

01:53:49.550 --> 01:53:51.900
Mike put his hand out in front of me to stop.

01:53:51.900 --> 01:53:58.360
He motioned to his ear, and I listened…

01:53:58.360 --> 01:54:01.910
I could hear breathing at the end of the hallway.

01:54:01.910 --> 01:54:06.340
There was no doubt that someone was standing
guard.

01:54:06.340 --> 01:54:10.690
We knew he was there and he knew we were here.

01:54:10.690 --> 01:54:15.400
Then, as if to break to break the silence
and tension, his voice called out of the dark,

01:54:15.400 --> 01:54:19.040
and told us we weren't allowed back here,
and to head back out to the casino.

01:54:19.040 --> 01:54:23.350
Mike whispered for me to keep quiet, then
spoke out to the guy.

01:54:23.350 --> 01:54:28.000
“Excuse me sir, I was just looking for my
wife.

01:54:28.000 --> 01:54:30.870
I believe she may have wandered back this
way.”

01:54:30.870 --> 01:54:34.970
The guard told him that nobody had been through
this way, but Mike insisted he double check.

01:54:34.970 --> 01:54:39.210
We heard the door he was guarding creak open
and Mike dragged me forward into the dark,

01:54:39.210 --> 01:54:40.810
to where we could see the end of the hall.

01:54:40.810 --> 01:54:45.610
He yanked on the door but it had automatically
locked, so he hid in the corner behind the

01:54:45.610 --> 01:54:46.610
door.

01:54:46.610 --> 01:54:49.300
[whispered] “Stand over there and wait for
him to come through.”

01:54:49.300 --> 01:54:50.980
I could see where Mike was going with this.

01:54:50.980 --> 01:54:54.730
I wasn’t convinced it would work but I couldn't
come up with much better.

01:54:54.730 --> 01:54:57.480
The guard came back through the door and saw
me standing there in the hall.

01:54:57.480 --> 01:54:58.550
I said nothing.

01:54:58.550 --> 01:55:00.670
He told me that nobody had gotten back there.

01:55:00.670 --> 01:55:01.670
“Thanks anyways.”

01:55:01.670 --> 01:55:06.520
The voice came from behind him as Mike jumped
on the guy's back, taking him by surprise

01:55:06.520 --> 01:55:08.833
before he had a chance to close the door behind
him!

01:55:08.833 --> 01:55:10.030
I bolted through the door and made it!

01:55:10.030 --> 01:55:13.830
It slammed shut with a huge metallic clang.

01:55:13.830 --> 01:55:16.440
I would be on my own from here on out.

01:55:16.440 --> 01:55:19.180
The room I found myself in was some kind of
lab.

01:55:19.180 --> 01:55:23.880
There was a row of several operation tables,
and these vertical tubes with a blue glow

01:55:23.880 --> 01:55:25.110
emanating from them.

01:55:25.110 --> 01:55:29.140
I inspected the first one, and it seemed to
just be an empty water tank, though it did

01:55:29.140 --> 01:55:33.050
contain what looked kind of like a scuba regulator
at the end of a tube.

01:55:33.050 --> 01:55:36.860
Before I could inspect any further I heard
a door being unlocked and I quickly dove behind

01:55:36.860 --> 01:55:39.630
the tank to hide.

01:55:39.630 --> 01:55:43.350
“We had no idea what we were getting ourselves
into.

01:55:43.350 --> 01:55:44.350
Please.

01:55:44.350 --> 01:55:48.350
I just want to get my husband and go back
to my hotel.

01:55:48.350 --> 01:55:49.350
Hey, what do you think you're doing?

01:55:49.350 --> 01:55:50.350
Get your hands off me!

01:55:50.350 --> 01:55:51.350
HELP!”

01:55:51.350 --> 01:55:52.350
Two men, who looked to be employees of the
casino, slammed this woman to the operating

01:55:52.350 --> 01:55:53.880
table with her screaming all the while.

01:55:53.880 --> 01:55:57.420
I couldn't fully see what they were doing
to her from where I was, but I did see the

01:55:57.420 --> 01:55:59.750
man's pants drop at his ankles…

01:55:59.750 --> 01:56:03.510
And based on the screams I'm sure you can
guess the rest...

01:56:03.510 --> 01:56:09.320
It was hard enough to stand by and let this
happen, but I also kept imagining my Lucy

01:56:09.320 --> 01:56:10.960
in the same situation.

01:56:10.960 --> 01:56:12.810
My fists were shaking with rage.

01:56:12.810 --> 01:56:15.990
I was gritting my teeth and I could barely
contain myself.

01:56:15.990 --> 01:56:21.530
Still, I had the advantage of them not knowing
I was here, and if I was going to have any

01:56:21.530 --> 01:56:23.730
chance, I had to keep it that way.

01:56:23.730 --> 01:56:27.670
The girl on the table seemed to just give
up the fight, and the man doing the thrusting

01:56:27.670 --> 01:56:32.210
said “ten to one” then spewed out a bunch
of different numbers as if he was some kind

01:56:32.210 --> 01:56:33.570
of twisted odds maker.

01:56:33.570 --> 01:56:37.880
Then the girl, now stark naked, was pushed
out into another room.

01:56:37.880 --> 01:56:40.600
The second guy followed her out there with
a rifle gun!

01:56:40.600 --> 01:56:41.600
Whoa.

01:56:41.600 --> 01:56:43.470
I was in way over my head.

01:56:43.470 --> 01:56:46.990
I had no way to defend myself against that.

01:56:46.990 --> 01:56:50.080
I had to find Lucy and get out without getting
caught.

01:56:50.080 --> 01:56:53.820
The first guy went into a different door and
it looked like he headed up some stairs.

01:56:53.820 --> 01:56:56.050
I jumped up to investigate the rest of the
lab.

01:56:56.050 --> 01:56:59.280
There were more of these water tanks stretching
down the length of the room.

01:56:59.280 --> 01:57:03.820
What I found was that many of them contained
women, again, completely exposed, breathing

01:57:03.820 --> 01:57:04.820
through tubes.

01:57:04.820 --> 01:57:08.630
I recognised one of them as the lady we'd
seen jump off the speedboat earlier.

01:57:08.630 --> 01:57:10.710
The next girl looked in much worse shape.

01:57:10.710 --> 01:57:14.690
Her skin looked charred and her hair was standing
up in every direction.

01:57:14.690 --> 01:57:17.720
My hope was dwindling, but what happened next…

01:57:17.720 --> 01:57:18.720
I…

01:57:18.720 --> 01:57:21.800
I can't even explain the feeling that shot
through me.

01:57:21.800 --> 01:57:23.380
It was Lucy.

01:57:23.380 --> 01:57:26.070
I nearly blacked out upon seeing her.

01:57:26.070 --> 01:57:30.130
I was feeling every emotion a person can feel
all at once.

01:57:30.130 --> 01:57:34.630
Her eyes were closed and she was just gracefully
floating there, breathing through a mask,

01:57:34.630 --> 01:57:35.930
but definitely breathing.

01:57:35.930 --> 01:57:40.170
I knocked on the glass, unsure of how to get
her out.

01:57:40.170 --> 01:57:41.510
She didn't hear.

01:57:41.510 --> 01:57:45.940
I knocked harder and her eyes shot open; you
could just see that they were immediately

01:57:45.940 --> 01:57:49.170
filled with fear; that she'd been conditioned
to expect abuse.

01:57:49.170 --> 01:57:52.440
But once she recognized me, everything changed.

01:57:52.440 --> 01:57:55.740
She put her hand up to the glass and I reached
up and did the same.

01:57:55.740 --> 01:57:58.610
Once again, I heard the door unlock and I
ducked into hiding.

01:57:58.610 --> 01:58:00.720
This time it was two men.

01:58:00.720 --> 01:58:03.840
One looked like he was native to the island,
the other was a foreigner.

01:58:03.840 --> 01:58:05.040
Both were wearing suits.

01:58:05.040 --> 01:58:07.090
The foreign guy had a drink in his hand.

01:58:07.090 --> 01:58:10.090
He was overweight and and seemed to have a
breathing problem.

01:58:10.090 --> 01:58:14.480
There was a metal tube coming out of his neck
that seemed to be regulating his respiratory

01:58:14.480 --> 01:58:15.630
system.

01:58:15.630 --> 01:58:22.410
“That really was quite a show you put on
there, I must say.

01:58:22.410 --> 01:58:31.000
I do understand the relevance, of games 2
and 3, when making such decisions, but what

01:58:31.000 --> 01:58:33.070
was the point of the first game?”

01:58:33.070 --> 01:58:36.550
The islander guy responded, “simply to break
them.”

01:58:36.550 --> 01:58:38.010
“I see.

01:58:38.010 --> 01:58:40.940
This one performed beautifully.

01:58:40.940 --> 01:58:42.850
A fine specimen indeed.

01:58:42.850 --> 01:58:49.230
No doubt I'll be willing to shell out for
her.”

01:58:49.230 --> 01:58:52.080
They started talking prices and times.

01:58:52.080 --> 01:58:53.080
That was it.

01:58:53.080 --> 01:58:56.570
I couldn't stand by anymore and watch this
frickin guy whore out my girlfriend.

01:58:56.570 --> 01:58:58.150
I didn't care if I got myself killed.

01:58:58.150 --> 01:58:59.970
I just couldn't sit there and hide anymore.

01:58:59.970 --> 01:59:01.900
I crawled out, the guy didn't see me.

01:59:01.900 --> 01:59:05.360
I got a running start and socked the **** in
the face full speed!

01:59:05.360 --> 01:59:08.520
I shattered my fist but I didn't even realize
it at the time.

01:59:08.520 --> 01:59:11.890
Before he knew what hit him, I grabbed that
fat **** by the back of the neck and thrashed

01:59:11.890 --> 01:59:13.360
his face into the glass.

01:59:13.360 --> 01:59:16.890
It didn't budge, but it must have set off
some kind of alarm and a red light started

01:59:16.890 --> 01:59:17.890
flashing.

01:59:17.890 --> 01:59:22.850
I thrust his face into the glass, 2, 3, 4
times before it started to show a crack, which

01:59:22.850 --> 01:59:27.370
I noticed on the growing splotch of liquid
red now on the surface of the window.

01:59:27.370 --> 01:59:32.120
I reared back one more time, and with all
my might, shattered the tank on this guy's

01:59:32.120 --> 01:59:33.120
skull.

01:59:33.120 --> 01:59:35.890
Water washed out everywhere with a greater
force than I expected.

01:59:35.890 --> 01:59:37.670
Lucy went sliding across the lab floor.

01:59:37.670 --> 01:59:40.960
I helped her get to her feet, but there was
no time for a heartfelt reunion.

01:59:40.960 --> 01:59:42.570
We ran for our lives.

01:59:42.570 --> 01:59:43.570
As we exited I heard the voices of yelling
men behind us.

01:59:43.570 --> 01:59:48.540
We made it to the hall where I had left Mike
and the guard.

01:59:48.540 --> 01:59:52.240
I wasn't sure where the guard had gone, but
it was clear what has happened to Mike, he

01:59:52.240 --> 01:59:54.690
was beaten to a pulp and left sprawled out
on the floor.

01:59:54.690 --> 01:59:56.250
Then was no time to mourn.

01:59:56.250 --> 01:59:58.810
If we were lucky we might just get out alive.

01:59:58.810 --> 01:59:59.880
We made to the hatch.

01:59:59.880 --> 02:00:01.920
Somehow I was able to pry it open.

02:00:01.920 --> 02:00:03.710
We were back into the open air.

02:00:03.710 --> 02:00:04.710
Almost home free!

02:00:04.710 --> 02:00:08.730
But what waited for us on the other side would
possibly be my toughest challenge yet.

02:00:08.730 --> 02:00:13.270
The guard who had beaten Mike was standing
over the jetski I had pulled up in, which

02:00:13.270 --> 02:00:15.980
was on fire, and he continued to pour on the
gasoline.

02:00:15.980 --> 02:00:18.030
He turned around and saw us.

02:00:18.030 --> 02:00:22.020
Not knowing what else to do, I pushed him,
hoping to catch him off balance or something,

02:00:22.020 --> 02:00:23.050
and somehow it worked!

02:00:23.050 --> 02:00:26.850
He went crashing down into the flaming vehicle
before falling into the water.

02:00:26.850 --> 02:00:30.690
I had no idea if he'd gotten to the other
jetski but it was our only hope.

02:00:30.690 --> 02:00:31.690
“This way!”

02:00:31.690 --> 02:00:34.510
I took my girlfriend's hand and jumped out
into the ocean.

02:00:34.510 --> 02:00:35.980
We swam like there was no tomorrow.

02:00:35.980 --> 02:00:38.990
*gasping for air* “Where are we going?”

02:00:38.990 --> 02:00:45.930
The ship billowed it's horn over and over,
and I began to fear it might be a distress

02:00:45.930 --> 02:00:46.930
call.

02:00:46.930 --> 02:00:50.310
Still, if we got to the jetski, there probably
wasn't much they could do to catch us.

02:00:50.310 --> 02:00:51.340
This was it.

02:00:51.340 --> 02:00:53.090
It all came down to the escape.

02:00:53.090 --> 02:00:56.520
We turned the corner around the outside of
the ship to where Mike's jetski should have

02:00:56.520 --> 02:00:57.520
been…

02:00:57.520 --> 02:00:59.700
But it was gone…

02:00:59.700 --> 02:01:02.250
So that's it then.

02:01:02.250 --> 02:01:04.600
It was all for nothing.

02:01:04.600 --> 02:01:05.600
“There!

02:01:05.600 --> 02:01:07.090
What's that over there?”

02:01:07.090 --> 02:01:08.860
Off in the distance was Mike’s jetski!

02:01:08.860 --> 02:01:10.730
It had just drifted away from the ship!

02:01:10.730 --> 02:01:16.940
It was a long swim but we made it!

02:01:16.940 --> 02:01:20.040
The rest of the night was mostly a blur.

02:01:20.040 --> 02:01:24.730
I don't remember much of when we crashed into
the shore terrifying the tourists who were

02:01:24.730 --> 02:01:27.390
enjoying the ocean in moonlight.

02:01:27.390 --> 02:01:33.020
I don't remember the trip to the emergency
room, but I do remember when the pain of what

02:01:33.020 --> 02:01:36.570
they had done to me finally set in.

02:01:36.570 --> 02:01:41.170
The police came to talk to us, as did some
representatives from the resort.

02:01:41.170 --> 02:01:47.530
The casino was in international waters, so
it was out of the jurisdiction of the law.

02:01:47.530 --> 02:01:52.660
But they told us they were doing everything
they could to stop abductions on the land

02:01:52.660 --> 02:01:57.220
and keep tourists informed on the dangers
of gambling offshore.

02:01:57.220 --> 02:02:03.120
They had warnings posted all over the island,
but that didn't stop people from being drawn

02:02:03.120 --> 02:02:08.280
to the thrill and they would find other ways
to lure people in.

02:02:08.280 --> 02:02:14.120
The resort wasn't involved in any of this,
but of course they told us they would be striving

02:02:14.120 --> 02:02:19.880
to improve their security on the beach and
make sure people knew what dangers lie beyond

02:02:19.880 --> 02:02:20.960
their walls.

02:02:20.960 --> 02:02:26.170
They were kind enough to pay our medical bill
and we wouldn't have to worry about paying

02:02:26.170 --> 02:02:28.010
for our stay either.

02:02:28.010 --> 02:02:34.780
They even offered a free week at the resort
at a time of our choosing, but I already knew

02:02:34.780 --> 02:02:38.390
we would NEVER be coming back.

02:02:38.390 --> 02:02:42.650
The pain of my broken hand was really starting
to set in.

02:02:42.650 --> 02:02:47.490
The police wanted to know more about Mike
and his wife, but we didn't have much information

02:02:47.490 --> 02:02:51.040
to help them, other than the fact that his
wife was still out there.

02:02:51.040 --> 02:02:54.480
I asked if trafficking had always been a problem
on this island.

02:02:54.480 --> 02:02:59.650
His response made everything that had happened
to us that night seem even scarier.

02:02:59.650 --> 02:03:06.380
He scoffed at me and said, “if only it was
just trafficking…”

02:03:06.380 --> 02:03:13.440
BONUS VIDEO - Unboxing my Silver Play Button

02:03:13.440 --> 02:03:16.370
Welcome to a little break in the creepypasta
action.

02:03:16.370 --> 02:03:21.441
