02:03:44.560 --> 02:03:46.560
Very nice packaging from YouTube.

02:03:46.560 --> 02:03:47.923
I’m gonna toss this box out of the way.

02:03:47.923 --> 02:03:52.550
I also removed any stickers from that that
might dox me.

02:03:52.550 --> 02:03:57.820
But yeah they changed the look of the play
buttons so I don’t actually know if I’m

02:03:57.820 --> 02:04:01.920
gonna have the new one or the old one because
they changed it pretty soon after I ordered

02:04:01.920 --> 02:04:04.520
my button.

02:04:04.520 --> 02:04:06.120
Very nice packaging.

02:04:06.120 --> 02:04:07.500
YouTube.

02:04:07.500 --> 02:04:11.460
It would be kind of cool if I had the old
one because then I would be one of the few

02:04:11.460 --> 02:04:15.871
creators who gets their silver play button
as the old one and their gold play button

02:04:15.871 --> 02:04:17.790
as the new one.

02:04:17.790 --> 02:04:19.340
From YouTube.

02:04:19.340 --> 02:04:22.890
You’ve just done something that very few
YouTube creators accomplish.

02:04:22.890 --> 02:04:26.990
You had an astonishing 100,000 people subscribe
to your channel.

02:04:26.990 --> 02:04:30.440
We know that numbers on YouTube can get really
big but we hope you don’t lose sight of

02:04:30.440 --> 02:04:33.110
the reality behind that six-digit milestone.

02:04:33.110 --> 02:04:36.450
Each and every person who has subscribed to
your channel has been touched by what you’ve

02:04:36.450 --> 02:04:37.450
created.

02:04:37.450 --> 02:04:39.590
They were inspired, challenged or entertained.

02:04:39.590 --> 02:04:46.310
I hope if you’re watching this then you
have been moved by what I created.

02:04:46.310 --> 02:04:50.490
You achieved this milestone with hard work,
perseverance, and probably a healthy sense

02:04:50.490 --> 02:04:52.110
of humor too.

02:04:52.110 --> 02:04:55.050
You can be the judge of that.

02:04:55.050 --> 02:04:59.390
What you’ve accomplished can’t be taken
away from you and we’d like to recognise

02:04:59.390 --> 02:05:04.270
you and all your hard work with this silver
creator award, a small token of our esteem

02:05:04.270 --> 02:05:05.470
and respect.

02:05:05.470 --> 02:05:09.270
We know that you don’t do this for awards,
you do it because you have a drive to create

02:05:09.270 --> 02:05:10.270
and share.

02:05:10.270 --> 02:05:12.580
Because you found an audience who cares.

02:05:12.580 --> 02:05:15.580
Believe us when we say that we can’t wait
to see what you do next.

02:05:15.580 --> 02:05:20.080
A million subscribers may be a long way off
now, but you’re closer than you think and

02:05:20.080 --> 02:05:21.720
we’re rooting for you.

02:05:21.720 --> 02:05:24.580
Sincerely,
Susan Wojcicki signed this paper.

02:05:24.580 --> 02:05:25.580
Alright.

02:05:25.580 --> 02:05:28.420
Enough of this.

02:05:28.420 --> 02:05:31.890
What you really want to see is the silver
creator award.

02:05:31.890 --> 02:05:35.080
And it does look like it’s the old one.

02:05:35.080 --> 02:05:36.230
So, very cool.

02:05:36.230 --> 02:05:39.230
I’ll take the packaging off of this thing.

02:05:39.230 --> 02:05:43.550
Congratulations CZsWorld on passing 100,000
subscribers.

02:05:43.550 --> 02:05:48.990
I’ll have to figure out where I’m gonna
put this.

02:05:48.990 --> 02:05:54.180
But anyway, just a quick little break from
the creepypasta narration, and let’s get

02:05:54.180 --> 02:05:55.180
right back….

02:05:55.180 --> 02:06:00.220
Let’s dig right back in with the next story.

02:06:00.220 --> 02:06:04.300
Number 16 - Forbidden House

02:06:04.300 --> 02:06:08.320
This is a story that happened several years
back when Trick-or-Treating with my friend

02:06:08.320 --> 02:06:12.960
Alex, my older brother, John, and his friend,
Evan.

02:06:12.960 --> 02:06:18.030
Every neighborhood has that one house that
nobody ever wants to trick-or-treat at.

02:06:18.030 --> 02:06:25.610
Whether it be because of bad candy, mean owners,
a dentist house, fear... or otherwise...

02:06:25.610 --> 02:06:30.220
In this case, our parents told us we could
go off on our own this year as long as we

02:06:30.220 --> 02:06:33.690
stayed together and agreed not to go to that
house.

02:06:33.690 --> 02:06:38.510
I was in fourth grade that year and the idea
of getting to go off on our own was exciting

02:06:38.510 --> 02:06:42.050
to me at the time, so naturally, I agreed.

02:06:42.050 --> 02:06:46.240
When Alex and Evan got to our house, we waited
around and answered the door for a while.

02:06:46.240 --> 02:06:48.850
Trying to scare some of the younger trick-or-treaters.

02:06:48.850 --> 02:06:52.900
Eventually, after our parents took our baby
sister to some of the houses, we grabbed our

02:06:52.900 --> 02:06:55.720
pillowcases and set off to get some candy.

02:06:55.720 --> 02:07:00.320
We lived in a pretty safe neighborhood, so
it was common for kids our age -- or even

02:07:00.320 --> 02:07:02.650
younger -- to go out alone.

02:07:02.650 --> 02:07:07.810
Looking back now, I had grown up in a borderline
pretentious suburbia neighborhood, the type

02:07:07.810 --> 02:07:13.400
of community you'd see in movies like Donnie
Darko or American Beauty.

02:07:13.400 --> 02:07:17.470
Almost everyone in our neighborhood had decorations,
and those who didn't had these decorative

02:07:17.470 --> 02:07:20.680
wooden ghosts nailed to the side of their
mailbox.

02:07:20.680 --> 02:07:25.070
They were more of a cutesy decoration than
scary, but they did give a nice uniformity

02:07:25.070 --> 02:07:27.530
to all the houses in the neighborhood.

02:07:27.530 --> 02:07:30.910
It was starting to get dark when we reached
the house that our parents told us not to

02:07:30.910 --> 02:07:32.300
go to.

02:07:32.300 --> 02:07:36.730
This wasn't your stereotypical dark manor
at the end of the block, but it was a little

02:07:36.730 --> 02:07:40.920
further away from the street than many of
the other houses, and sort of tucked back

02:07:40.920 --> 02:07:42.650
behind some trees.

02:07:42.650 --> 02:07:47.040
I suggested that we go back to our house to
dump whatever candy we had off before hitting

02:07:47.040 --> 02:07:50.660
up another neighborhood,
but John and the others were curious to see

02:07:50.660 --> 02:07:53.130
what the big deal was about the dark house.

02:07:53.130 --> 02:07:57.920
I'll have to admit, I was quite curious about
why our parents didn't want us going over

02:07:57.920 --> 02:08:01.510
there,
and it did seem harmless enough, so I figured

02:08:01.510 --> 02:08:04.490
they would have no way of knowing if we quickly
hit this house.

02:08:04.490 --> 02:08:08.880
The driveway was long and dark, and there
was no light coming from the house whatsoever.

02:08:08.880 --> 02:08:12.620
This was one of those houses where the front
door was more on the side of the house,

02:08:12.620 --> 02:08:14.780
with a curved path leading back up to the
front.

02:08:14.780 --> 02:08:18.570
I noticed that this house did not have the
wood ghost nailed to the mailbox like every

02:08:18.570 --> 02:08:20.050
other house in the neighborhood.

02:08:20.050 --> 02:08:24.010
As we walked up, I was starting to get a little
nervous and I told John that I didn't think

02:08:24.010 --> 02:08:26.340
anyone was home,
but he thought I was just trying to chicken

02:08:26.340 --> 02:08:28.380
out and continued on anyways.

02:08:28.380 --> 02:08:31.530
We reached the house and John loudly banged
on the door.

02:08:31.530 --> 02:08:35.800
It was taking forever, and I was fairly convinced
that the guy wasn't home or didn't want to

02:08:35.800 --> 02:08:37.470
deal with trick-or-treaters.

02:08:37.470 --> 02:08:41.411
Just as I was ready to turn and give up on
the house, we all fell silent as the sound

02:08:41.411 --> 02:08:50.570
of footsteps could be heard on the other side
of the door.

02:08:50.570 --> 02:08:54.861
While this did make me nervous,
I was also excited to see what was on the

02:08:54.861 --> 02:08:58.490
other side of the door,
that made my parents so worried about this

02:08:58.490 --> 02:08:59.490
house.

02:08:59.490 --> 02:09:04.199
So I stepped back a little bit, giving myself
some room to run if need be.

02:09:04.199 --> 02:09:05.820
The door opened...

02:09:05.820 --> 02:09:06.820
revealing...

02:09:06.820 --> 02:09:09.030
an older man with a kane.

02:09:09.030 --> 02:09:14.050
This immediately alleviated some of my anxiety,
as it would be pretty easy to run if need

02:09:14.050 --> 02:09:15.050
be.

02:09:15.050 --> 02:09:18.630
The man was actually very nice and told us
that we were the first visitors of the night

02:09:18.630 --> 02:09:21.670
and that he didn't expect to see many trick-or-treaters
this year.

02:09:21.670 --> 02:09:26.130
Apparently, he lived alone and had had some
kind of dispute with the neighborhood homeowner's

02:09:26.130 --> 02:09:28.820
association over the upkeep of his property.

02:09:28.820 --> 02:09:32.670
So many of the adults were trying to get back
at him by excluding him from all the neighborhood

02:09:32.670 --> 02:09:33.670
festivities.

02:09:33.670 --> 02:09:37.670
He seemed like such a nice guy, and we actually
felt pretty bad for him.

02:09:37.670 --> 02:09:40.670
We all wished him a happy Halloween before
going on our way.

02:09:40.670 --> 02:09:44.150
I had felt silly about being nervous about
visiting this house...

02:09:44.150 --> 02:09:48.250
at least...
...that's how I felt before what happened

02:09:48.250 --> 02:09:50.260
next...

02:09:50.260 --> 02:09:53.320
As we walked down the path back to the street
side of the house,

02:09:53.320 --> 02:09:57.490
I happened to glance at the upstairs window,
and saw a man in a black hood peaking out

02:09:57.490 --> 02:09:59.920
from behind the window frame.

02:09:59.920 --> 02:10:05.030
As soon as I made eye contact with him, he
moved back out of sight.

02:10:05.030 --> 02:10:09.690
My stomach immediately dropped,
as the man had just said that he lived alone.

02:10:09.690 --> 02:10:13.101
I bolted as I told the guys to run,
but John and Evan seemed convinced that I

02:10:13.101 --> 02:10:14.101
was just being a baby.

02:10:14.101 --> 02:10:17.100
I tried to quickly tell them that there was
man in the window, but I don't think they

02:10:17.100 --> 02:10:18.100
believed me.

02:10:18.100 --> 02:10:23.030
However, John, being the older of the two
of us, was supposed to keep an eye on me,

02:10:23.030 --> 02:10:25.620
so when I made a mad dash back towards our
house,

02:10:25.620 --> 02:10:27.100
he effectively gave chase.

02:10:27.100 --> 02:10:31.530
I knew in the back of my mind that although
the old man may not have been mobile,

02:10:31.530 --> 02:10:35.760
that this other guy was most likely a fully
capable adult, who probably would be able

02:10:35.760 --> 02:10:40.190
to catch us,
so I didn't stop until I was inside the door.

02:10:40.190 --> 02:10:43.860
My parents had just returned from taking my
sister out for a round of the neighborhood,

02:10:43.860 --> 02:10:46.050
and they could immediately see that there
was something wrong.

02:10:46.050 --> 02:10:50.530
Not wanting to get in trouble for disobeying
them, I lied and told them that we were walking

02:10:50.530 --> 02:10:54.840
by the house when I saw a man in black climbing
through the window of the old man's house,

02:10:54.840 --> 02:10:57.450
and that he had seen us catching him in the
act.

02:10:57.450 --> 02:11:01.490
Apparently, this was a pretty good cover story,
as it was enough to get my Mom to call the

02:11:01.490 --> 02:11:03.740
cops and
and the four of us locked inside the house

02:11:03.740 --> 02:11:04.990
for the rest of the night.

02:11:04.990 --> 02:11:07.890
The other guys were pretty bummed out to have
our trick-or-treating cut short,

02:11:07.890 --> 02:11:12.450
and we decided we'd watch a movie and begin
trade negotiations on our candy a little early

02:11:12.450 --> 02:11:13.450
this year.

02:11:13.450 --> 02:11:17.200
I had a hard time paying attention to the
movie, and kept looking back to the window

02:11:17.200 --> 02:11:20.820
thinking about what the possibility might
be that the guy tracked us here.

02:11:20.820 --> 02:11:23.990
Not much later that night,
we learned that the police had searched the

02:11:23.990 --> 02:11:29.190
old man's house, and found a 19 year old man
hiding in the closet with a knife.

02:11:29.190 --> 02:11:33.780
Apparently, the intruder had no idea who lived
there, and decided to break in after seeing

02:11:33.780 --> 02:11:37.560
that the house was completely dark and
being avoided by trick-or-treaters on Halloween

02:11:37.560 --> 02:11:38.590
night.

02:11:38.590 --> 02:11:40.400
The old man was also unharmed.

02:11:40.400 --> 02:11:46.050
But years later I still shudder to think about
what could have gone down that night.

02:11:46.050 --> 02:11:50.610
What if I had seen the intruder on the way
up to the house before learning that the old

02:11:50.610 --> 02:11:51.610
man lived alone?

02:11:51.610 --> 02:11:56.190
What if the intruder had been on the first
floor and decided to give chase to us?

02:11:56.190 --> 02:12:00.920
But what chills me the most...
is what would have happened to that nice old

02:12:00.920 --> 02:12:10.530
man,
if we had never trick-or-treated at his house?

02:12:10.530 --> 02:12:12.691
Number 17 - Secret Santa

02:12:12.691 --> 02:12:19.150
For the last couple of years, my wife and
I have hosted a Secret Santa gift exchange

02:12:19.150 --> 02:12:20.220
during the holidays.

02:12:20.220 --> 02:12:24.620
It’s a fairly new tradition, but we thought
it was nice to put together since us and a

02:12:24.620 --> 02:12:27.500
lot of our friends can’t really afford to
buy gifts for everyone.

02:12:27.500 --> 02:12:31.700
We do it a little bit differently than some
people might be accustomed to.

02:12:31.700 --> 02:12:35.980
Everyone randomly gets a name and has to buy
that person a gift around $50.

02:12:35.980 --> 02:12:40.720
We have one get together where everyone opens
their gifts, but even after the swap, you

02:12:40.720 --> 02:12:42.930
never find out who gave you the gift.

02:12:42.930 --> 02:12:45.720
My wife and I agreed that part is important.

02:12:45.720 --> 02:12:50.620
She says that what makes the holiday special
is having good faith in all our friends to

02:12:50.620 --> 02:12:52.430
get the person something good.

02:12:52.430 --> 02:12:56.580
In other words, if you’re only buying a
gift in order to get recognition for it, than

02:12:56.580 --> 02:12:58.820
the whole idea is kind of cheapened.

02:12:58.820 --> 02:12:59.820
Besides.

02:12:59.820 --> 02:13:00.880
These are our friends.

02:13:00.880 --> 02:13:03.600
If you can’t trust them, then who can you
trust?

02:13:03.600 --> 02:13:08.990
Sure, there are exceptions where it’s obvious
who gave the gift; like last year when our

02:13:08.990 --> 02:13:13.180
friends Emily and Alaina, who are married,
ended up getting each other.

02:13:13.180 --> 02:13:18.970
Or… also last year; when Cynthia received
a cheap ice tray as her gift from her recently

02:13:18.970 --> 02:13:20.200
ex-boyfriend, Marc.

02:13:20.200 --> 02:13:25.550
We were optimistic that this year would be
filled with positivity… which it was…

02:13:25.550 --> 02:13:26.900
to a point anyway.

02:13:26.900 --> 02:13:31.400
We have a secret santa app that automatically
emails everyone involved and tells them who

02:13:31.400 --> 02:13:32.400
they got.

02:13:32.400 --> 02:13:37.150
It’s great, because it allows us as the
organizers to not get our Secret Santas spoiled.

02:13:37.150 --> 02:13:40.510
I got Troy, the newest addition to our party
this year.

02:13:40.510 --> 02:13:43.030
I think I got the perfect gift for him too.

02:13:43.030 --> 02:13:46.730
Every time I go over to his apartment, there’s
stuff everywhere.

02:13:46.730 --> 02:13:48.370
Plates, silverware, Blu-Rays…

02:13:48.370 --> 02:13:53.280
It’s not like he’s just too lazy to clean
up after himself, it just seems like he doesn’t

02:13:53.280 --> 02:13:54.950
have anywhere to put it all.

02:13:54.950 --> 02:13:59.110
So I got him one of those knife blocks, a
dishrack and a silverware organizer.

02:13:59.110 --> 02:14:02.310
That will just cover the kitchen, but it’s
a start.

02:14:02.310 --> 02:14:05.250
I had a feeling Troy was going to appreciate
it.

02:14:05.250 --> 02:14:07.380
The day of the gift exchange arrived.

02:14:07.380 --> 02:14:10.450
We had people drop off gifts in a pile as
they came in.

02:14:10.450 --> 02:14:14.480
We all enjoyed some drinks and snacks as we
caught up with each other for a couple hours

02:14:14.480 --> 02:14:16.120
before getting to down to it.

02:14:16.120 --> 02:14:20.710
By the time we started to open the gifts,
everyone was getting a bit…

02:14:20.710 --> 02:14:21.710
giggly.

02:14:21.710 --> 02:14:25.950
My wife pointed out that Troy seemed to have
taken an interest in her friend Cynthia, which

02:14:25.950 --> 02:14:29.520
we could both get behind since they were the
only two there who were still single.

02:14:29.520 --> 02:14:31.950
It seemed like the party was alive and well.

02:14:31.950 --> 02:14:35.930
Most of the gifts were really good too, and
people kept up their poker faces as far as

02:14:35.930 --> 02:14:38.310
I could tell when the present they brought
was being opened.

02:14:38.310 --> 02:14:44.150
Of course, there were a couple obvious ones,
like our friend James who most likely got

02:14:44.150 --> 02:14:48.730
his own wife, seeing as how she didn’t know
how anyone else would have known what she

02:14:48.730 --> 02:14:49.730
wanted this year.

02:14:49.730 --> 02:14:52.570
Marco actually ended up getting two presents
somehow.

02:14:52.570 --> 02:14:54.010
I couldn’t figure out why.

02:14:54.010 --> 02:14:58.000
I was worried that the app had messed up and
someone was going to end up with no presents,

02:14:58.000 --> 02:15:02.400
but I did a quick count and realized there
were 11 total presents for the 10 of us.

02:15:02.400 --> 02:15:06.980
I guess someone just wanted to make Marco’s
day and get him something in addition to buying

02:15:06.980 --> 02:15:08.990
something for their person.

02:15:08.990 --> 02:15:13.650
He ended up loving both presents, so it seemed
like no harm done for the most part, though

02:15:13.650 --> 02:15:16.070
I just worried it was a bit unfair to everyone
else.

02:15:16.070 --> 02:15:19.810
The final present remaining came down to my
wife.

02:15:19.810 --> 02:15:24.610
It was a little black box wrapped in… what
looked to be just a plastic trash bag and

02:15:24.610 --> 02:15:27.310
tied up in actual rope.

02:15:27.310 --> 02:15:28.310
It was…

02:15:28.310 --> 02:15:33.240
I’m not going to lie, a really ugly exterior,
and she had a lot of trouble opening it by

02:15:33.240 --> 02:15:34.240
herself.

02:15:34.240 --> 02:15:38.250
In fact, nobody could seem to pry the knot
off of it, granted we were all kind of drunk

02:15:38.250 --> 02:15:41.420
at that point, so we ended up having to cut
the thing open.

02:15:41.420 --> 02:15:45.150
She opened the box… and pulled out a small
piece of paper.

02:15:45.150 --> 02:15:47.710
She looked upset as she read it.

02:15:47.710 --> 02:15:51.690
Then her hands started to shake and her eyes
glazed over.

02:15:51.690 --> 02:15:53.730
“What is it?”

02:15:53.730 --> 02:15:54.920
She showed me the slip of paper.

02:15:54.920 --> 02:15:57.100
There were just a couple of words on it.

02:15:57.100 --> 02:16:01.010
“Santa says… you all die.”

02:16:01.010 --> 02:16:04.380
I quickly looked inside the box, only to find,
there was nothing else inside.

02:16:04.380 --> 02:16:09.330
I can get kind of defensive at times and I
got pretty upset and took it out on everyone.

02:16:09.330 --> 02:16:13.280
Within a couple minutes the party was over
and everyone was out in the cold.

02:16:13.280 --> 02:16:17.030
I wanted to get to the bottom of who the hell
thought this would be funny by asking everyone

02:16:17.030 --> 02:16:21.470
who who their secret santa was and doing a
little research of my own to find out who

02:16:21.470 --> 02:16:27.200
was lying, but she insisted that it wasn’t
that big of a deal and she’d rather not

02:16:27.200 --> 02:16:28.520
ruin it for everyone.

02:16:28.520 --> 02:16:29.980
Still, I felt really betrayed.

02:16:29.980 --> 02:16:33.841
These were supposed to be our friends, and
I couldn’t understand who would want to

02:16:33.841 --> 02:16:35.260
hurt her like that.

02:16:35.260 --> 02:16:39.260
But we were tired and just decided to retire
to bed for the evening.

02:16:39.260 --> 02:16:43.510
I told myself I would get her something great
to make up for it and started brainstorming

02:16:43.510 --> 02:16:45.050
some gift ideas.

02:16:45.050 --> 02:16:48.700
But all I could think about was… who would
do this?

02:16:48.700 --> 02:16:52.841
I stayed awake for a while longer trying to
think of any reason that someone would have

02:16:52.841 --> 02:16:54.390
to try to spook us.

02:16:54.390 --> 02:16:56.429
That’s when I heard…

02:16:56.429 --> 02:16:58.150
someone rummaging around the house.

02:16:58.150 --> 02:17:04.430
A chill went up my spine and after being frozen
in fear for a few moments, I sat up and began

02:17:04.430 --> 02:17:06.010
to formulate a plan.

02:17:06.010 --> 02:17:08.610
My wife woke up and asked me what I was doing.

02:17:08.610 --> 02:17:10.440
“There’s someone in the house.

02:17:10.440 --> 02:17:13.320
Stay here keep the door locked until I give
you the OK.”

02:17:13.320 --> 02:17:16.120
With that, I slipped out and locked the door
behind me.

02:17:16.120 --> 02:17:18.510
My blood was boiling at this point.

02:17:18.510 --> 02:17:22.219
I didn’t know if this had anything to do
with the present from earlier but all I wanted

02:17:22.219 --> 02:17:25.550
to do was find who was behind this and bash
his head in.

02:17:25.550 --> 02:17:27.050
The only issue was…

02:17:27.050 --> 02:17:29.599
I couldn’t hear anyone moving around anymore…

02:17:29.599 --> 02:17:33.679
It seemed that the house was quiet.

02:17:33.679 --> 02:17:35.950
I methodically checked the entire upstairs.

02:17:35.950 --> 02:17:37.130
It was empty.

02:17:37.130 --> 02:17:40.760
As I was checking the last closet, I heard
a huge crash from downstairs.

02:17:40.760 --> 02:17:45.980
I sprinted down, fists blazing, but the scene
I found in the living room was far more horrifying

02:17:45.980 --> 02:17:47.200
than I could have imagined.

02:17:47.200 --> 02:17:52.969
The tree had been knocked over into the fireplace
which was now on and it had begun to burn.

02:17:52.969 --> 02:17:56.639
I heard footsteps running to the door, but
I knew I couldn’t go after him now.

02:17:56.639 --> 02:18:00.760
In a panic, I turned off the gas fireplace
and ran to the kitchen to grab a jug of water.

02:18:00.760 --> 02:18:04.580
I poured it over the tree which was beginning
to burn even more, but all I could manage

02:18:04.580 --> 02:18:07.099
to do was slow down the rapidly spreading
fire.

02:18:07.099 --> 02:18:11.750
Luckily my wife had already called 9-1-1 and
the fire department showed up before long.

02:18:11.750 --> 02:18:14.620
I was able to slow down the fire enough until
they arrived.

02:18:14.620 --> 02:18:18.290
I wish I could say that was the end of it.

02:18:18.290 --> 02:18:20.300
But it gets worse from there.

02:18:20.300 --> 02:18:23.940
The police showed up and questioned us about
what had gone down that evening.

02:18:23.940 --> 02:18:29.050
We told the entire story, and they were particularly
interested in the app we had used to sort

02:18:29.050 --> 02:18:30.920
the names for the secret santa.

02:18:30.920 --> 02:18:34.840
The chief told us that an undercover police
officer would be on our block for the time

02:18:34.840 --> 02:18:38.219
being, and to call 9-1-1 if we had any other
disturbances.

02:18:38.219 --> 02:18:43.000
He also gave me a card, a point of contact
for if we had any other information.

02:18:43.000 --> 02:18:47.429
It was nearly 4AM at that point, and we were
ready to put this nightmarish evening behind

02:18:47.429 --> 02:18:51.940
us when I got a call from Terry, James’s
wife.

02:18:51.940 --> 02:18:55.679
They were both at the secret Santa that night
and I noticed a couple of missed calls from

02:18:55.679 --> 02:18:57.080
from her as well.

02:18:57.080 --> 02:19:00.740
Desperate for more information, I picked up,
but before I could explain the mess that we

02:19:00.740 --> 02:19:05.179
had been in, she explained that she was calling
from the hospital.

02:19:05.179 --> 02:19:08.870
Apparently they had been driving home from
our house when some maniac ran them off the

02:19:08.870 --> 02:19:09.870
road!

02:19:09.870 --> 02:19:14.150
She was fine, but went on to explain that
James had been injured pretty badly, though

02:19:14.150 --> 02:19:16.230
he was expected to make a recovery.

02:19:16.230 --> 02:19:18.550
I decided that enough was enough.

02:19:18.550 --> 02:19:21.519
It was time to do a little investigation of
my own.

02:19:21.519 --> 02:19:25.960
The next morning I headed out to the spot
of the crash, as Terry had described to me.

02:19:25.960 --> 02:19:28.960
If I was going to get to the bottom of this,
I had to be thorough.

02:19:28.960 --> 02:19:33.400
Afterall, as far as I knew Terry was trying
to cover up her or James’s guilt with that

02:19:33.400 --> 02:19:34.500
phone call.

02:19:34.500 --> 02:19:38.540
I found tire tracks going off the road, but
that really only clears one of them.

02:19:38.540 --> 02:19:40.639
I made a call on over to the hospital.

02:19:40.639 --> 02:19:44.190
I knew they wouldn’t share any information,
since that’s someone’s private medical

02:19:44.190 --> 02:19:48.650
info, but I acted like a concerned family
member and asked if they’d been found.

02:19:48.650 --> 02:19:53.410
I was able to find out they both got admitted
at the same time, so they were both in the

02:19:53.410 --> 02:19:54.410
clear.

02:19:54.410 --> 02:19:58.350
My next step was finding out who they got
gifts for in the secret santa, which involved

02:19:58.350 --> 02:20:01.011
me showing up and asking to see the email.

02:20:01.011 --> 02:20:04.830
I had to catch them by surprise to make sure
they didn’t try to doctor anything.

02:20:04.830 --> 02:20:07.990
So I knew I had Troy and my wife had Emily.

02:20:07.990 --> 02:20:13.180
It was already fairly obvious that James had
his wife Terry, but I did find out that Terry

02:20:13.180 --> 02:20:14.180
had Alaina.

02:20:14.180 --> 02:20:18.510
Don’t worry about keeping track of all the
names, just know that my list of suspects

02:20:18.510 --> 02:20:19.800
was narrowing.

02:20:19.800 --> 02:20:24.060
I also discovered that the person who went
after them was in a white van with black tape

02:20:24.060 --> 02:20:25.920
over the license plate.

02:20:25.920 --> 02:20:28.220
Next on my list were Emily and Alaina.

02:20:28.220 --> 02:20:32.320
It took me a while to come up with an idea
about how I might prove their whereabouts,

02:20:32.320 --> 02:20:35.780
but I ended up finding a way to check on them
without either of them knowing.

02:20:35.780 --> 02:20:40.310
See, every year there’s this big Christmas
tree in town square.

02:20:40.310 --> 02:20:43.600
Everyone in the town is encouraged to put
up an ornament of their own, and the whole

02:20:43.600 --> 02:20:46.550
thing is livestreamed for the entire month
of December.

02:20:46.550 --> 02:20:48.931
They would most certainly go past it on their
way home.

02:20:48.931 --> 02:20:52.780
All I had to do was go back to last night
around the time they should have been driving

02:20:52.780 --> 02:20:53.780
home.

02:20:53.780 --> 02:20:57.470
Luckily enough, I was able to spot their car
on the stream.

02:20:57.470 --> 02:21:01.441
While that didn't necessarily clear both of
them from what happened at our house, it did

02:21:01.441 --> 02:21:04.490
make them innocent of running James and Terry
off the road.

02:21:04.490 --> 02:21:08.810
Unless they had just gotten a second car that
I don't know about, but I figured I could

02:21:08.810 --> 02:21:11.540
reevaluate them if that came to be the case.

02:21:11.540 --> 02:21:15.680
I also had to make the assumption that the
intruder at our house and the crazy driver

02:21:15.680 --> 02:21:20.400
that went after our friends were related incidents,
and the time frame of the events seemed to

02:21:20.400 --> 02:21:21.970
line up with that theory.

02:21:21.970 --> 02:21:26.130
Of course, the nasty present my wife received
only backed this idea up further.

02:21:26.130 --> 02:21:30.130
I tried getting ahold of Emily and Alaina
to see who they got gifts for, but neither

02:21:30.130 --> 02:21:31.931
one could be reached.

02:21:31.931 --> 02:21:35.110
The next and final couple was Marco and Gina.

02:21:35.110 --> 02:21:39.360
They’d taken an Uber home from the party,
so all I had to do was show up and ask to

02:21:39.360 --> 02:21:40.960
see their ride history.

02:21:40.960 --> 02:21:45.770
When I arrived Marco was actually kind of
upset that I was accusing them.

02:21:45.770 --> 02:21:47.970
I thought to myself, this was it.

02:21:47.970 --> 02:21:49.170
It must be one of them.

02:21:49.170 --> 02:21:53.660
But I hadn’t really planned for what I would
do if I’d gotten this far.

02:21:53.660 --> 02:21:56.130
I didn’t bring anything to defend myself
with.

02:21:56.130 --> 02:21:58.931
Not only was Macro a big guy, but it was 2
against one.

02:21:58.931 --> 02:22:04.550
I clenched my fists behind my back and slowly
stepped away as Marco yelled at me, going

02:22:04.550 --> 02:22:09.010
on about how he was appalled that I didn’t
trust him after everything we’d been through.

02:22:09.010 --> 02:22:12.380
I figured that my best bet was to turn and
run for my car.

02:22:12.380 --> 02:22:15.030
Then I could hopefully make a getaway and
alert the police.

02:22:15.030 --> 02:22:19.471
Tension within me built as I waited for him
to make a move.

02:22:19.471 --> 02:22:24.160
Just when I was ready to turn and run, Gina
came up with the phone to her ear and said

02:22:24.160 --> 02:22:27.800
that Terry was on the line, and she had just
found out about the car crash.

02:22:27.800 --> 02:22:33.710
She invited me in to show me the evidence
I was looking for, and stupidly, I accepted.

02:22:33.710 --> 02:22:37.890
For all I knew, this could have been an act
to lure me in and make me more vulnerable.

02:22:37.890 --> 02:22:43.400
Still, when Gina delivered the news, I thought
I saw something change in Marco’s expression.

02:22:43.400 --> 02:22:45.830
Like an understanding had come over him.

02:22:45.830 --> 02:22:49.760
Like he realized now why I had to see their
whereabouts last night.

02:22:49.760 --> 02:22:54.030
Still I was jumpy inside of their house and
in my mind I was keeping track of where they

02:22:54.030 --> 02:22:58.860
both were at all times for my own safety,
though I tried not to show it.

02:22:58.860 --> 02:23:03.500
Marco brought up their trip history on Uber
and… to my surprise, they had gone home

02:23:03.500 --> 02:23:05.480
after the party, no doubt about it.

02:23:05.480 --> 02:23:10.210
They also showed me who their secret santa
recipients were: Marco’s was Cynthia and

02:23:10.210 --> 02:23:11.210
Gina’s was James.

02:23:11.210 --> 02:23:15.990
I told them I had to be on my way and headed
out, where a van was pulling up to the curb

02:23:15.990 --> 02:23:16.990
by their house.

02:23:16.990 --> 02:23:20.930
As soon as I looked up at it, it haphazardly
sped away down the street.

02:23:20.930 --> 02:23:25.620
I ran after it and found that the license
plate was covered with black tape, it was

02:23:25.620 --> 02:23:27.550
just like what Terry had described to me.

02:23:27.550 --> 02:23:30.220
I dialed 9-1-1 and let them know what had
just happened.

02:23:30.220 --> 02:23:33.550
He was still going after people, so I knew
I was racing the clock here.

02:23:33.550 --> 02:23:38.320
There were only two suspects left: Troy and
Cynthia, the two singles who had been flirting

02:23:38.320 --> 02:23:39.480
at the party.

02:23:39.480 --> 02:23:44.751
I hoped to God it wasn’t Troy after I had
put so much into my gift for him, but deep

02:23:44.751 --> 02:23:47.351
down I knew it was.

02:23:47.351 --> 02:23:50.320
The nature of the crime at my house pointed
to it being a male.

02:23:50.320 --> 02:23:55.010
Still, I touched base with my wife and told
her to look into Cynthia while I confronted

02:23:55.010 --> 02:23:56.180
him.

02:23:56.180 --> 02:23:58.610
Everything was boiling down to this.

02:23:58.610 --> 02:24:02.561
Troy lived alone so I wouldn’t be able to
get any info from anyone else.

02:24:02.561 --> 02:24:06.900
He did live in an apartment complex however,
so there had to be a camera somewhere that

02:24:06.900 --> 02:24:10.160
would prove he was out several hours later
after the party ended.

02:24:10.160 --> 02:24:14.420
I gave the police chief a call and he agreed
to send someone to meet me at Troy’s apartment

02:24:14.420 --> 02:24:15.580
complex with a warrant.

02:24:15.580 --> 02:24:17.570
I waited out by the office.

02:24:17.570 --> 02:24:19.221
This was our chance to nail him.

02:24:19.221 --> 02:24:20.931
What was it taking them so long?

02:24:20.931 --> 02:24:22.220
As I waited around…

02:24:22.220 --> 02:24:24.240
I heard a familiar voice.

02:24:24.240 --> 02:24:25.680
It was Troy.

02:24:25.680 --> 02:24:26.680
I was so stupid.

02:24:26.680 --> 02:24:30.170
Of course he'd come back here after nearly
getting caught back at Marco’s.

02:24:30.170 --> 02:24:32.030
This was not good.

02:24:32.030 --> 02:24:33.351
He knew I knew.

02:24:33.351 --> 02:24:35.870
But he didn't let onto it right away.

02:24:35.870 --> 02:24:38.221
Well, two can play at that game.

02:24:38.221 --> 02:24:40.101
My only choice was to play dumb.

02:24:40.101 --> 02:24:42.460
He pretended to be surprised to see me.

02:24:42.460 --> 02:24:44.650
He always did have a good poker face.

02:24:44.650 --> 02:24:48.830
I told him that I had come to check on him
when I heard about James and Terry.

02:24:48.830 --> 02:24:52.690
He told me he had just heard this morning
and went over to the hospital to visit James.

02:24:52.690 --> 02:24:55.320
He was finally telling me something I could
believe.

02:24:55.320 --> 02:24:56.760
A good move on his part.

02:24:56.760 --> 02:24:59.540
It would definitely make them less suspicious
of him.

02:24:59.540 --> 02:25:01.300
But that wouldn't work on me.

02:25:01.300 --> 02:25:03.050
I'd caught him red handed.

02:25:03.050 --> 02:25:05.770
But he knew I knew too much.

02:25:05.770 --> 02:25:06.771
What was his plan?

02:25:06.771 --> 02:25:08.980
How long was he going to play dumb?

02:25:08.980 --> 02:25:11.771
All I had to do was stall a little bit longer.

02:25:11.771 --> 02:25:13.580
I decided to press him on it.

02:25:13.580 --> 02:25:17.530
I asked if anything weird had happened after
he had left the night before.

02:25:17.530 --> 02:25:21.500
I was hoping to trip him up with an inconsistency
in his story.

02:25:21.500 --> 02:25:24.480
Something that didn't line up with the actual
timeline of events.

02:25:24.480 --> 02:25:28.061
All I got out of him though, was that he had
gone straight home.

02:25:28.061 --> 02:25:30.880
He asked what I had done after everyone had
left.

02:25:30.880 --> 02:25:35.230
And it was at that moment that something clicked
in my head.

02:25:35.230 --> 02:25:37.891
He was going to try paint me as the villain.

02:25:37.891 --> 02:25:42.490
He knew we would be home and asleep after
the party, so we would have no alibi to prove

02:25:42.490 --> 02:25:46.950
that we hadn't gone and run down James’s
car before coming back to set our own Christmas

02:25:46.950 --> 02:25:50.970
tree ablaze in an attempt to make ourselves
look like victims.

02:25:50.970 --> 02:25:52.820
After all, we'd setup the party.

02:25:52.820 --> 02:25:57.240
We could have structured it so that my wife
would receive the creepy note… from me.

02:25:57.240 --> 02:25:59.140
He was going to try to pin it all on me.

02:25:59.140 --> 02:26:01.960
But I was one step ahead of him.

02:26:01.960 --> 02:26:04.680
The detective arrived.

02:26:04.680 --> 02:26:10.170
I told Troy he was busted, but I knew it would
be a battle to prove my own innocence as well.

02:26:10.170 --> 02:26:12.010
He continued to play dumb.

02:26:12.010 --> 02:26:16.200
The detective provided the apartment complex
with a warrant and we all sat down to watch

02:26:16.200 --> 02:26:17.270
the footage.

02:26:17.270 --> 02:26:20.500
This next part, I deeply regret.

02:26:20.500 --> 02:26:26.190
I'll never be able to erase that look of betrayal
out of my mind.

02:26:26.190 --> 02:26:30.570
Because the footage proved that Troy was innocent.

02:26:30.570 --> 02:26:36.811
I wish I had more time to apologise for accusing
him, but I had to go check on my wife.

02:26:36.811 --> 02:26:40.010
All signs now pointed to Cynthia being the
culprit.

02:26:40.010 --> 02:26:44.620
I rushed home where my wife informed me she
had just gotten off the phone with Cynthia’s

02:26:44.620 --> 02:26:45.620
roommate.

02:26:45.620 --> 02:26:47.710
Cynthia was also innocent.

02:26:47.710 --> 02:26:49.511
This didn't make any sense.

02:26:49.511 --> 02:26:51.450
We'd cleared everyone who was at the party.

02:26:51.450 --> 02:26:53.051
Had we overlooked someone?

02:26:53.051 --> 02:26:54.480
Was it somebody else?

02:26:54.480 --> 02:26:56.120
Outside of the group?

02:26:56.120 --> 02:26:58.570
We soon got our answer.

02:26:58.570 --> 02:27:01.561
If you're easily disturbed, I suggest you
don't continue.

02:27:01.561 --> 02:27:04.500
We got another call from the police chief.

02:27:04.500 --> 02:27:08.880
Emily and Alaina were dead.

02:27:08.880 --> 02:27:13.690
Somebody had broken down their door and slit
both of their throats, leaving them to bleed

02:27:13.690 --> 02:27:15.110
out under the Christmas tree.

02:27:15.110 --> 02:27:19.940
The killer had also slathered a message on
the carpet in blood.

02:27:19.940 --> 02:27:24.270
It read, “lesbo cunts” with arrows pointed
up at them.

02:27:24.270 --> 02:27:27.641
I was sickened just by hearing about this.

02:27:27.641 --> 02:27:32.439
But the police had a strong lead on who the
killer might be.

02:27:32.439 --> 02:27:33.439
Marc Berklee.

02:27:33.439 --> 02:27:37.420
Cynthia’s ex from last year's secret santa.

02:27:37.420 --> 02:27:41.740
The a-hole who got her an ice tray for a gift.

02:27:41.740 --> 02:27:45.900
Apparently, one of the first things the detective
on our case did was contact the developer

02:27:45.900 --> 02:27:47.590
of the secret santa app.

02:27:47.590 --> 02:27:50.310
He was given a master list of everyone involved.

02:27:50.310 --> 02:27:54.640
I guess we never removed Marc from the list
when we added Troy this year and the app told

02:27:54.640 --> 02:27:56.100
Troy to get a present for Marc.

02:27:56.100 --> 02:28:00.790
Troy must have thought it supposed to be Marco,
seeing as how he would have no idea who Marc

02:28:00.790 --> 02:28:01.840
even is.

02:28:01.840 --> 02:28:05.310
That would also explain why Marco ended up
with two gifts.

02:28:05.310 --> 02:28:09.660
Then Marc must have snuck in at some point
and dropped my wife’s gift into the pile.

02:28:09.660 --> 02:28:12.380
It was all starting to come together.

02:28:12.380 --> 02:28:16.880
We also found out that Marc completely lost
his mind when Cynthia had broken up with him

02:28:16.880 --> 02:28:18.560
a little over a year ago.

02:28:18.560 --> 02:28:23.601
There were multiple police reports of him
threatening her, stalking her and loitering

02:28:23.601 --> 02:28:24.851
outside of her apartment.

02:28:24.851 --> 02:28:28.670
Maybe when Marc accidentally got the email
about our secret santa that somehow set him

02:28:28.670 --> 02:28:31.810
off again and he decided to terrorize all
of us.

02:28:31.810 --> 02:28:33.470
Everyone still in her life.

02:28:33.470 --> 02:28:37.270
Everyone who is as close to her as he wishes
he could be.

02:28:37.270 --> 02:28:41.430
The chief told me he had already sent his
squad over to Cynthia’s, as Marc would likely

02:28:41.430 --> 02:28:45.380
be heading there next after having hit every
other couple at the party.

02:28:45.380 --> 02:28:47.430
But I knew that wouldn't be the case.

02:28:47.430 --> 02:28:50.710
If Marc really had snuck into my party to
deliver the fake gift, he'd have seen what

02:28:50.710 --> 02:28:54.381
went on between Cynthia and Troy and he'd
be in a furious rage.

02:28:54.381 --> 02:29:01.150
He was saving his best, most brutal and cold-blooded
strike for last and Cynthia was never on his

02:29:01.150 --> 02:29:02.150
hit list.

02:29:02.150 --> 02:29:06.080
I raced over to Troy’s as quickly as I could,
but feared I may be too late when I arrived

02:29:06.080 --> 02:29:08.800
to find his front door had been left wide
open.

02:29:08.800 --> 02:29:10.930
I walked inside.

02:29:10.930 --> 02:29:12.840
It seemed…

02:29:12.840 --> 02:29:14.120
strangely empty.

02:29:14.120 --> 02:29:15.920
My heart sank.

02:29:15.920 --> 02:29:17.261
Was I too late?

02:29:17.261 --> 02:29:20.590
Or was Troy even home when Marc had arrived?

02:29:20.590 --> 02:29:21.970
I called out.

02:29:21.970 --> 02:29:23.060
“Troy?”

02:29:23.060 --> 02:29:25.250
No response.

02:29:25.250 --> 02:29:26.340
“Marc?”

02:29:26.340 --> 02:29:30.330
I headed into the kitchen where I saw that
the dish rack and silverware organizer I'd

02:29:30.330 --> 02:29:32.720
gotten him had been put to good use.

02:29:32.720 --> 02:29:35.910
He'd finally tidied his crazy mess of stuff.

02:29:35.910 --> 02:29:39.420
For that little moment I was glad I was able
to get him something worthwhile.

02:29:39.420 --> 02:29:41.630
But then it happened.

02:29:41.630 --> 02:29:43.600
I never heard it coming.

02:29:43.600 --> 02:29:47.000
But I did see a shadow come over me as I noticed
the other gift I had gotten Troy.

02:29:47.000 --> 02:29:48.000
The knife block.

02:29:48.000 --> 02:29:55.510
But… one of knives was missing.

02:29:55.510 --> 02:29:59.300
Number 18 - Blind Date

02:29:59.300 --> 02:30:03.600
I'd always found the concept of a blind date
to be somewhat of a gamble.

02:30:03.600 --> 02:30:09.320
At best, it could lead to a very fun time,
and who knows, maybe even something more.

02:30:09.320 --> 02:30:14.470
But you run the risk of a terrible and awkward
hour or more, and you never know what you

02:30:14.470 --> 02:30:15.470
might get.

02:30:15.470 --> 02:30:19.990
Tara and I exchanged names and phone numbers
online, then decided only to text each other

02:30:19.990 --> 02:30:23.950
before the date in order to preserve the blind
aspect of the encounter.

02:30:23.950 --> 02:30:28.130
I arrived at the restaurant a few minutes
early to find that she was already there.

02:30:28.130 --> 02:30:30.590
We quickly got a table and sat down.

02:30:30.590 --> 02:30:34.680
After our initial introductions, one of the
first things she did was suggest that we both

02:30:34.680 --> 02:30:37.060
turn off our phones for the remainder of the
date.

02:30:37.060 --> 02:30:41.850
While I was surprised at her progressive request,
I quickly agreed and powered down my device.

02:30:41.850 --> 02:30:45.480
I had been on all too many bad dates where
the girl had fallen back on looking at her

02:30:45.480 --> 02:30:47.450
phone at the first hint of an awkward moment.

02:30:47.450 --> 02:30:52.041
I mean, I've been guilty of it too, so I figured
we may as well at least attempt to get to

02:30:52.041 --> 02:30:54.920
know each other now that we had taken the
time to arrange a date.

02:30:54.920 --> 02:30:56.561
We started with the small talk.

02:30:56.561 --> 02:30:59.480
The city, our jobs, the obligatory stuff.

02:30:59.480 --> 02:31:02.870
Then she started to ask some weird questions.

02:31:02.870 --> 02:31:06.230
Questions like: Have you ever thought about
murdering someone?

02:31:06.230 --> 02:31:09.061
I told her, we all have at some point… right?

02:31:09.061 --> 02:31:11.970
In a joking manner of course.

02:31:11.970 --> 02:31:15.620
She went on about how planning the perfect
murder in her head was kind of a fun hobby

02:31:15.620 --> 02:31:16.820
of hers.

02:31:16.820 --> 02:31:21.510
When she asked me how I would do it, I explained
that I kind of like the Alfred Hitchcock idea

02:31:21.510 --> 02:31:23.590
of stabbing someone with an icicle.

02:31:23.590 --> 02:31:26.440
I wasn't really sure what to think when I
heard what she said next.

02:31:26.440 --> 02:31:32.320
She told me, if you do it right, you've got
no reason to make the evidence disappear."

02:31:32.320 --> 02:31:35.870
Of course, I was curious as to where she was
going with this.

02:31:35.870 --> 02:31:39.210
"These detectives always look for a motive,”
she explained.

02:31:39.210 --> 02:31:48.480
“So you simply have to have no reason to
be there, no connection to the person, and

02:31:48.480 --> 02:31:52.050
of course, no witnesses."

02:31:52.050 --> 02:31:57.510
While it would be easy to get away with something
like that, I did have to wonder why would

02:31:57.510 --> 02:31:59.640
you want to kill a random person?"

02:31:59.640 --> 02:32:02.391
She just said that she finds it kind of exciting.

02:32:02.391 --> 02:32:05.381
It's not that I didn't realize this conversation
was weird…

02:32:05.381 --> 02:32:08.721
Normally, I wouldn't find myself talking about
such things with a girl...

02:32:08.721 --> 02:32:10.910
Nonetheless on the first date.

02:32:10.910 --> 02:32:14.420
But, for whatever reason, I didn't really
mind discussing it with her.

02:32:14.420 --> 02:32:16.971
I even found it kind of fun.

02:32:16.971 --> 02:32:18.680
At the end of the date I picked up the bill.

02:32:18.680 --> 02:32:21.340
And she asked if I had any plans for the rest
of the night.

02:32:21.340 --> 02:32:26.420
Taking the hint, I invited her back to my
place, and before long, we were off.

02:32:26.420 --> 02:32:31.640
Upon arriving home I stepped into the bathroom
to freshen up and brush my teeth, just in

02:32:31.640 --> 02:32:32.640
case.

02:32:32.640 --> 02:32:35.730
While I was in there, I turned my phone back
on to see if I had missed any messages while

02:32:35.730 --> 02:32:36.820
I was out on the date.

02:32:36.820 --> 02:32:40.820
Tara was waiting for me out in the living
room, so I tried to be quick.

02:32:40.820 --> 02:32:43.400
I noticed just one message on my phone.

02:32:43.400 --> 02:32:45.360
It was from Tara.

02:32:45.360 --> 02:32:46.980
Thirty minutes ago.

02:32:46.980 --> 02:32:48.350
That's odd.

02:32:48.350 --> 02:32:51.380
We hadn't even left the restaurant thirty
minutes ago.

02:32:51.380 --> 02:32:53.380
Both of our phones were off at the time.

02:32:53.380 --> 02:32:54.720
I opened the message.

02:32:54.720 --> 02:32:55.720
“Hey.

02:32:55.720 --> 02:32:57.210
I'm SO sorry I didn't make it.

02:32:57.210 --> 02:32:58.351
Someone slashed my tires.

02:32:58.351 --> 02:33:02.690
I tried calling but your phone was dead.

02:33:02.690 --> 02:33:08.260
Did you still want to try to meet up?”

02:33:08.260 --> 02:33:13.180
As I tried to comprehend what I had just read,
I heard her doing something out in the kitchen.

02:33:13.180 --> 02:33:15.550
The sound of a drawer opening or something.

02:33:15.550 --> 02:33:18.980
I was about to go out there and find out what
she was doing rummaging through my stuff,

02:33:18.980 --> 02:33:24.051
when a wave of realization hit me with a petrifying
force.

02:33:24.051 --> 02:33:29.170
“No reason to be there, no connection to
the person, no witnesses.”

02:33:29.170 --> 02:33:33.590
I locked the bathroom door, grabbed my phone
and called up the number I had for Tara.

02:33:33.590 --> 02:33:34.590
It rang.

02:33:34.590 --> 02:33:36.200
Once, twice, three times.

02:33:36.200 --> 02:33:41.220
I started sweating bullets as I saw her shadow
appear from the crack under the door.

02:33:41.220 --> 02:33:44.950
She had made an effort to make sure all of
her movements were silent, then she just stood

02:33:44.950 --> 02:33:46.021
outside the door.

02:33:46.021 --> 02:33:50.920
After what seemed like ages, I heard a voice
on the other side of the line.

02:33:50.920 --> 02:33:51.920
“Hello?

02:33:51.920 --> 02:33:52.920
Hello?”

02:33:52.920 --> 02:33:57.760
The woman that picked up the phone was not
the same woman standing outside my bathroom

02:33:57.760 --> 02:33:59.130
door.

02:33:59.130 --> 02:34:02.500
Not knowing what else to do I hung up the
phone and began to dial 9-1-1.

02:34:02.500 --> 02:34:05.960
She must have heard me dialing, because she
then grabbed the door handle and tried to

02:34:05.960 --> 02:34:07.271
come into the bathroom.

02:34:07.271 --> 02:34:10.260
As soon as she realized it was locked, she
quickly moved away from the door.

02:34:10.260 --> 02:34:13.180
I braced myself for her to barge down the
door or something…

02:34:13.180 --> 02:34:16.360
That’s when I heard my front door open and
quickly close.

02:34:16.360 --> 02:34:20.230
I assumed that she had left, but I didn't
dare leave the safety of the locked bathroom

02:34:20.230 --> 02:34:22.771
until the cops had arrived and locked down
the area.

02:34:22.771 --> 02:34:25.460
Of course, they found no trace of the woman.

02:34:25.460 --> 02:34:27.120
After telling the police my account of what
went on that night, I tried to get them to

02:34:27.120 --> 02:34:31.820
take down a description of her appearance,
but I was told that there was no case.

02:34:31.820 --> 02:34:36.120
Since I had invited her in, she hadn't actually
broken any law.

02:34:36.120 --> 02:34:39.430
As far as I could tell nothing had been stolen.

02:34:39.430 --> 02:34:43.510
Besides, without knowing her name, or who
she actually was, it was unlikely they would

02:34:43.510 --> 02:34:45.051
have found her anyway.

02:34:45.051 --> 02:34:50.260
Eventually, I got in contact with the real
Tara, and told her about what happened.

02:34:50.260 --> 02:34:54.200
She was understanding when I said that I no
longer felt comfortable meeting up for a blind

02:34:54.200 --> 02:34:55.200
date.

02:34:55.200 --> 02:35:00.021
It's been a couple of days now since the incident
and I've had an uneasy feeling since then.

02:35:00.021 --> 02:35:02.370
I've barely gotten any sleep.

02:35:02.370 --> 02:35:05.911
Sometimes I think I hear the sound of my door
handle wiggling like someone is trying to

02:35:05.911 --> 02:35:11.210
get in, but when I get up to check on it,
the sound dissipates.

02:35:11.210 --> 02:35:12.440
She knew where I lived now.

02:35:12.440 --> 02:35:15.480
What was to stop her from coming back and
finishing the job?

02:35:15.480 --> 02:35:19.760
I tried to tell myself that the whole thing
was a cruel prank… that she was trying to

02:35:19.760 --> 02:35:23.330
mess with me for her own entertainment, and
that she probably just wanted to scare me

02:35:23.330 --> 02:35:24.820
or something…

02:35:24.820 --> 02:35:26.780
Until today.

02:35:26.780 --> 02:35:30.750
See, since that day, I haven’t really had
much of an appetite.

02:35:30.750 --> 02:35:34.910
I finally had the stomach to eat something
again and decided to go to the kitchen and

02:35:34.910 --> 02:35:36.410
prepare something for myself…

02:35:36.410 --> 02:35:45.381
when I found the kitchen knife put away in
the wrong drawer…

02:35:45.381 --> 02:35:52.330
Number 19 - CreepsMcPasta Narrated My Nightmare

02:35:52.330 --> 02:35:57.550
I recently began listening to creepypasta
narrations each night before bed.

02:35:57.550 --> 02:36:02.430
Now I know for some people, that is probably
a terrible idea, that would likely result

02:36:02.430 --> 02:36:07.290
in a state of fear; not being able to sleep
or being riddled with terrible nightmares.

02:36:07.290 --> 02:36:12.690
I even have friends that won't watch a horror
movie past 9PM, for fear that they will not

02:36:12.690 --> 02:36:14.830
be able to sleep that night if they do.

02:36:14.830 --> 02:36:18.560
I, however, am not like most people.

02:36:18.560 --> 02:36:24.180
I've been mostly desensitized to such movies,
so finding a story that really scares me is

02:36:24.180 --> 02:36:25.650
an exciting occurrence.

02:36:25.650 --> 02:36:28.550
I welcome any nightmares that may arise.

02:36:28.550 --> 02:36:32.550
As you get older, it becomes very difficult
to find anything that scares you like when

02:36:32.550 --> 02:36:33.700
you were a child.

02:36:33.700 --> 02:36:38.890
Sure there are worries and stresses that come
with adulthood, but real terror becomes a

02:36:38.890 --> 02:36:44.130
real rarity by the time you hit 8th grade,
other than in your dreams.

02:36:44.130 --> 02:36:48.410
So I started pulling up a creepypasta on YouTube
each night before bed and letting it play

02:36:48.410 --> 02:36:53.890
as I closed my eyes, visualized the story
in my head, and hoped that if I was lucky,

02:36:53.890 --> 02:36:58.660
maybe I'd get the thrill of a nightmare racksacking
my thoughts that evening.

02:36:58.660 --> 02:37:04.600
At least, that's what I thought I wanted...
until recently, when I had a nightmare so

02:37:04.600 --> 02:37:07.720
terrifying, I've had to rethink my outlook
entirely.

02:37:07.720 --> 02:37:13.440
See, the strange thing about the horror narrators
on YouTube, is that while their voices can

02:37:13.440 --> 02:37:18.230
be creepy and unsettling, they also have to
be aesthetically pleasing to the listeners'

02:37:18.230 --> 02:37:24.190
ears, so they also tend to have the most soothing,
full-sounding voices out of anyone you might

02:37:24.190 --> 02:37:25.190
hear.

02:37:25.190 --> 02:37:29.870
And what I've come to find is that oftentimes
the result, is like that of a lullaby and

02:37:29.870 --> 02:37:35.090
after listening to a couple of stories, their
voices can ease you right to sleep.

02:37:35.090 --> 02:37:39.210
That's another reason I had continued to listen
to stories before bed.

02:37:39.210 --> 02:37:45.160
Some of my favorite narrators were The Dark
Somnium, Lady White Rabbit, Mortis Media and

02:37:45.160 --> 02:37:46.690
CreepsMcPasta.

02:37:46.690 --> 02:37:51.610
Creeps was usually my go-to for falling asleep,
as he has that relaxing tone of voice that

02:37:51.610 --> 02:37:55.780
just puts you at ease and makes it easy to
drift off while listening to some classic

02:37:55.780 --> 02:37:57.410
internet horror stories.

02:37:57.410 --> 02:38:02.730
He also uploads nearly every day, so there's
usually a new video to listen to each night,

02:38:02.730 --> 02:38:04.080
which is nice.

02:38:04.080 --> 02:38:08.680
Every now and then, Creeps will upload something
known as a compilation video, which consists

02:38:08.680 --> 02:38:13.181
of all of his narrations from that month,
combined into one long video, which tends

02:38:13.181 --> 02:38:15.470
to land around 4 hours or so.

02:38:15.470 --> 02:38:19.970
I had fallen asleep listening to one of these
compilation videos when I discovered what

02:38:19.970 --> 02:38:22.550
I'll call... an intriguing life hack.

02:38:22.550 --> 02:38:28.720
I found that listening to a long enough story
at just the right volume can result in me

02:38:28.720 --> 02:38:32.590
actually hearing the creepypasta narration
in my dreams!

02:38:32.590 --> 02:38:37.500
This was obviously insanely cool for me, but
it didn't stop there.

02:38:37.500 --> 02:38:41.930
What I discovered, was that my dreams would
actually change based on what I was hearing

02:38:41.930 --> 02:38:43.261
in the story.

02:38:43.261 --> 02:38:46.800
Have you ever had someone touch you or kick
you while you were asleep, and have something

02:38:46.800 --> 02:38:49.380
similar happen in your dream as result?

02:38:49.380 --> 02:38:54.240
I imagine that it's the same concept here,
only instead of a physical response, my brain

02:38:54.240 --> 02:38:56.400
was responding to the audio.

02:38:56.400 --> 02:39:01.050
Needless to say, I had a lot of fun experimenting
with this trick, forcing myself to have dreams

02:39:01.050 --> 02:39:05.700
of classic horror stories, creating playlists
for myself so I can control which stories

02:39:05.700 --> 02:39:11.300
play when I enter my REM sleep cycle and getting
myself genuinely horrified when the stories

02:39:11.300 --> 02:39:13.130
took a turn for the worst.

02:39:13.130 --> 02:39:18.250
At first, if there was any kind of loud noise
or music change in the narrative [stinger]

02:39:18.250 --> 02:39:24.080
it would jolt me awake, but the more I listened,
the more I became desensitized to it.

02:39:24.080 --> 02:39:28.800
After a couple of months I was able to sleep
through any music or sound effects and Creeps

02:39:28.800 --> 02:39:31.220
was the soundtrack to my nightmares.

02:39:31.220 --> 02:39:37.150
I worked my way through the essentials, until
I got to Teeth.jpg...

02:39:37.150 --> 02:39:40.380
I had set it up so that the story would start
after 90 minutes.

02:39:40.380 --> 02:39:45.810
So basically, when my dream picked up, the
story has just started.

02:39:45.810 --> 02:39:50.250
Teeth.jpg, if you’re not familiar with it,
is about four art students who live together

02:39:50.250 --> 02:39:55.850
and come back from one summer break to one
of the roommates undergoing a strange and

02:39:55.850 --> 02:39:57.730
disturbing behaviour change.

02:39:57.730 --> 02:40:02.000
What made this experience so real for me,
was that when you are in a dream, you don’t

02:40:02.000 --> 02:40:04.730
really question what’s going on for whatever
reason.

02:40:04.730 --> 02:40:10.280
So although the characters in this creepypasta,
Josh, Lily, and Daniel, the psycho one, are

02:40:10.280 --> 02:40:14.460
completely fictional, I felt like they were
my closest friends during the dream.

02:40:14.460 --> 02:40:18.920
My mind never really tried to challenge the
fact that I just lived in this world with

02:40:18.920 --> 02:40:19.920
these characters.

02:40:19.920 --> 02:40:25.170
In one of the early scenes, Daniel goes missing
late at night and I, as the main character

02:40:25.170 --> 02:40:42.560
of this story, end up finding the creepy teeth.jpg
file on his computer.

02:40:42.560 --> 02:40:52.700
In the dream, when I am going through his
files, I keep on looking over the door, and

02:40:52.700 --> 02:40:56.300
despite the fact that I know this story in
real life, it’s like I don’t know what’s

02:40:56.300 --> 02:41:00.760
going to happen in the moment, so I feel like
Daniel is going to come walking in any second.

02:41:00.760 --> 02:41:06.220
The strange thing was, every time I looked
back at the door, it was different.

02:41:06.220 --> 02:41:11.300
The lighting outside would change, and the
angle at which the door was open was always

02:41:11.300 --> 02:41:12.640
different.

02:41:12.640 --> 02:41:19.340
I would see shadows on the wall sometimes,
despite the fact that nobody was really there.

02:41:19.340 --> 02:41:22.860
That was tripping me out, but in addition
to that, there were a bunch of files on Daniel’s

02:41:22.860 --> 02:41:27.400
computer other than those mentioned in the
story, and I looked at them, despite the fact

02:41:27.400 --> 02:41:30.940
that Creeps’ narration did not instruct
me to do so.

02:41:30.940 --> 02:41:32.110
They were photos.

02:41:32.110 --> 02:41:35.460
Real photos from my Facebook page.

02:41:35.460 --> 02:41:37.561
Most of which were ones that I was in.

02:41:37.561 --> 02:41:38.590
Me and my friends.

02:41:38.590 --> 02:41:40.130
Me and my girlfriend.

02:41:40.130 --> 02:41:42.280
Me and my ex-girlfriend.

02:41:42.280 --> 02:41:46.710
And again, at the time, I didn’t realize
I was dreaming, I was just taking this all

02:41:46.710 --> 02:41:50.030
at face, and it was really freaking me out.

02:41:50.030 --> 02:41:53.110
I ran out of the room and hit my foot on the
doorframe on the way out.

02:41:53.110 --> 02:41:54.240
It really hurt.

02:41:54.240 --> 02:41:55.510
It wasn’t like a dream at all.

02:41:55.510 --> 02:41:59.220
The pain was so realistic and it was pulsing
through my leg.

02:41:59.220 --> 02:42:02.820
There were more strange deviations that occurred
in this dream.

02:42:02.820 --> 02:42:09.860
For example, when we suspected Daniel of doing
something to Lily and went through his bag.

02:42:09.860 --> 02:42:15.300
I immediately recognized the items that poured
out of my bag.

02:42:15.300 --> 02:42:19.979
The were all the same objects that I have
sitting on my nightstand: the alarm clock,

02:42:19.979 --> 02:42:23.060
my phone, a box of tissue and a picture frame.

02:42:23.060 --> 02:42:27.360
I reached out to pick up my alarm clock, but
when my hand got to the point of touching

02:42:27.360 --> 02:42:28.650
it, I couldn’t feel anything.

02:42:28.650 --> 02:42:30.340
I couldn’t pick it up.

02:42:30.340 --> 02:42:33.110
Since this was a dream, I didn’t find this
that out of the ordinary.

02:42:33.110 --> 02:42:37.270
It just felt more like I was doing something
wrong, as opposed to some kind of glitch in

02:42:37.270 --> 02:42:38.270
reality.

02:42:38.270 --> 02:42:50.380
There were also some photographs 

02:42:50.380 --> 02:42:57.170
of Lily.

02:42:57.170 --> 02:43:01.170
I found that these were much easier for me
to interact with and I was able to pick up

02:43:01.170 --> 02:43:03.510
each one and inspect the markings.

02:43:03.510 --> 02:43:07.580
They were polaroid photos, which doesn’t
really make sense thinking back on it, but

02:43:07.580 --> 02:43:10.590
each one had Lily’s teeth notated with permanent
marker.

02:43:10.590 --> 02:43:15.700
We began searching for Lily, and it felt like
we were wandering around aimlessly forever.

02:43:15.700 --> 02:43:16.700
Days even.

02:43:16.700 --> 02:43:20.550
It’s strange how time can seem to be uncompressed
when you’re dreaming.

02:43:20.550 --> 02:43:22.890
Eventually we found the house.

02:43:22.890 --> 02:43:26.930
Josh kicked down the door and we explored
onward into the basement.

02:43:26.930 --> 02:43:32.150
Upon entering, I was met with a foul odor
that instantly sickened me.

02:43:32.150 --> 02:43:37.950
Typically smell has usually been a non-factor
for me in dreams, but this, just like when

02:43:37.950 --> 02:43:39.510
I banged my foot, was so real.

02:43:39.510 --> 02:43:42.160
I didn’t want to be there anymore.

02:43:42.160 --> 02:43:43.610
I couldn’t stand to go on.

02:43:43.610 --> 02:43:46.550
But I was fighting the movement of my own
body!

02:43:46.550 --> 02:43:52.060
It was obeying each of Creeps’ commands,
which were booming over us in his calm, familiar

02:43:52.060 --> 02:43:54.700
voice and echoing all throughout the basement.

02:43:54.700 --> 02:43:59.220
I wasn’t in control anymore but I could
still feel the wretched nausea caused by that

02:43:59.220 --> 02:44:00.220
smell.

02:44:00.220 --> 02:44:03.140
I wanted to go outside and throw up but I
couldn’t do that.

02:44:03.140 --> 02:44:05.470
I was continuing on against my own will.

02:44:05.470 --> 02:44:10.630
I looked at Josh and he actually seemed to
be unaffected by it, and it was at that point

02:44:10.630 --> 02:44:14.970
where I think I gradually started to realize
that I was in a dream.

02:44:14.970 --> 02:44:20.340
No… a nightmare, I could not wake up from.

02:44:20.340 --> 02:44:22.271
We found Lily’s sweater.

02:44:22.271 --> 02:44:25.180
At this point I actually did throw up.

02:44:25.180 --> 02:44:29.090
I’ll avoid the grotesque details of what
happened next as much as possible.

02:44:29.090 --> 02:44:31.010
But I have to get my point across.

02:44:31.010 --> 02:44:34.790
Through my own eyes I could see the puke piling
up on the floor.

02:44:34.790 --> 02:44:37.420
But how I felt was much different than that.

02:44:37.420 --> 02:44:40.420
It was like it was piling up and wouldn’t
leave my mouth.

02:44:40.420 --> 02:44:45.540
I started spitting, choking, doing whatever
I could to prevent myself from drowning in

02:44:45.540 --> 02:44:46.601
my own waste.

02:44:46.601 --> 02:44:51.130
But the grossness of all of this was making
me sicker and making it clog my mouth even

02:44:51.130 --> 02:44:52.130
more.

02:44:52.130 --> 02:44:57.380
I felt like I was going to suffocate, and
then somehow I was able to clear my airways.

02:44:57.380 --> 02:44:59.380
I’m not really sure how.

02:44:59.380 --> 02:45:01.530
Sorry about that.

02:45:01.530 --> 02:45:04.090
No more gross parts.

02:45:04.090 --> 02:45:09.479
We wandered around around in the dark.

02:45:09.479 --> 02:45:11.700
Someone turned on a red light.

02:45:11.700 --> 02:45:13.170
I heard Josh scream.

02:45:13.170 --> 02:45:14.700
It was probably the loudest thing I had ever
heard.

02:45:14.700 --> 02:45:18.930
It was so loud that it temporarily overtook
the sound of CreepsMcPasta’s narrations.

02:45:18.930 --> 02:45:23.531
It echoed everywhere in the room, piercing
my eardrums.

02:45:23.531 --> 02:45:26.950
It felt like my head might pop, but then the
echoes slowly faded out.

02:45:26.950 --> 02:45:30.920
That’s when I saw Lily.

02:45:30.920 --> 02:45:31.920
Eyes gouged.

02:45:31.920 --> 02:45:33.030
Teeth repurposed.

02:45:33.030 --> 02:45:37.590
At this point I knew I was in a nightmare.

02:45:37.590 --> 02:45:38.590
And I wanted out.

02:45:38.590 --> 02:45:39.590
I tried sitting up.

02:45:39.590 --> 02:45:40.590
Opening my eyes.

02:45:40.590 --> 02:45:41.590
None of that worked.

02:45:41.590 --> 02:45:44.640
I heard the footsteps come up behind me.

02:45:44.640 --> 02:45:46.890
I pinched myself.

02:45:46.890 --> 02:45:48.020
Nothing.

02:45:48.020 --> 02:45:53.431
I’m sorry you had to find out this way.

02:45:53.431 --> 02:45:54.431
But it’s OK.

02:45:54.431 --> 02:45:55.431
It’s all for the sake of art.

02:45:55.431 --> 02:45:58.420
Daniel’s dialogue was perfectly in sync
with the booming narration.

02:45:58.420 --> 02:46:00.450
I beat my fist against my body.

02:46:00.450 --> 02:46:01.450
No luck.

02:46:01.450 --> 02:46:02.680
I started punching myself in the face.

02:46:02.680 --> 02:46:04.570
NO MATTER WHAT I DID…

02:46:04.570 --> 02:46:05.721
I couldn’t.

02:46:05.721 --> 02:46:06.721
Wake.

02:46:06.721 --> 02:46:07.721
Myself.

02:46:07.721 --> 02:46:08.721
Up.

02:46:08.721 --> 02:46:11.720
That’s when I was yanked backwards into
the dark.

02:46:11.720 --> 02:46:16.500
My stomach dropped as this happened and my
eyes were blurry and filled with tears.

02:46:16.500 --> 02:46:17.500
I kicked.

02:46:17.500 --> 02:46:18.500
I fought.

02:46:18.500 --> 02:46:19.500
But I couldn’t make contact.

02:46:19.500 --> 02:46:23.210
Daniel was was beating and bludgeoning my
with what must have been a somewhat sharp

02:46:23.210 --> 02:46:24.720
metal post.

02:46:24.720 --> 02:46:26.771
All the pain was real.

02:46:26.771 --> 02:46:28.400
It was an intense searing pain.

02:46:28.400 --> 02:46:32.770
It was unlike anything I had felt, in waking
or in sleep.

02:46:32.770 --> 02:46:33.770
I was bleeding.

02:46:33.770 --> 02:46:37.350
I could tell because I reached to grasp my
injury and it felt wet.

02:46:37.350 --> 02:46:53.500
And then suddenly, it just stopped, as Creeps
gave the final narration.

02:46:53.500 --> 02:46:58.590
I thought I was done for, but then everything
around me, the entire environment, just faded

02:46:58.590 --> 02:46:59.590
away.

02:46:59.590 --> 02:47:02.230
I found myself laying in a white void.

02:47:02.230 --> 02:47:04.000
I guess it's true what they say.

02:47:04.000 --> 02:47:06.210
How you can't die in your dream.

02:47:06.210 --> 02:47:11.761
I've just been laying here for... what feels
like days, but realistically has been about

02:47:11.761 --> 02:47:12.761
9 hours and 15 minutes.

02:47:12.761 --> 02:47:13.761
How do I know this?

02:47:13.761 --> 02:47:22.160
My alarm just went off for the second time,
and it isn't waking me up.

02:47:22.160 --> 02:47:30.590
I’m starting to doubt it ever will.

02:47:30.590 --> 02:47:36.120
Number 20 - Tower of Terror: Last Ride

02:47:36.120 --> 02:47:40.510
When I heard that The Tower of Terror at Disney’s
California Adventure was being remodeled into

02:47:40.510 --> 02:47:44.950
a Guardians of the Galaxy ride, I immediately
made plans with my friends, Joey and Matt,

02:47:44.950 --> 02:47:46.830
to go pay the ride one last visit.

02:47:46.830 --> 02:47:51.140
We all decided to take a Monday off, and visit
the park on the last day of the ride’s operation,

02:47:51.140 --> 02:47:53.870
in hopes that there might be some kind of
special send off.

02:47:53.870 --> 02:47:57.830
If you’ve never been to Disney, Tower of
Terror was a part dark-ride part free-fall

02:47:57.830 --> 02:48:00.410
ride themed around an abandoned Hollywood
Hotel.

02:48:00.410 --> 02:48:04.070
Guests are told they are entering a special
episode of The Twilight Zone.

02:48:04.070 --> 02:48:08.460
Five people riding in an elevator on one Halloween
night in the 30s were struck by lightning,

02:48:08.460 --> 02:48:12.271
causing them, and an entire section of the
hotel to disappear into another dimension.

02:48:12.271 --> 02:48:16.410
Let me make one thing clear: I was never the
type of guy who believes in ghosts.

02:48:16.410 --> 02:48:18.890
That’s part of what made me love The Tower
of Terror though.

02:48:18.890 --> 02:48:22.830
The theming and effects were so well done
that you really did feel like you were stepping

02:48:22.830 --> 02:48:26.860
into a dimension where ghosts do exist, and
it was a lot of fun.

02:48:26.860 --> 02:48:30.920
As we walked through the Hollywood Blvd area
of the park towards Hollywood Tower, I couldn’t

02:48:30.920 --> 02:48:35.530
help but notice how iconic it looked, and
think about how much I was going to miss this

02:48:35.530 --> 02:48:36.810
ride when it was gone.

02:48:36.810 --> 02:48:40.700
The California Adventure skyline was going
to look a lot different without it, that much

02:48:40.700 --> 02:48:41.700
was for sure.

02:48:41.700 --> 02:48:44.590
As we turned the corner to the street where
the tower was located, we were met with a

02:48:44.590 --> 02:48:48.180
huge line, pouring way outside of the ordinary
queue area.

02:48:48.180 --> 02:48:51.810
Understandably, it seemed that lots of other
Disney fans had the same idea that we did,

02:48:51.810 --> 02:48:54.010
and wanted to give the ride a proper send
off.

02:48:54.010 --> 02:48:57.630
We decided to hit up some of the other rides
first and return to Tower of Terror once the

02:48:57.630 --> 02:48:58.930
sun had gone down.

02:48:58.930 --> 02:49:04.110
This turned out to be a great idea… or so
it seemed at the time... because most of the

02:49:04.110 --> 02:49:06.750
rest of the park was relatively empty in comparison.

02:49:06.750 --> 02:49:10.050
We ended getting on just about everything
else that we wanted to do before returning

02:49:10.050 --> 02:49:12.060
to The Tower of Terror that evening.

02:49:12.060 --> 02:49:16.280
The tower was lit with those ominous glowing
blue lights as we approached it for the final

02:49:16.280 --> 02:49:17.280
time.

02:49:17.280 --> 02:49:20.950
There was still a very long line when we got
there, which we expected, so it was getting

02:49:20.950 --> 02:49:24.780
pretty late by the time we even hit the front
gates to the attraction’s official queue.

02:49:24.780 --> 02:49:28.710
Joey was starting to get nervous about us
making it in before the park closed, even

02:49:28.710 --> 02:49:30.090
though they were open late that night.

02:49:30.090 --> 02:49:33.740
We were actually one of the last groups to
get through before they started turning people

02:49:33.740 --> 02:49:34.740
away.

02:49:34.740 --> 02:49:38.060
After welcoming us to the Hollywood Tower
Hotel, a man in a bellhop uniform with dark

02:49:38.060 --> 02:49:42.850
circles under his eyes closed up the giant
metal gates behind us, presumably never to

02:49:42.850 --> 02:49:45.210
be opened again.

02:49:45.210 --> 02:49:50.990
At first, I was feeling relieved to have made
it in time to go on the ride, but I was quickly

02:49:50.990 --> 02:49:53.190
overcome with an uneasy feeling…

02:49:53.190 --> 02:49:55.410
Something was off.

02:49:55.410 --> 02:49:58.780
Before entering the building, the line winds
through the main level terrace leading up

02:49:58.780 --> 02:50:00.110
to the building’s entrance.

02:50:00.110 --> 02:50:03.860
I know the area is supposed to look worn down
by the elements, but it looked even shabbier

02:50:03.860 --> 02:50:04.860
than usual.

02:50:04.860 --> 02:50:08.960
The plants were all overgrown, and some of
the lamp posts were broken, making it very

02:50:08.960 --> 02:50:09.960
difficult to see.

02:50:09.960 --> 02:50:13.141
I even came close to stepping on some broken
glass on the ground!

02:50:13.141 --> 02:50:15.850
But the strangest part, was the screaming.

02:50:15.850 --> 02:50:20.430
These were no ordinary theme park screams
though, they sounded like screams of agony,

02:50:20.430 --> 02:50:22.090
like someone was being tortured.

02:50:22.090 --> 02:50:25.700
We were wondering what was getting such violent
sounding reactions out of the riders, but

02:50:25.700 --> 02:50:29.470
eventually came to find that the screaming
was coming from the speakers hidden around

02:50:29.470 --> 02:50:30.470
the area.

02:50:30.470 --> 02:50:33.770
I’m not sure if that made me feel any better
to be honest, why would they be playing such

02:50:33.770 --> 02:50:35.310
disturbing audio for their guests?

02:50:35.310 --> 02:50:37.229
It all just seemed so weird.

02:50:37.229 --> 02:50:40.700
When we got to the covered area just outside
the building, it seemed like the pillars holding

02:50:40.700 --> 02:50:44.810
up the structure had some considerable decay…
and all the windows were broken.

02:50:44.810 --> 02:50:48.520
I couldn’t remember exactly what this area
looked like last time I was here, but I was

02:50:48.520 --> 02:50:52.300
fairly certain it was at least a little bit
more put together than this.

02:50:52.300 --> 02:50:55.630
After what seemed like forever, we finally
made it into the hotel.

02:50:55.630 --> 02:50:57.710
This when things really got weird.

02:50:57.710 --> 02:51:01.300
Normally, the hotel lobby is made to look
like it was abandoned in the 30s.

02:51:01.300 --> 02:51:02.931
Which it still was.

02:51:02.931 --> 02:51:07.490
Only this time, the room was filled with 15-20
Disney employees, all wearing the same Hollywood

02:51:07.490 --> 02:51:09.630
Tower Hotel bellhop uniform.

02:51:09.630 --> 02:51:13.290
They were standing straight up like soldiers
around all the major set pieces in the room,

02:51:13.290 --> 02:51:16.190
and every single one of them was just staring
at us.

02:51:16.190 --> 02:51:20.300
It was almost as if they were guarding something,
but none of them said one word the entire

02:51:20.300 --> 02:51:21.300
time.

02:51:21.300 --> 02:51:23.979
Matt even tried asking one of the employees
how much longer it would be until we reached

02:51:23.979 --> 02:51:28.130
the front of the line… to which… the guy
made eye contact with him and just stared

02:51:28.130 --> 02:51:30.190
into his soul with a completely straight face.

02:51:30.190 --> 02:51:34.300
I’ll never forget the look of those blue
eyes with the dark bags underneath piercing

02:51:34.300 --> 02:51:37.221
at us from his pale, almost greyish skin.

02:51:37.221 --> 02:51:40.440
At this point, I was thinking that this all
must be part of the park’s special going

02:51:40.440 --> 02:51:44.360
away present to the fans of this ride and
they were really going all out to make the

02:51:44.360 --> 02:51:45.960
last night as creepy as possible.

02:51:45.960 --> 02:51:50.170
I let myself think that they were really outdoing
themselves, and I was really enjoying the

02:51:50.170 --> 02:51:51.170
show.

02:51:51.170 --> 02:51:54.910
I also noticed that the iconic owl statue
in the center of the lobby had it’s wings

02:51:54.910 --> 02:52:06.660
broken off and was now inside of a cage.

02:52:06.660 --> 02:52:09.561
At some point a couple men in construction
helmets came in and started to remove the

02:52:09.561 --> 02:52:11.990
cage and some of the other furniture.

02:52:11.990 --> 02:52:15.200
This was the first time I saw one of the bellhops
react and speak up.

02:52:15.200 --> 02:52:18.470
He grabbed the construction worker’s hand
and said, “sir, please.

02:52:18.470 --> 02:52:20.860
The hour is not yet upon us.”

02:52:20.860 --> 02:52:24.430
I assumed that this was also part of the show…

02:52:24.430 --> 02:52:27.810
I mean, they wouldn’t really be clearing
the place out minutes after the closure, right?

02:52:27.810 --> 02:52:32.271
At this point, riders are taken in groups
to the Hotel Library for a briefing video.

02:52:32.271 --> 02:52:36.190
Matt and Joey walked ahead into the library,
but when I tried to pass through, the bellhop

02:52:36.190 --> 02:52:38.260
stopped me and told me to wait for the next
group.

02:52:38.260 --> 02:52:42.320
I tried to explain that I was with those two
guys, but the bellhop wouldn’t let me pass.

02:52:42.320 --> 02:52:45.650
Matt and Joey didn’t seem to notice I was
gone, but I figured I would catch up with

02:52:45.650 --> 02:52:47.520
them before they boarded the elevator.

02:52:47.520 --> 02:52:50.810
When it was my turn to go see the briefing
video, there were only a couple of a people

02:52:50.810 --> 02:52:53.300
left in line behind me, so the three of us
went in.

02:52:53.300 --> 02:52:55.980
We get into the orientation room and the lights
go out.

02:52:55.980 --> 02:52:58.840
We sit there in the dark for what seems like
ages.

02:52:58.840 --> 02:53:01.280
That's when I hear someone shuffle around
behind me…

02:53:01.280 --> 02:53:05.620
I could SWEAR, it was just me and those two
other guests who had come into the library.

02:53:05.620 --> 02:53:08.120
I was positive they were the only ones behind
me in line.

02:53:08.120 --> 02:53:12.690
I had to to think that whoever was behind
me was just one of the employees, but then,

02:53:12.690 --> 02:53:16.479
seemingly just to disprove that theory, they
guy moves closer to me, and starts breathing

02:53:16.479 --> 02:53:17.479
down my neck.

02:53:17.479 --> 02:53:21.940
I was getting very uncomfortable, but then
just as I was about to say something…

02:53:21.940 --> 02:53:22.940
*Bzzt!*

02:53:22.940 --> 02:53:28.181
The orientation video starts, so I just take
a step forward, away from that creep behind

02:53:28.181 --> 02:53:29.181
me.

02:53:29.181 --> 02:53:32.160
“You unlock this door with the key of imagination.

02:53:32.160 --> 02:53:34.150
Beyond it, is another dimension.

02:53:34.150 --> 02:53:35.750
A dimension of sound.

02:53:35.750 --> 02:53:37.341
A dimension of sight.

02:53:37.341 --> 02:53:38.950
A dimension of mind.”

02:53:38.950 --> 02:53:42.780
I wasn’t sure if there was something weird
going on with Rod Serling’s voice, almost

02:53:42.780 --> 02:53:45.500
like it was off pitch or something…

02:53:45.500 --> 02:53:51.330
“You’re moving into a land of both shadow
and substance, of things and ideas you just

02:53:51.330 --> 02:53:52.330
crossed over into…

02:53:52.330 --> 02:53:54.180
The Twilight Zone.”

02:53:54.180 --> 02:53:58.160
The rest of the introduction video went on
as it normally does…

02:53:58.160 --> 02:54:01.760
That is, until it got to the part where Rod
addresses the audience.

02:54:01.760 --> 02:54:06.300
“Tonight’s story of the Twilight Zone
will be your last.”

02:54:06.300 --> 02:54:07.300
Ok…

02:54:07.300 --> 02:54:08.370
Now that was definitely not normal.

02:54:08.370 --> 02:54:11.940
They must have changed up the intro video
for the final night or something.

02:54:11.940 --> 02:54:16.140
“This, as you may recognize, is a maintenance
service elevator.

02:54:16.140 --> 02:54:18.190
Still in operation, but not for long.

02:54:18.190 --> 02:54:23.150
At midnight tonight, normal operation of this
machine will cease and at that moment the

02:54:23.150 --> 02:54:24.150
Stars…

02:54:24.150 --> 02:54:26.500
Will come out to play.

02:54:26.500 --> 02:54:33.271
When this happens, you, will have to fend
for yourself and your safety is not guaranteed.

02:54:33.271 --> 02:54:36.640
You are about to embark on a ride through
history, and your destination?

02:54:36.640 --> 02:54:37.640
The Twilight Zone.”

02:54:37.640 --> 02:54:38.640
All right!

02:54:38.640 --> 02:54:40.550
This is exactly why we wanted to come on the
last day!

02:54:40.550 --> 02:54:41.550
I was so excited.

02:54:41.550 --> 02:54:44.420
I couldn't wait to find Joey and Matt and
get on this ride.

02:54:44.420 --> 02:54:48.190
The doors opened and we continued onto the
boiler room, the last part of the hotel before

02:54:48.190 --> 02:54:49.520
we get into the elevator.

02:54:49.520 --> 02:54:52.021
The creep who was standing behind me didn't
join us however.

02:54:52.021 --> 02:54:55.120
I looked back and saw him just standing there
in the dark.

02:54:55.120 --> 02:54:59.190
I couldn’t see him that well, he was basically
just a silhouette in this lighting, I was

02:54:59.190 --> 02:55:02.340
about to see what I think was an outline of
a bellhop uniform…

02:55:02.340 --> 02:55:03.340
Whatever.

02:55:03.340 --> 02:55:06.110
I scanned the boiler room for my friends,
but didn't see them anywhere.

02:55:06.110 --> 02:55:08.400
I hoped they hadn't gotten on the ride without
me.

02:55:08.400 --> 02:55:12.070
The more I searched around for them, the more
I realized that the entire room felt kind

02:55:12.070 --> 02:55:15.930
of empty, at least considering how many people
had just been ahead of us.

02:55:15.930 --> 02:55:17.400
It was also freezing cold down here.

02:55:17.400 --> 02:55:18.400
I was getting goosebumps.

02:55:18.400 --> 02:55:22.780
I know it was January, but we were inside
and it was Southern California after all.

02:55:22.780 --> 02:55:24.710
It doesn’t usually get this cold.

02:55:24.710 --> 02:55:28.340
The two other guys from the library and I
were directed past the usual boarding stations

02:55:28.340 --> 02:55:30.330
to a creaky stairway leading up.

02:55:30.330 --> 02:55:32.400
This was completely new to me…

02:55:32.400 --> 02:55:36.021
I mean, I remembered seeing these stairs before
but I always thought they were just a decoration

02:55:36.021 --> 02:55:38.660
to make the hotel feel more fleshed out than
it really is.

02:55:38.660 --> 02:55:42.330
Or maybe one of those secret entrances for
the cast members to access their changing

02:55:42.330 --> 02:55:43.490
rooms and whatnot.

02:55:43.490 --> 02:55:47.940
Apparently, I was wrong, and there are more
elevator entrances up above, as well as more

02:55:47.940 --> 02:55:49.940
pipes, machinery and theming.

02:55:49.940 --> 02:55:52.320
The only thing that wasn’t wasn’t up there
was people.

02:55:52.320 --> 02:55:55.771
I tried to text my friends to see where they
were at, but my phone was dead from a long

02:55:55.771 --> 02:55:56.820
day at the park.

02:55:56.820 --> 02:55:59.440
One of the employees led us to a station that
was completely empty.

02:55:59.440 --> 02:56:01.990
We didn’t have to wait long for the car
to arrive.

02:56:01.990 --> 02:56:05.320
The elevator shaft doors parted, and we entered
the ride.

02:56:05.320 --> 02:56:08.480
I chose a seat towards the middle, and the
other two guys filled in on either side of

02:56:08.480 --> 02:56:09.480
me.

02:56:09.480 --> 02:56:13.010
The Tower of Terror starts by traveling up
to the first floor, where the doors open and

02:56:13.010 --> 02:56:14.010
the guests see a mirror.

02:56:14.010 --> 02:56:16.290
The narrator then asks them to wave goodbye
to the real world.

02:56:16.290 --> 02:56:22.300
When the doors opened for our ride I saw a
man sitting directly behind me with what appeared

02:56:22.300 --> 02:56:23.840
to be a hunting rifle!

02:56:23.840 --> 02:56:25.530
This REALLY startled me!

02:56:25.530 --> 02:56:29.070
Thinking it might have been some kind of effect,
like the hitchhiking ghosts in the Haunted

02:56:29.070 --> 02:56:31.891
Mansion, I turned back to see that there really
was someone there!

02:56:31.891 --> 02:56:34.200
It was the creepy bellhop guy again!

02:56:34.200 --> 02:56:35.870
At this point I started to freak out.

02:56:35.870 --> 02:56:40.100
Not only was this the second time this guy
inexplicably appeared behind me, but he was

02:56:40.100 --> 02:56:41.460
carrying a weapon?!

02:56:41.460 --> 02:56:45.340
I know Disney can have a dark side at times,
but this is still Disney we’re talking about

02:56:45.340 --> 02:56:46.340
here.

02:56:46.340 --> 02:56:47.340
A family company.

02:56:47.340 --> 02:56:50.271
I was truly getting scared that something
was very wrong here… but what could I do?

02:56:50.271 --> 02:56:51.780
I was strapped into the seat.

02:56:51.780 --> 02:56:55.860
So I start to scream and panic, I don’t
really remember exactly what I said, but I

02:56:55.860 --> 02:56:58.900
do remember the ride violently jolting up
to the next floor.

02:56:58.900 --> 02:57:02.350
The next scene is the hallway full of guest
rooms where riders are shown the ghosts of

02:57:02.350 --> 02:57:03.650
the five hotel guests who disappeared years
ago.

02:57:03.650 --> 02:57:09.550
Only this time, the holograms look shockingly
realistic and they don’t seem to notice

02:57:09.550 --> 02:57:10.550
us.

02:57:10.550 --> 02:57:11.990
They are just standing in the hotel talking.

02:57:11.990 --> 02:57:15.979
The audio isn’t that loud, but they seem
to be arguing with the employee about something

02:57:15.979 --> 02:57:17.570
and the woman is sobbing.

02:57:17.570 --> 02:57:21.300
Again, it was difficult to hear over the rain
and thunder, but she said something along

02:57:21.300 --> 02:57:23.290
the lines of, “don’t make us go”.

02:57:23.290 --> 02:57:27.351
She’s crying, begging and pleading, and
the employee is just standing there with a

02:57:27.351 --> 02:57:28.560
disgusted look on his face.

02:57:28.560 --> 02:57:34.700
Before I can gather any more information,
a huge flash of lightning fills the room,

02:57:34.700 --> 02:57:36.362
and I hear the boom of thunder, accompanied
by broken glass and horrific screaming.

02:57:36.362 --> 02:57:39.310
This may have been a special effect, but I
distinctly remember feeling the heat of this

02:57:39.310 --> 02:57:40.310
lightning strike.

02:57:40.310 --> 02:57:43.580
What I saw then the smoke cleared, completely
devastated me!

02:57:43.580 --> 02:57:48.270
I saw all five of the the bodies sprawled
out on the floor, in a disturbingly realistic

02:57:48.270 --> 02:57:49.270
death scene.

02:57:49.270 --> 02:57:52.479
The man seemed to have vomited blood all over
himself, and the little girl’s hair was

02:57:52.479 --> 02:57:53.570
standing up on end.

02:57:53.570 --> 02:57:57.700
But the creepiest part, had to have been her
eyes, which had rolled to the back of her

02:57:57.700 --> 02:57:58.700
head.

02:57:58.700 --> 02:58:02.210
Her eyelids seemed to be sparked open and
it was almost as if her blank stare was pointed

02:58:02.210 --> 02:58:03.420
right at me.

02:58:03.420 --> 02:58:08.750
I was completely at a loss for words, sounds…
anything, when the ride jerked upward again

02:58:08.750 --> 02:58:09.970
to the top level.

02:58:09.970 --> 02:58:11.970
The ride stopped at the top, like it always
does.

02:58:11.970 --> 02:58:15.400
It was dark, there were only a few main lights
left on in the park.

02:58:15.400 --> 02:58:18.990
I guess the other major attractions were already
shut down for the night.

02:58:18.990 --> 02:58:22.990
Instead of the usual audio, the narrator was
just laughing like a madman.

02:58:22.990 --> 02:58:26.500
After a while, it went quiet and nothing happened.

02:58:26.500 --> 02:58:31.310
I was beginning to think the ride was stuck,
and to be honest it was almost a relief after

02:58:31.310 --> 02:58:32.920
everything I had seen.

02:58:32.920 --> 02:58:37.550
The moment of solace however, was short lived,
when I felt the man behind me, who I guess

02:58:37.550 --> 02:58:42.380
I had temporarily forgotten about in all the
chaos, grab onto my shoulder.

02:58:42.380 --> 02:58:46.271
At this point, I knew that there was nobody
who could help me, but internally I was freaking

02:58:46.271 --> 02:58:49.790
out, and I didn’t dare turn around or acknowledge
what he was doing.

02:58:49.790 --> 02:58:53.610
I know people are going to call me out and
say that I made up this story for attention.

02:58:53.610 --> 02:58:57.280
And I know people are going to try to prove
that most of these occurrences are absolutely

02:58:57.280 --> 02:59:00.271
impossible, and I really can’t blame them
for that.

02:59:00.271 --> 02:59:05.770
But what I saw next… even if it was just
for a fraction of a second, has stuck in my

02:59:05.770 --> 02:59:10.950
mind perfectly since that night, and I am
100% sure of what I saw.

02:59:10.950 --> 02:59:15.311
As the ride started to drop and the man behind
me increased pressure on my shoulder, the

02:59:15.311 --> 02:59:20.830
on ride photo camera flashed, and for a split
second I saw three construction workers hanging

02:59:20.830 --> 02:59:23.911
by the neck from the top pole upon which the
camera is mounted.

02:59:23.911 --> 02:59:34.811
These were not holograms, and even though
I only saw them for a split second, I’m

02:59:34.811 --> 02:59:36.710
quite sure that they were not props.

02:59:36.710 --> 02:59:41.860
After that first drop the elevator continued
to bounce up and down at nauseating speeds.

02:59:41.860 --> 02:59:45.440
Between the G-Force and the pressure of the
man grabbing my shoulder, I felt like I was

02:59:45.440 --> 02:59:46.620
about to pass out.

02:59:46.620 --> 02:59:53.880
I actually started to black out and closed
my eyes when I felt the ride come to a screeching

02:59:53.880 --> 02:59:54.880
halt.

02:59:54.880 --> 02:59:59.000
I was ready for this horrific nightmare to
be over, but apparently, the ride had other

02:59:59.000 --> 03:00:00.000
plans.

03:00:00.000 --> 03:00:03.490
Once I opened my eyes and regained my composure
I found myself back on the second floor, the

03:00:03.490 --> 03:00:04.880
one with all the guest rooms.

03:00:04.880 --> 03:00:08.520
The dead bodies were still there, but now
they had the ghosts standing over them, motioning

03:00:08.520 --> 03:00:09.990
for us to come closer.

03:00:09.990 --> 03:00:14.030
This was actually probably the most normal
thing I had seen since getting on the ride,

03:00:14.030 --> 03:00:17.660
as it resembled the scene that usually takes
place on this floor during normal operation

03:00:17.660 --> 03:00:18.660
of the ride.

03:00:18.660 --> 03:00:21.950
Then, to my surprise our harnesses came off.

03:00:21.950 --> 03:00:24.290
I was essentially frozen in complete shock.

03:00:24.290 --> 03:00:25.820
What the hell was going on?

03:00:25.820 --> 03:00:29.330
The creepo behind me continued to hold my
shoulder, while the other two riders got out

03:00:29.330 --> 03:00:33.060
of their seats and casually walked through
the door to the right, which to this point

03:00:33.060 --> 03:00:37.330
I wasn’t even aware was a real door, I had
always just thought it was a facade, much

03:00:37.330 --> 03:00:39.960
like the stairs in the boiler room earlier.

03:00:39.960 --> 03:00:44.250
After I’m not sure exactly how long, I snapped
out of my daze and realized this was my chance

03:00:44.250 --> 03:00:45.250
to get out.

03:00:45.250 --> 03:00:48.840
I wriggled myself free of the man’s grasp
and made a b-line for the right side door.

03:00:48.840 --> 03:00:49.840
It was locked.

03:00:49.840 --> 03:00:53.860
I banged myself against it but it wouldn’t
budge, so I darted across to the left side

03:00:53.860 --> 03:00:56.400
door, glancing at the elevator car in passing.

03:00:56.400 --> 03:01:00.710
The man in the bellhop uniform was just sitting
there, giving me this creepy, sadistic grin.

03:01:00.710 --> 03:01:04.561
To my surprise, the door on the left worked
and I slammed it shut behind me.

03:01:04.561 --> 03:01:08.380
I stumbled down a seedy, narrow staircase
at the end of which was another door.

03:01:08.380 --> 03:01:12.260
I bursted through, hoping to make it into
the lobby or something, but instead found

03:01:12.260 --> 03:01:14.450
myself in an abandoned swimming pool.

03:01:14.450 --> 03:01:16.750
What in the world?

03:01:16.750 --> 03:01:18.670
I mean, how could this possibly exist here?

03:01:18.670 --> 03:01:22.260
I know for a fact that the pool has never
been part of the ride, the queue, or any of

03:01:22.260 --> 03:01:23.550
of the theming surrounding it.

03:01:23.550 --> 03:01:27.690
I vaguely remember a sign pointing to a pool
in the beginning of the line, but come on,

03:01:27.690 --> 03:01:28.690
it was just a sign.

03:01:28.690 --> 03:01:31.560
Did I just stumble upon one of those crazy
Disney secrets?

03:01:31.560 --> 03:01:35.860
Like Walt Disney’s New Orleans square apartment,
or the fabled basketball court under the peak

03:01:35.860 --> 03:01:36.900
of the Matterhorn?

03:01:36.900 --> 03:01:41.050
Perhaps this pool was at one time an employee
lounge area of some kind?

03:01:41.050 --> 03:01:45.010
All the tiles were cracked and the pool was
filled with rust and who knows what else.

03:01:45.010 --> 03:01:47.580
There were a couple of dark objects at the
bottom of the pool.

03:01:47.580 --> 03:01:51.360
I had to force myself not to look and assume
that they were pool chairs or something, but

03:01:51.360 --> 03:01:55.420
I had a bad feeling in my gut about what they
may actually be.

03:01:55.420 --> 03:01:58.360
Whatever it was, it looked disgusting and
I wanted to get the hell out of there.

03:01:58.360 --> 03:02:03.260
I looked around for another exit, but the
first thing I noticed, was a lump across the

03:02:03.260 --> 03:02:04.260
pool.

03:02:04.260 --> 03:02:08.140
My first thought was that it was a dead body…
until I saw the guy stand up and start wobbling

03:02:08.140 --> 03:02:09.370
around like a drunk.

03:02:09.370 --> 03:02:11.960
He was wearing a hoodie, and tattered jeans.

03:02:11.960 --> 03:02:16.010
My initial impression was that it was a homeless
guy, who had somehow snuck in and was living

03:02:16.010 --> 03:02:17.010
in here.

03:02:17.010 --> 03:02:18.560
When he saw me, he started screaming at me.

03:02:18.560 --> 03:02:21.860
He kept saying, “you can’t take my home,
and cursing at me.”

03:02:21.860 --> 03:02:23.740
He was clearly intoxicated.

03:02:23.740 --> 03:02:27.740
As soon as I figured out where the door was,
I made a mad dash for the exit, which may

03:02:27.740 --> 03:02:31.960
have in fact been an entrance, because it
led me into a dimly lit locker room.

03:02:31.960 --> 03:02:35.979
I guess if that was at one time a pool for
the employees, this must be the corresponding

03:02:35.979 --> 03:02:36.979
locker room.

03:02:36.979 --> 03:02:40.810
The lockers were pretty small, and all of
them were open, and empty.

03:02:40.810 --> 03:02:45.240
The only sound I could hear was that of running
water on the far side of the locker room,

03:02:45.240 --> 03:02:46.720
in the dark.

03:02:46.720 --> 03:02:50.400
After all I had experienced, I thought it
might be best to approach the door on the

03:02:50.400 --> 03:02:52.780
other side of the room more stealthily.

03:02:52.780 --> 03:02:56.330
I was also feeling very sick, and needed to
catch my breath.

03:02:56.330 --> 03:02:58.620
I still felt like I was going to pass out.

03:02:58.620 --> 03:03:02.950
I walk over to the source of the water, keeping
my footsteps as quiet as possible.

03:03:02.950 --> 03:03:09.020
There are a few shower stalls up ahead.

03:03:09.020 --> 03:03:14.100
I poke my head into the first, and it is empty.

03:03:14.100 --> 03:03:18.350
I proceed, continuing on to check the second,
third and fourth stalls.

03:03:18.350 --> 03:03:24.010
But what I see in the fourth stall stops me
dead in my track.

03:03:24.010 --> 03:03:27.460
In the corner of the shower, an old man stands
in the water’s stream.

03:03:27.460 --> 03:03:32.860
He is naked, senile and borderline deformed
and he has his head buried in the corner.

03:03:32.860 --> 03:03:37.360
Luckily he doesn’t seem to notice me, so
I decide to tip-toe past him to get to the

03:03:37.360 --> 03:03:38.780
door.

03:03:38.780 --> 03:03:44.460
I make it across safely, but as I grip the
door handle, I hear a terrifying cry out from

03:03:44.460 --> 03:03:45.460
behind me.

03:03:45.460 --> 03:03:46.460
“I see you.

03:03:46.460 --> 03:03:47.979
You’ll never get me out of here.

03:03:47.979 --> 03:03:52.520
You’re the one who has to go!”

03:03:52.520 --> 03:03:56.560
I hear wet footsteps charging out of the shower
stall behind me and waste no time yanking

03:03:56.560 --> 03:03:59.450
the door open and fumbling my way through
the next room in the dark.

03:03:59.450 --> 03:04:01.570
This leads me back to the the level one mirror
room.

03:04:01.570 --> 03:04:05.101
The elevator car from the ride is now there,
seemingly just waiting for me.

03:04:05.101 --> 03:04:08.480
The creepy bellhop guy is in the same seat,
continuing to stare me down!

03:04:08.480 --> 03:04:11.780
I don’t even bother to stop running across
the mirror room and through the door on the

03:04:11.780 --> 03:04:13.360
other side.

03:04:13.360 --> 03:04:17.560
Now I’m in another hotel corridor, but different
from the one upstairs.

03:04:17.560 --> 03:04:21.710
At the end of the hall, I see a woman, and
yet another bellhop character, this one wearing

03:04:21.710 --> 03:04:25.230
a red pair of Mickey Mouse ears with an Iron
Man logo on it.

03:04:25.230 --> 03:04:26.860
The two are having a dispute.

03:04:26.860 --> 03:04:30.291
She is screaming and grabbing onto the sides
of the doorframe as he violently tries to

03:04:30.291 --> 03:04:31.291
pull her out of the room.

03:04:31.291 --> 03:04:34.230
She is screaming, “please, don’t make
me go.”

03:04:34.230 --> 03:04:38.390
and he would just methodically respond by
telling her that her stay is up and she is

03:04:38.390 --> 03:04:40.240
welcome to check into one of their other hotels.

03:04:40.240 --> 03:04:44.890
He then yanked her hard enough for her to
lose her grip on the door and she flew across

03:04:44.890 --> 03:04:48.280
the hallway, crashing her head against the
wall hard enough to draw to blood.

03:04:48.280 --> 03:04:50.250
She collapsed on the floor in front of him.

03:04:50.250 --> 03:04:54.900
That’s when he looked up and noticed me,
with the same intense stare that the bellhops

03:04:54.900 --> 03:04:57.561
down in the lobby had given us.

03:04:57.561 --> 03:05:01.720
My vision was starting to get blurry, so I
decided to try to go into one of the rooms

03:05:01.720 --> 03:05:03.590
if I could to buy myself some time.

03:05:03.590 --> 03:05:07.311
I assumed that all the doors were fakes, but
was pleasantly surprised when one of them

03:05:07.311 --> 03:05:10.301
actually opened, leading to yet another corridor.

03:05:10.301 --> 03:05:14.270
I was too tired to try to comprehend how this
was possible, given the layout of this ride

03:05:14.270 --> 03:05:18.460
and given the fact that these secret rooms
have no reason to exist in the first place.

03:05:18.460 --> 03:05:22.891
Just then, the room went dark, and the walls,
floor and ceiling became projection mapped

03:05:22.891 --> 03:05:27.270
with the starry night sky, the same effect
used in the 2nd floor of the actual version

03:05:27.270 --> 03:05:28.440
of the ride.

03:05:28.440 --> 03:05:31.350
At the end, was a single door.

03:05:31.350 --> 03:05:35.890
I took this as the metaphorical exit to the
Twilight Zone, so I ran to it as fast as I

03:05:35.890 --> 03:05:36.890
could.

03:05:36.890 --> 03:05:39.330
As I was running I heard the narrator’s
booming voice one last time.

03:05:39.330 --> 03:05:40.330
“Next time you try to mess with history,
make sure you know just what kind of vacancy

03:05:40.330 --> 03:05:41.330
you’re filling, or you may find a few nasty
surprises coming your way.

03:05:41.330 --> 03:05:45.221
You may or may not have made it through tonight,
but to close this door is to forever live

03:05:45.221 --> 03:05:50.840
on in your head in…

03:05:50.840 --> 03:05:57.740
The Twilight Zone.”

03:05:57.740 --> 03:06:04.330
And just like that, it was over.

03:06:04.330 --> 03:06:08.729
The sound of the 30s soundtrack played in
my ears and I was making my way down the exit

03:06:08.729 --> 03:06:13.460
stairs, trying to think about if Joey and
Matt had a similar experience to what I had.

03:06:13.460 --> 03:06:15.240
And what happened to those two strangers?

03:06:15.240 --> 03:06:17.960
What if I was the only one to make it out?

03:06:17.960 --> 03:06:19.760
Who would believe me?

03:06:19.760 --> 03:06:20.979
A light caught my eye.

03:06:20.979 --> 03:06:22.600
THE RIDE PHOTO.

03:06:22.600 --> 03:06:25.050
At the top of the drop, that guy was grabbing
onto my shoulder.

03:06:25.050 --> 03:06:28.460
Not to mention the hanging bodies would also
probably be in frame.

03:06:28.460 --> 03:06:29.900
I ran up to the preview screen.

03:06:29.900 --> 03:06:32.550
If I needed proof, this would be it!!

03:06:32.550 --> 03:06:37.261
But when I looked at the photo, it was just
me and the other two guys.

03:06:37.261 --> 03:06:38.660
No creepy bellhop.

03:06:38.660 --> 03:06:40.320
No bodies.

03:06:40.320 --> 03:06:41.920
Just a regular ride photo...

03:06:41.920 --> 03:06:46.870
The gift shop was completely devoid of any
gifts or people so, feeling defeated I passed

03:06:46.870 --> 03:06:49.050
through and met up with my friends.

03:06:49.050 --> 03:06:53.590
As I had feared, they made no mention of anything
abnormal and asked if I was OK.

03:06:53.590 --> 03:06:57.570
A regular Disney employee in a yellow button
down shirt informs us the park is closing

03:06:57.570 --> 03:06:59.990
and to make our way to the exits.

03:06:59.990 --> 03:07:01.229
We walk out of the park.

03:07:01.229 --> 03:07:05.110
I turn back and see the lights coming down
on The Tower of Terror one last time.There

03:07:05.110 --> 03:07:09.880
are already cranes in place, ready to start
ripping off pieces of the structure.

03:07:09.880 --> 03:07:13.090
Other than that though, it looks completely
normal from the outside.

03:07:13.090 --> 03:07:16.101
No hanging bodies at the top.

03:07:16.101 --> 03:07:17.410
Nothing out of the ordinary.

03:07:17.410 --> 03:07:21.540
Before turning back, I see a window open on
one of the floors near the top.

03:07:21.540 --> 03:07:23.470
I stop walking.

03:07:23.470 --> 03:07:27.580
Joey asks what’s gotten into me as I stare
back at the ride for the the final time.

03:07:27.580 --> 03:07:31.570
A light shines out of the window, and the
silhouette of a bellhop sticks his head out

03:07:31.570 --> 03:07:39.510
and waves at me.

03:07:39.510 --> 03:07:57.170
I don’t plan on going back to ride the new
Guardians of the Galaxy ride when it opens.

03:07:57.170 --> 03:07:58.420
I believe in ghosts.

03:07:58.420 --> 03:08:00.780
Thanks for listening, to all of Al Dente Creepypasta.

03:08:00.780 --> 03:08:06.310
Your total today comes out to $249,172.84
, but if you like this video right now, I'll

03:08:06.310 --> 03:08:11.290
waive that fee and give you everything you
just listened to, absolutely free.

03:08:11.290 --> 03:08:15.740
If you made it this far, my question for you
is this: if I were to make a movie out of

03:08:15.740 --> 03:08:19.330
one of these stories, which one would you
like to see adapted the most?

03:08:19.330 --> 03:08:21.750
Let me know when you stop by the comment section.

03:08:21.750 --> 03:08:25.804
And congratulations on making it to the end
of Season 1.

03:08:25.804 --> 03:08:28.771
This season I tried to push the boundaries
of what could be done with with an audio horror

03:08:28.771 --> 03:08:29.771
story.

03:08:29.771 --> 03:08:34.601
I brought you all new and original scripts,
some of the best narrators in the game, cinematic

03:08:34.601 --> 03:08:37.500
sound design and a completely original score.

03:08:37.500 --> 03:08:42.960
Next season, I'm taking it even further and
doing some things that have never been done

03:08:42.960 --> 03:08:43.960
before.

03:08:43.960 --> 03:08:48.100
I've already got a ton of cool episodes planned
for Season 2 and I'm hoping to once again

03:08:48.100 --> 03:08:52.330
change the game of audio based horror and
continue to collaborate with some of your

03:08:52.330 --> 03:08:53.330
favorite narrators.

03:08:53.330 --> 03:08:58.210
If that's something you'd like to see, make
sure you're subscribed to CZsWorld for new

03:08:58.210 --> 03:09:04.200
horrors, every week, ring that deathbell for
notifications and I'll see you in the next

03:09:04.200 --> 03:09:06.431
season.

03:09:06.431 --> 03:09:15.351
Assuming we both survive.

